\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 White House will not overrule $15 minimum wage decision despite progressives' plea \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Gabrielle Canon (now), Joan E Greve and Martin Belam (earlier) \par \uc2 12,537 \uc2 words\par \uc2 2 March 2021\par 01:38 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2021.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Senate to take up Covid relief bill this week, says SchumerJen Psaki: Biden doesn\u8217\'20\'19t plan to overrule Senate parliamentarianCDC director warns of potential \u8216\'20\'18fourth surge\u8217\'20\'19 in Covid casesDHS secretary: Trump \u8216\'20\'18dismantled immigration system in its entirety\u8217\'20\'19\uc2 Johnson & Johnson\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s vaccine to roll out within 48 hoursSign up to receive First Thing \u8211\'20\'13 our daily briefing by email\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.30am GMT\par \par \uc2 What's happened today\par \par \uc2 Wrapping up here on the west coast. Here\u8217\'20\'19s what happened this afternoon and evening:\par \par \uc2 * A third accuser has come forward alleging sexual harassment from the New York governor, \uc2 Andrew Cuomo\uc2 , as more join in calling for his resignation.\par \par \uc2 * Trump quietly received a vaccine in January, along with his wife Melania, but it wasn\u8217\'20\'19t publicized until now.\par \par \uc2 * Miguel Cardona, a former public school teacher and the first Latino to serve as education commissioner for the state of Connecticut was confirmed as the next US education secretary.\par \par \uc2 * Democrats are planning to reintroduce a voting rights bill hoping new support from the White House will push it through.\par \par \uc2 * President Biden virtually met with the Mexican president, \uc2 Andr\u233\'00\'E9s Manuel L\u243\'00\'F3pez Obrador\uc2 , to discuss migration, Covid, and other priorities.\par \par \uc2 Thanks for reading along! Hope you all have a great night.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.38am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.28am GMT\par \par \uc2 A third woman has come forward to accuse the New York governor, \uc2 Andrew Cuomo\uc2 , of sexual harassment, amid calls for his resignation.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 New York Times\uc2  reports that Anna Ruch joined two former aids and offered details of Cuomo\u8217\'20\'19s behavior.\par \par \uc2 From the \uc2 NYT\uc2 :\par \par \uc2 Mr. Cuomo put his hand on Ms. Ruch\u8217\'20\'19s bare lower back, she said in an interview on Monday.\par \par \uc2 When she removed his hand with her own, Ms. Ruch recalled, the governor remarked that she seemed \u8220\'20\'1Caggressive\u8221\'20\'1D and placed his hands on her cheeks. He asked if he could kiss her, loudly enough for a friend standing nearby to hear. Ms. Ruch was bewildered by the entreaty, she said, and pulled away as the governor drew closer.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI was so confused and shocked and embarrassed,\u8221\'20\'1D said Ms. Ruch, whose recollection was corroborated by the friend, contemporaneous text messages and photographs from the event. \u8220\'20\'1CI turned my head away and didn\u8217\'20\'19t have words in that moment.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Cuomo released a statement apologizing for past behavior Sunday night, calling the actions \u8220\'20\'1Cmisinterpreted as an unwanted flirtation\u8221\'20\'1D and adding, \u8220\'20\'1Cto the extent anyone felt that way, I am truly sorry about that\u8221\'20\'1D but has not responded to the new allegations.\par \par \uc2 On Monday, \uc2 the Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Miranda Bryan {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/mar/01/andrew-cuomo-new-york-governor-apology-sexual-harassment-resign-calls-"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reports}}}\uc2 , a group of former legislative employees joined Republican and Democrat lawmakers in denouncing the apology and called for him to step down or be removed from office:\par \par \uc2 Members of the Sexual Harassment Working Group also said they expected more allegations to follow \u8211\'20\'13 and accused Cuomo of \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/lifeandstyle/2019/mar/02/abuse-prevention-how-to-turn-off-the-gaslighters"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 gaslighting}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D his accusers.\par \par \uc2 Letitia James, the state attorney general, meanwhile, announced the first step in mounting an external investigation of the governor\u8217\'20\'19s behaviour.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.35am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.29am GMT\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 World Health Organization\uc2  is now officially advising against the use of hydroxychloroquine, a drug promoted by the Trump administration as a Covid treatment, ABC News {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://abcnews.go.com/Health/panel-advises-hydroxychloroquine-prevent-covid-19/story?id=76186122&cid=social_twitter_abcn"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reports}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 A panel of experts said Monday that there was \u8220\'20\'1Chigh certainty evidence\u8221\'20\'1D that the anti-inflammatory drug typically used to battle malaria, didn\u8217\'20\'19t stop Covid deaths or hospitalizations but actually increases the problems for patients.\par \par \uc2 Trump once called the drug a \u8220\'20\'1Cgame-changer\u8221\'20\'1D citing no evidence, even as \uc2 Dr Anthony Fauci\uc2  said it was ineffective. Even after the \uc2 Food and Drug Administration\uc2  revoked an emergency authorization, the former president retweeted a video full of misinformation about the virus and the importance of wearing masks. \u8220\'20\'1CI happen to believe in it\u8221\'20\'1D he said in response.\par \par \uc2 enltrAsked about video he shared featuring figure blasting masks recommendations and touting hydroxychloroquine, \uc2 Pres. Trump\uc2  said, "I thought her voice was an important voice, but I know nothing about her."\par \par \uc2 Pressed further, Trump left the briefing room. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/9dy1mk3Z73"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/9dy1mk3Z73}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/jMfRrlth12"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/jMfRrlth12}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 ABC News Politics (@ABCPolitics) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ABCPolitics/status/1288476650620039168?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 29, 2020}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.47am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.03am GMT\par \par \uc2 The former president \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and the former first lady Melania Trump have both been vaccinated, according to an unnamed advisor who shared the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.axios.com/trump-vaccinated-coronavirus-bd88b0fa-6a19-483d-8fd4-d949f23f25f9.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 news}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2021/03/01/us/politics/donald-trump-melania-coronavirus-vaccine.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 with}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2021/03/01/politics/trump-melania-vaccinated-white-house/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reporters}}}\uc2  Monday.\par \par \uc2 While other officials, including President Biden, Vice-president Harris, and the former vice-president \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2 , chose to get their shots publicly to encourage confidence in the vaccines, the Trumps opted to quietly get vaccinated while still at the White House in January, the source said. There was no detail on which shot they received or how many doses they had been given.\par \par \uc2 The revelation first came to light after Trump took the stage at the Conservative Political Action Conference in Florida. \u8220\'20\'1CEveryone should go get your shot,\u8221\'20\'1D he told the audience, prompting questions from reporters about whether he\u8217\'20\'19d had his.\par \par \uc2 enltrTrump yesterday, at CPAC, said for the first time that "everyone" should get the coronavirus vaccine developed while he was in office. An adviser tells me both Trump and Melania Trump got vaccinated at the White House in January.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Maggie Haberman (@maggieNYT) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/maggieNYT/status/1366461056164507648?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 March 1, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 The speech was the first time Trump has told supporters \u8211\'20\'13 who include groups that are the most skeptical of the vaccine \u8211\'20\'13 to get their shots. According to Axios, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.axios.com/trump-vaccinated-coronavirus-bd88b0fa-6a19-483d-8fd4-d949f23f25f9.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 white Republicans have shown more uncertainty}}}\uc2  than any other demographic group.\par \par \uc2 Still, the former president has not hesitated to take credit for the rollout. \u8220\'20\'1CNever let them forget this was us. We did this,\u8221\'20\'1D he said at CPAC.\par \par \uc2 His claim contradicts {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2021/01/21/politics/biden-covid-vaccination-trump/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reporting from January}}}\uc2 , that showed Biden had to start from scratch when he took office and that there was no vaccine distribution plan left behind by the Trump administration. From CNN:\par \par \uc2 In the immediate hours following Biden being sworn into office on Wednesday, sources with direct knowledge of the new administration\u8217\'20\'19s Covid-related work told CNN one of the biggest shocks that the Biden team had to digest during the transition period was what they saw as a complete lack of a vaccine distribution strategy under Trump, even weeks after multiple vaccines were approved for use in the United States.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.19am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.33pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Miguel Cardona confirmed to lead US education department\par \par \uc2 The Senate has voted 64-33 to confirm Miguel Cardona to serve as education secretary, who will now be charged with the difficult job of navigating how to reopen schools during the Covid crisis.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAt this moment of crisis, Dr. Cardona is exactly the leader we need at the Department of Education,\u8221\'20\'1D said the senator \uc2 Patty Murray\uc2 , chairwoman of the Senate education committee {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/education/miguel-cardona-education-secretary/2021/03/01/67f6ed5a-7ac4-11eb-b3d1-9e5aa3d5220c_story.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 to the Washington Post}}}\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CHe has the experience, principles and perspective that we need in this critical role.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 During his confirmation hearing he said classroom safety would be his top priority as secretary. He is also expected to help Biden achieve his goal to open most elementary schools within his first 100 days.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI recognize the frustration and distrust and fear that is out there and if confirmed as secretary of education, I\u8217\'20\'19ll do everything in my power to make sure that our rollout strategy for reopening schools includes communication on how to safely reopen schools,\u8221\'20\'1D said Cardona to the Senate Health, Education, Labor and Pensions committee in February.\par \par \uc2 Cardona was a public school teacher and a principal before becoming the first Latino to serve as education commissioner in Connecticut.\par \par \uc2 This week, the Senate will confirm:\par \par \uc2 Dr. Miguel Cardona as Education Secretary\par \par \uc2 Governor \uc2 Gina Raimondo\uc2  as Commerce Secretary\par \par \uc2 Dr. Cecilia Rouse\uc2  as the Chair of the Council of Economic Advisors\par \par \uc2 All three are exceptionally well-qualified.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Chuck Schumer (@SenSchumer) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SenSchumer/status/1366506970723794959?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 March 1, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 Updated at 12.03am GMT\par \par \uc2 11.18pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Democrats are gearing up for a new battle over voting rights, but this time, with the backing of the White House. In a statement issued Monday, the Biden administration threw its weight behind the For the People Act, which would make Election Day a federal holiday, give more power to the justice department to reinforce voting rights, and increase vote by mail opportunities.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIn the wake of an unprecedented assault on our democracy, a never before seen effort to ignore, undermine, and undo the will of the people, and a newly aggressive attack on voting rights taking place right now all across the country, this landmark legislation is urgently needed to protect the right to vote and the integrity of our elections, and to repair and strengthen American democracy,\u8221\'20\'1D President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Office of Management and Budget said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 Despicable, discriminatory, anti-democratic proposals are on the move in Republican state legislatures\par \par \uc2 Make no mistake: They must be opposed by every American who cherishes our democracy\par \par \uc2 This Senate is working to pass the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/ForThePeople?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #ForThePeople}}}\uc2  Act to renew democracy and our elections\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Chuck Schumer (@SenSchumer) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SenSchumer/status/1366522692124426240?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 March 1, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 The election reform bill could be put to a vote as soon as this week, and is expected to pass in the House. The narrow majority in the Senate may make things a bit more difficult. In order to get the bill through, all 50 members of the Democratic caucus would have to be on board, along with 10 Republicans. The GOP has claimed that the expanded voting rights would increase fraud and step on states\u8217\'20\'19 rights.\par \par \uc2 And, though Biden supports the legislation, he isn\u8217\'20\'19t going to ditch the filibuster to help Democrats get a win.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe president\u8217\'20\'19s view on the filibuster is well known. He has not changed that point of view,\u8221\'20\'1D White House press secretary \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2  told reporters Monday. \u8220\'20\'1CThe president is committed to protecting the fundamental right to vote and making it easier for all eligible Americans to vote. His campaign was about fighting for democracy, and we\u8217\'20\'19re going to continue to fight for democracy in the White House.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Updated at 12.06am GMT\par \par \uc2 10.50pm GMT\par \par \uc2 President Biden is meeting virtually with Mexican President \uc2 Andr\u233\'00\'E9s Manuel L\u243\'00\'F3pez Obrador\uc2  today, with migration and the coronavirus pandemic at the top of the agenda.\par \par \uc2 President Biden tells Mexican President \uc2 Andres Manuel Lopez Obrador\uc2 : "We look at Mexico as an equal, not as somebody who is south of our border. You are equal. And what you do in Mexico and how you succeed impacts dramatically on what the rest of the hemisphere will look like." {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/jr1QSio3pY"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/jr1QSio3pY}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 CBS News (@CBSNews) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/CBSNews/status/1366519818585800711?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 March 1, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 Amlo has been clear about his intentions to propose a new \u8220\'20\'1CBracero\u8221\'20\'1D style labor program to the new US President, which could enable between 600,000 and 800,000 Mexican and Central American immigrants to work within the US. The idea isn\u8217\'20\'19t a new one.\par \par \uc2 Starting in the second world war, Mexicans helped shore up labor shortages in the US, and \uc2 L\u243\'00\'F3pez Obrador\uc2  would like to see the program reinstated, expanding opportunities for both agricultural workers and those in other sectors.\par \par \uc2 The Associated Press{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/biden-obrador-us-mexico-migration-issues-edb25cf298b7c9a83d15ff4f6c7ea95f"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reports}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 A senior Biden administration official declined to say whether the U.S. president would back or oppose the proposal, saying only that both countries agree on the need to expand legal pathways for migration. The official insisted on anonymity to discuss private conversations. Asked about the Mexican president\u8217\'20\'19s proposal. White House press secretary \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2  said that reinstituting the Bracero program would require action by Congress.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, Reuters {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.reuters.com/article/us-usa-mexico/u-s-to-give-americans-covid-19-vaccines-before-discussing-sharing-with-mexico-white-house-idUSKCN2AT2ME?il=0"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reports}}}\uc2 , the Biden administration is not expected to offer Covid vaccines to Mexico, but the president told pool reporters that it might be discussed.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe administration\u8217\'20\'19s focus is on ensuring that every American is vaccinated. And once we accomplish that objective we\u8217\'20\'19re happy to discuss further steps,\u8221\'20\'1D White House Press Secretary \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2  said at a White House news conference.\par \par \uc2 Asked if US will send coronavirus vaccines to Mexico that AMLO wants, Biden tells the press pool during their virtual meeting that he and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/lopezobrador_?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @lopezobrador_}}}\uc2  will talk about it.\par \par \uc2 Biden\u8217\'20\'19s press sec earlier today said no.\par \par \uc2 Photos by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/nancook?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @nancook}}}\uc2 . {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/VtfHr64qHM"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/VtfHr64qHM}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Jennifer Jacobs (@JenniferJJacobs) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/JenniferJJacobs/status/1366512893798338564?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 March 1, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 Updated at 11.59pm GMT\par \par \uc2 10.30pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Keith Gill, who is perhaps better known as \u8220\'20\'1CRoaring Kitty\u8221\'20\'1D after he helped spur a surge in \uc2 GameStop\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s stock price on Reddit, is no longer a registered broker with the \uc2 Financial Industry Regulatory Authority\uc2 , Reuters {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.reuters.com/article/us-retail-trading-roaringkitty/roaring-kitty-no-longer-has-financial-broker-license-filing-idUSKCN2AT3OX?il=0"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reports}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Gill, whose posted \uc2 YouTube\uc2  videos on investing under the name Roaring Kitty and became a central figure on r/Wallstreetbets under the name DeepFuckingValue, helped send the struggling video game retailer\u8217\'20\'19s stocks up more than 1,000% in two weeks.\par \par \uc2 In a proposed class-action suit filed in Massachusetts federal court against Gill in February, he was accused of misrepresenting himself and manipulating the market to his own benefit.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CGill\u8217\'20\'19s deceitful and manipulative conduct not only violated numerous industry regulations and rules, but also various securities laws by undermining the integrity of the market for \uc2 GameStop\uc2  shares,\u8221\'20\'1D the suit said. \u8220\'20\'1CHe caused enormous losses not only to those who bought option contracts, but also to those who fell for Gill\u8217\'20\'19s act and bought \uc2 GameStop\uc2  stock during the market frenzy at greatly inflated prices.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He has not yet responded to requests from Reuters for comment but the news organization said \u8220\'20\'1Chis online broker profile now flags the pending litigation, as well as an ongoing investigation by Massachusetts financial regulators\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 If you missed the news, here\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2021/jan/29/wallstreetbets-founder-jaime-rogozinski-gamestop-shares-reddit"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the background}}}\uc2  from Guardian reporter Edward Helmore:\par \par \uc2 Small investors bonded together on the Reddit forum, spurred on by members with names such as Roaring Kitty, to take on some of Wall Street\u8217\'20\'19s biggest investors who they believed had made a bad bet on the company collapsing.\par \par \uc2 The professional investors had \u8220\'20\'1Cshorted\u8221\'20\'1D \uc2 GameStop\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 a bet its price will collapse \u8211\'20\'13 along with other companies that have since soared including the cinema chain AMC and \uc2 BlackBerry\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Incredibly, the WallStreetBets crowd won the round, forcing some out of the trade and causing consternation and fears of an electronic financial insurgency on Wall Street.\par \par \uc2 Updated at 11.06pm GMT\par \par \uc2 9.59pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Even as Covid continues to spread across the country, states have begun easing the restrictions put in place to curb the disease, the Associated Press {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/kansas-city-michael-brown-kansas-coronavirus-pandemic-massachusetts-3599a9631d08de3945f5c95f000e5611"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reports}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 Massachusetts on Monday made it much easier to grab dinner and a show. In Missouri, where individual communities get to make the rules, the two biggest metropolitan areas \u8212\'20\'14 St. Louis and Kansas City \u8212\'20\'14 are relaxing some measures. Iowa\u8217\'20\'19s governor recently lifted mask requirements and limits on the number of people allowed in bars and restaurants, while the town of Lawrence, home to the \uc2 University of Kansas\uc2 , now lets establishments stay open until midnight.\par \par \uc2 Maps from the \uc2 New York Times\uc2  show most states are \u8220\'20\'1Cmostly open\u8221\'20\'1D for business and few remain under stay-at-home orders.\par \par \uc2 States continue to adjust their virus restrictions and mask mandates.\par \par \uc2 \u8226\'20\'22 Massachusetts relaxed rules on performance venues.\par \par \uc2 \u8226\'20\'22 South Carolina lifted restrictions on gathering sizes and alcohol sales.\par \par \uc2 \u8226\'20\'22 Kentucky extended its mask order.\par \par \uc2 See more here. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/eJXpCDi0vY"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/eJXpCDi0vY}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 NYT Graphics (@nytgraphics) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/nytgraphics/status/1366503764128124930?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 March 1, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 With the US approaching the one-year mark for when the fast-spreading coronavirus first prompted lockdowns, roughly 28.4 million cases and 511,893 deaths have been reported, according to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://covid.cdc.gov/covid-data-tracker/#vaccinations"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Centers for Disease Control and Prevention}}}\uc2 . As of Monday, 25.5 million people have been fully vaccinated, and roughly 50.7 million have had at least one shot.\par \par \uc2 Updated at 11.03pm GMT\par \par \uc2 9.40pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Georgia House passes bill that will make it harder to vote\par \par \uc2 Gabrielle Canon here, signing on from the west coast for the afternoon. Before I jump in, here\u8217\'20\'19s an important update from my colleague Sam Levine :\par \par \uc2 The Georgia house of representatives{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.legis.ga.gov/legislation/59831"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 passed a major bill}}}\uc2  with new sweeping voting restrictions on Monday that limits ballot drop boxes and early voting, and requires voters to provide identification information when they vote by mail.\par \par \uc2 The measure, which passed on a party line vote of 97-72, comes months after the state saw record turnout that helped Democrats \uc2 Jon Ossoff\uc2  and \uc2 Raphael Warnock\uc2  win stunning upsets in two \uc2 US Senate\uc2  races and \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  carry the presidential vote. The measure, one of several that would restrict voting in Georgia, is a thinly veiled effort to make it harder to cast a ballot for minority voters, voting advocates say.\par \par \uc2 One of the most notable provisions in the law would cut back significantly on the amount of weekend early voting in the state.\par \par \uc2 It would allow county officials to offer just one additional day of weekend early voting in addition to the one on Saturday that\u8217\'20\'19s required by law. Counties can currently offer up to four days of early voting and many have noted that Sundays ahead of an election are traditionally popular dates for early voting among Black voters as churches use \u8220\'20\'1CSouls to the Polls\u8221\'20\'1D efforts to encourage voters to cast a ballot. It would also require election officials to reject provisional ballots entirely that are cast in the wrong precinct and shorten the runoff election period from nine weeks until just four.\par \par \uc2 This gives lie to Fleming\u8217\'20\'19s assertion that only \u8220\'20\'1Ca few hundred\u8221\'20\'1D provisional ballots were cast up until 2018.\par \par \uc2 THOUSANDS have been cast in EVERY election. They are predominantly Democratic, and predominantly Black.\par \par \uc2 This data comes straight from the SOS website. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/71kYCZQ2tM"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/71kYCZQ2tM}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Sara Tindall Ghazal (@TindallSara) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/TindallSara/status/1366466774384979970?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 March 1, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 The measure also shortens the window voters have to cast an absentee ballot and requires them to present ID information when they request a ballot and when they turn it in. The measure also places new limits on ballot drop boxes, restricting where election officials can place them and the hours they can be accessible to the public.\par \par \uc2 During a two hour debate on Monday, Barry Fleming, the bill\u8217\'20\'19s sponsor, and fellow Republicans defended the measure as commonsense changes needed to restore confidence in elections. State officials, including Georgia\u8217\'20\'19s top election official, a Republican, have said repeatedly there was no evidence of fraud.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHouse Bill 531 is designed to bring back the confidence of our voters back into our election system. A main component of that effort is by enacting several revisions which will make the administration of elections easier by our local election officials,\u8221\'20\'1D Fleming said.\par \par \uc2 The legislation would only allow officials to have ballot drop boxes inside early voting locations and only operational during early voting hours.\par \par \uc2 Several Republicans also pointed for the need to have uniform election processes across the state.\par \par \uc2 But several Democrats said that was weak justification for a measure that would make it harder to vote. They noted that the current bill leaves room for neighboring counties to offer different weekend early voting days, which was likely to cause confusion.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s pathetically obvious to anyone paying attention that when Trump lost the November election and Georgia flipped control of the \uc2 US Senate\uc2  to Democrats \u8211\'20\'13 shortly after, Republicans got the message that they were in a political death spiral,\u8221\'20\'1D said state representative Renitta Shannon, a Democrat. \u8220\'20\'1CAnd now they\u8217\'20\'19re doing anything they can to silence the voices of black and brown voters specifically because they largely powered these wins.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The bill now moves to the Georgia senate.\par \par \uc2 Updated at 11.02pm GMT\par \par \uc2 9.30pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Today so far\par \par \uc2 That\u8217\'20\'19s it from me today. My west coast colleague, Gabrielle Canon, will take over the blog for the next few hours.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s where the day stands so far:\par \par \uc2 * The White House said \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  does not intend to overrule the Senate parliamentarian on including a $15 minimum wage provision in the coronavirus relief package. The parliamentarian announced Thursday that the minimum wage proposal does not meet the requirements to be passed using reconciliation, but a group of House progressives has called on Biden to overrule that decision by having Vice-President \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , the leader of the Senate, allow for the provision\u8217\'20\'19s inclusion in the relief bill. White House press secretary \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2  said moments ago, \u8220\'20\'1CThat is not an action that we intend to take.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 * The Senate will take up the coronavirus relief bill \u8220\'20\'1Cthis week,\u8221\'20\'1D majority leader Chuck Schumer announced. \u8220\'20\'1CThe Senate will take up the American Rescue Plan this week,\u8221\'20\'1D the Democratic leader said this afternoon. \u8220\'20\'1CI expect a hearty debate and some late nights.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 * The director of the Centers for Disease Control and Prevention warned of a potential \u8220\'20\'1Cfourth surge\u8221\'20\'1D in coronavirus cases. The CDC director, \uc2 Dr Rochelle Walensky\uc2 , voiced concern about a recent uptick in cases during today\u8217\'20\'19s briefing from the White House coronavirus response team. \u8220\'20\'1CAt this level of cases, with variants spreading, we stand to completely lose the hard-earned ground we have gained,\u8221\'20\'1D Walensky said. \u8220\'20\'1CWe have the ability to stop a potential fourth surge of cases in this country.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 * The secretary of homeland security accused the Trump administration of having \u8220\'20\'1Cdismantled our nation\u8217\'20\'19s immigration system in its entirety\u8221\'20\'1D. Secretary Alejandro Mayorkas said that the DHS is working to \u8220\'20\'1Creplace the cruelty of the past administration with an orderly, humane and safe immigration process\u8221\'20\'1D. \u8220\'20\'1CIt is hard, and it will take time, but rest assured: it will get done,\u8221\'20\'1D Mayorkas told reporters at the White House press briefing.\par \par \uc2 * New York Governor \uc2 Andrew Cuomo\uc2  is facing mounting calls for his resignation, after he was accused of sexual harassment by two women. Democratic Assemblyman Ron Kim, who previously clashed with Cuomo over his administration\u8217\'20\'19s failure to disclose the full extent of coronavirus deaths in New York nursing homes, said today, \u8220\'20\'1CHe should be issuing a genuine apology and thinking about resigning as soon as possible.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Gabrielle will have more coming up, so stay tuned.\par \par \uc2 9.16pm GMT\par \par \uc2 New York Assemblyman Ron Kim criticized \uc2 Andrew Cuomo\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s apology after the Democratic governor was accused of sexual harassment by two women.\par \par \uc2 Kim said Cuomo\u8217\'20\'19s apology failed to address the impact of his actions on the two women who have come forward, Charlotte Bennett and Lindsey Boylan.\par \par \uc2 NY Assemblyman Ron Kim (D) says \uc2 Gov. Andrew Cuomo\uc2  should be "issuing a genuine apology" and "thinking about resigning as soon as possible" over sexual harassment allegations. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/3Qnssp5w2w"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/3Qnssp5w2w}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Recount (@therecount) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/therecount/status/1366490321765486597?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 March 1, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThat is not an apology,\u8221\'20\'1D Kim said. \u8220\'20\'1CHe should be issuing a genuine apology and thinking about resigning as soon as possible.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Kim {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2021/02/17/politics/cuomo-ron-kim-nursing-home/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said last month}}}\uc2  that Cuomo threatened to \u8220\'20\'1Cdestroy\u8221\'20\'1D him, after the Democratic legislator raised concerns about the governor\u8217\'20\'19s team failing to disclose the full extent of coronavirus deaths in New York nursing homes.\par \par \uc2 9.00pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Cuomo faces mounting calls for his resignation\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 Miranda Bryant\uc2  reports from New York:\par \par \uc2 A collective of former New York state legislative employees on Monday denounced \uc2 Andrew Cuomo\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s apology for his past behaviour, after the governor was accused of sexually harassing two women, and called for his removal or resignation.\par \par \uc2 Members of the Sexual Harassment Working Group also said they expected more allegations to follow \u8211\'20\'13 and accused Cuomo of \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/lifeandstyle/2019/mar/02/abuse-prevention-how-to-turn-off-the-gaslighters"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 gaslighting}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D his accusers.\par \par \uc2 New York attorney general Letitia James, meanwhile, announced the first step in mounting an external investigation of the governor\u8217\'20\'19s behaviour.\par \par \uc2 Cuomo, the son of a former governor and himself a former US housing secretary, is one of America\u8217\'20\'19s most prominent governors. On Sunday he acknowledged for the first time that some of his behaviour towards women \u8220\'20\'1Cmay have been insensitive or too personal\u8221\'20\'1D. He also said he would cooperate with an investigation led by the state attorney general.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI acknowledge some of the things I have said have been misinterpreted as an unwanted flirtation,\u8221\'20\'1D said the Democrat, amid growing criticism from his own party. \u8220\'20\'1CTo the extent anyone felt that way, I am truly sorry about that.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/mar/01/andrew-cuomo-new-york-governor-apology-sexual-harassment-resign-calls-"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Andrew Cuomo faces new calls to resign after apology for behaviour}}}\par \par \uc2 8.45pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Sonceria Ann Berry was sworn in as the secretary of the Senate this afternoon, making her the first African American to serve in the role.\par \par \uc2 Sonceria Ann Berry is sworn in as Secretary of the U.S. Senate. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/fW9TlZmrLU"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/fW9TlZmrLU}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 CSPAN (@cspan) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/cspan/status/1366481896675409921?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 March 1, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 Senate majority leader Chuck Schumer noted it was fitting that Berry was sworn in today, as African American History Month was ending and Women\u8217\'20\'19s History Month is beginning.\par \par \uc2 8.30pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Senate will take up coronavirus relief bill 'this week', Schumer says\par \par \uc2 Senate majority leader Chuck Schumer just announced that the chamber will take up the $1.9 trillion coronavirus relief package later this week.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe Senate will take up the American Rescue Plan this week. I expect a hearty debate and some late nights,\u8221\'20\'1D the Democratic leader said.\par \par \uc2 The announcement comes two days after the House passed its version of the relief package, in a vote of 219-212.\par \par \uc2 The Senate version of the relief bill is not expected to include the $15 minimum wage provision, after the Senate parliamentarian ruled that the proposal did not meet the requirements for passage via reconciliation.\par \par \uc2 If the Senate passes a version of the bill without the minimum wage provision, the package will need to be sent back to the House for final passage.\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has said he wants to sign the relief bill by March 14, when extended unemployment benefits are currently set to expire.\par \par \uc2 Updated at 8.48pm GMT\par \par \uc2 8.16pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The Biden administration is reportedly preparing to unveil new sanctions against Russia over the poisoning and imprisonment of Kremlin critic \uc2 Alexei Navalny\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 CNN {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2021/03/01/politics/biden-administration-russia-sanctions-alexei-navalny/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reports}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 The rollout of the sanctions will happen in coordination with the \uc2 European Union\uc2 , the officials said. The measures and the exact timing will be fleshed out by US and \uc2 EU\uc2  officials in the coming days.\par \par \uc2 These sanctions would be the first costs imposed on Russia by the Biden administration and will set the tone for their policy towards Moscow going forward. They would mark a clear departure from the approach of the Trump administration, which declined to impose penalties over the poisoning and shied away from directly confronting Russia over its nefarious actions.\par \par \uc2 The Biden administration is seeking to send a \u8216\'20\'18strong message\u8217\'20\'19 on human rights and the importance of acting alongside allies with these sanctions, and there are plans to tackle a broader set of challenges posed by Russia in the coming weeks, [two administration] officials said.\par \par \uc2 Last month, a Moscow court sentenced Navalny to two years and eight months in a prison colony, sparking protests across Russia and international condemnation.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/feb/02/russian-opposition-leader-alexei-navalny-jailed"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Alexei Navalny: 1,000 arrested after protests over jailing of Russian opposition leader}}}\par \par \uc2 7.55pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Warren proposes ultra-millionaire tax on wealthiest households\par \par \uc2 Senator Elizabeth Warren has introduced a bill to impose a tax on the wealthiest US households, which was a key part of her presidential campaign last year.\par \par \uc2 If Warren\u8217\'20\'19s bill became law, it would impose a 2% annual tax on those with a net worth above $50 million. For those with a net worth above $1 billion, the annual tax would increase to 3%.\par \par \uc2 According to Warren\u8217\'20\'19s Senate office, the measure could bring in $3 trillion in revenue over 10 years, without increasing taxes for 99.95% of Americans.\par \par \uc2 Billionaire wealth is 40% higher now than when the COVID crisis began \u8211\'20\'13 but our tax system is still tilted toward the ultra-rich. Today {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RepJayapal?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @RepJayapal}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/CongBoyle?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @CongBoyle}}}\uc2  and I are introducing our {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/WealthTax?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #WealthTax}}}\uc2  bill to make the wealthiest Americans pay their fair share. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/sDgDOKr07F"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/sDgDOKr07F}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Elizabeth Warren (@SenWarren) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SenWarren/status/1366388160184352771?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 March 1, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CA wealth tax is popular among voters on both sides for good reason: because they understand the system is rigged to benefit the wealthy and large corporations,\u8221\'20\'1D Warren said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m confident lawmakers will catch up to the overwhelming majority of Americans who are demanding more fairness, more change, and who believe it\u8217\'20\'19s time for a wealth tax.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The legislation is co-sponsored by seven of Warren\u8217\'20\'19s Senate colleagues, including Bernie Sanders, and it was introduced in the House by Representatives \uc2 Pramila Jayapal\uc2  and \uc2 Brendan Boyle\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Asked about Warren\u8217\'20\'19s proposal this afternoon, White House press secretary \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2  said \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  supports increasing taxes on the wealthiest Americans, but she did not explicitly endorse the bill.\par \par \uc2 7.35pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Donald and Melania Trump received their coronavirus vaccines before leaving the White House in January, according to the \uc2 New York Times\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The report comes a day after the former president said at the Conservative Political Action Conference, \u8220\'20\'1CEverybody go get your shot.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Trump yesterday, at CPAC, said for the first time that "everyone" should get the coronavirus vaccine developed while he was in office. An adviser tells me both Trump and Melania Trump got vaccinated at the White House in January.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Maggie Haberman (@maggieNYT) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/maggieNYT/status/1366461056164507648?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 March 1, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s worth noting that the then-president chose not to receive his vaccine on camera, which might have boosted confidence in the vaccines among his supporters.\par \par \uc2 A number of senior officials, including then-Vice-President \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2 , received their vaccinations on live television in order to encourage Americans to get vaccinated as soon as they are able to.\par \par \uc2 7.28pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The words \uc2 Rudy Giuliani\uc2  and \uc2 YouTube\uc2  don\u8217\'20\'19t typically spring to mind as belonging in the same sentence together, but here we go.\par \par \uc2 YouTube\uc2  reports it has suspended Giuliani for the second time in two months after the former New York City mayor, and lawyer-cum-super-loyalist to Donald Trmp lied again in videos that the 2020 presidential election was stolen from Trump and therefore that Joe Biden \u8217\'20\'19s presidency is fraudulent.\par \par \uc2 Giuliani, who sought, spectacularly unsuccessfully, to overturn November\u8217\'20\'19s election results via legal action, will not be allowed to upload new videos for two weeks. \uc2 YouTube\uc2  also cited Giuliani\u8217\'20\'19s promotion of nicotine, in explaining its action, Bloomberg News {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bloomberg.com/news/articles/2021-03-01/youtube-suspends-rudy-giuliani-again-for-election-fraud-claims?sref=6flipp83"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reports}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe removed content from the Rudy W. Giuliani channel for violating our sale of regulated goods policy, which prohibits content facilitating the use of nicotine, and our presidential election integrity policy,\u8221\'20\'1D a YouTube spokeswoman says in a statement. \u8220\'20\'1CAdditionally, in accordance with our long standing strikes system, we issued a strike against the Rudy W. Giuliani channel, which temporarily restricts uploading or live-streaming.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Bloomberg adds that:\par \par \uc2 YouTube\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://support.google.com/youtube/answer/2802032?hl=en"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 strikes system}}}\uc2 revokes a user\u8217\'20\'19s uploading privileges for two weeks if they violate the company\u8217\'20\'19s content policies for the second time within a 90-day period. If Giuliani runs afoul of the video site\u8217\'20\'19s rules again in the same timespan, his channel will be permanently shut down. The former mayor was previously {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bloomberg.com/news/articles/2021-01-26/youtube-temporarily-suspends-rudy-giuliani-from-partner-program"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 suspended}}}\uc2  in January for election misinformation, and \uc2 YouTube\uc2  temporarily prevented him from making money from ads that run with his videos.\par \par \uc2 The former politician has accused \uc2 YouTube\uc2  of biasagainst conservatives and also posts his videos to the website Rumble, which has looser content-moderation policies.\par \par \uc2 7.04pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Democrats have backed down for their plan to use the $1.9tr coronavirus relief bill as a vehicle to phase in increases to the minimum wage to $15 an hour without Republicans backing it - but efforts to address the issue in Congress haven\u8217\'20\'19t died.\par \par \uc2 Reuters reports:\par \par \uc2 Democrats and some Republicans have voiced support for the idea of raising the minimum wage, now $7.25, for the first time since 2009, though they disagree on how much.\par \par \uc2 Republican Senators \uc2 Mitt Romney\uc2  and Tom Cotton last week proposed an increase to $10 per hour, but said employers should also verify the wage is going to workers who are legally in the US.\par \par \uc2 But two Senate Democrats acknowledged that passing an increase would be challenging in the 50-50 chamber.\par \par \uc2 The House of Representatives narrowly approved the Covid-19 package, one of Biden\u8217\'20\'19s top priorities, and aim to pass it through the Senate through a maneuver known as \u8220\'20\'1Creconciliation,\u8221\'20\'1D which would allow the bill to pass with a simple majority rather than the 60 votes normally required by that chamber\u8217\'20\'19s rules.\par \par \uc2 Senate Democrats over the weekend gave up on the Plan B idea trying to pass the wage hike by adding tax penalties to the Covid-19 bill [as not feasible] and some moderate Democrats think $15 is too high, suggesting $11 instead.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe worked through the weekend and it became clear that finalizing \u8216\'20\'18plan B\u8217\'20\'19 with the caucus would delay passage and risk going over the jobless benefits cliff on March 14,\u8221\'20\'1D one source said.\par \par \uc2 Democrats want the Covid-19 bill signed into law by March 14, when enhanced unemployment benefits expire.\par \par \uc2 Senator Bernie Sanders, an independent who caucuses with the Democrats, voiced hope that a wage hike would still happen.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSenator Sanders is determined to increase the minimum wage to $15 an hour, and he is looking at all available strategies to make it happen,\u8221\'20\'1D a source close to Sanders said.\par \par \uc2 The Senate\u8217\'20\'19s number two Democrat, Dick Durbin, said lawmakers should look for another venue to raise the minimum wage, but that it will be a challenge.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf it takes some 60 votes or a supermajority of some kind, it\u8217\'20\'19s going to be very difficult, obviously,\u8221\'20\'1D Durbin told reporters.\par \par \uc2 Another Democrat, Senator Richard Blumenthal, said he was optimistic the Democrats would find a way to raise the wage, \u8220\'20\'1Ceven though we may not have the votes right now.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The coronavirus measure would pay for vaccines and send a new round of aid to households, small businesses and state and local governments.\par \par \uc2 6.52pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Garland edges closer to confirmation\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s choice as attorney general, \uc2 Merrick Garland\uc2 , has taken an important step closer to confirmation a little earlier, when the Senate judiciary committee voted in favor of his nomination, with a strong element of bipartisan support.\par \par \uc2 The federal appellate judge\u8217\'20\'19s nomination will now come before the full senate for a vote on his confirmation. The vote was 15 in favor, seven against. Republicans, including Chuck Grassley of Iowa, \uc2 Lindsey Graham\uc2  of South Carolina, and \uc2 John Cornyn\uc2  of Texas voted to support Garland.\par \par \uc2 New: Senate Judiciary has voted to send AG nomination of \uc2 Merrick Garland\uc2  to the full Senate for a vote\par \par \uc2 Vote was 15-7. Senators Grassley, Cornyn, Tillis and Graham joined Democrats voting Yes.\par \par \uc2 Republicans Lee, Cruz, Sasse, Hawley, Cotton, Kennedy, & Blackburn voted No\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Jim Sciutto (@jimsciutto) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/jimsciutto/status/1366458098412642311?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 March 1, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 Democrats hope that Garland will now be confirmed some time this week.\par \par \uc2 Reuters further reports that:\par \par \uc2 Garland was nominated to lead a Justice Department now in the midst of intensive investigations into the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/jan/09/us-capitol-insurrection-white-supremacist-terror"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 6 attack}}}\uc2  on the US Capitol by a mob of Republican \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s supporters - an incident Garland has called \u8220\'20\'1Cheinous.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 6.24pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Today so far\par \par \uc2 The White House press briefing has now concluded. Here\u8217\'20\'19s where the day stands so far:\par \par \uc2 * The White House said \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  does not intend to overrule the Senate parliamentarian on including a $15 minimum wage provision in the coronavirus relief package. The parliamentarian announced Thursday that the minimum wage proposal does not meet the requirements to be passed using reconciliation, but a group of House progressives has called on Biden to overrule that decision by having Vice-President \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , the leader of the Senate, allow for the provision\u8217\'20\'19s inclusion in the relief bill. White House press secretary \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2  said moments ago, \u8220\'20\'1CThat is not an action that we intend to take.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 * The director of the Centers for Disease Control and Prevention warned of a potential \u8220\'20\'1Cfourth surge\u8221\'20\'1D in coronavirus cases. The CDC director, \uc2 Dr Rochelle Walensky\uc2 , voiced concern about a recent uptick in cases during today\u8217\'20\'19s briefing from the White House coronavirus response team. \u8220\'20\'1CAt this level of cases, with variants spreading, we stand to completely lose the hard-earned ground we have gained,\u8221\'20\'1D Walensky said. \u8220\'20\'1CWe have the ability to stop a potential fourth surge of cases in this country.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 * The secretary of homeland security accused the Trump administration of having \u8220\'20\'1Cdismantled our nation\u8217\'20\'19s immigration system in its entirety\u8221\'20\'1D. Secretary Alejandro Mayorkas said that the DHS is working to \u8220\'20\'1Creplace the cruelty of the past administration with an orderly, humane and safe immigration process\u8221\'20\'1D. \u8220\'20\'1CIt is hard, and it will take time, but rest assured: it will get done,\u8221\'20\'1D Mayorkas told reporters at the White House press briefing.\par \par \uc2 The blog will have more coming up, so stay tuned.\par \par \uc2 6.15pm GMT\par \par \uc2 White House press secretary \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2  would not provide clarity on how \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  intends to increase the minimum wage.\par \par \uc2 Psaki has said Biden does not plan to overrule the Senate parliamentarian, who has said the $15 minimum wage provision does not meet the requirements to be passed using reconciliation.\par \par \uc2 Given that ruling, the minimum wage proposal cannot be included in the coronavirus relief bill, but Biden has not indicated how (or when) he otherwise intends to increase the minimum wage.\par \par \uc2 Psaki simply said that Biden remains committed to raising the minimum wage to help working Americans.\par \par \uc2 6.06pm GMT\par \par \uc2 White House press secretary \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2  declined to respond to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s attacks against \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  during his speech at the Conservative Political Action Conference yesterday.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re going to spend more of our time communicating our agenda for the American people than responding to criticism from the former president,\u8221\'20\'1D Psaki said.\par \par \uc2 The White House has consistently avoided commenting on Trump since Biden took office, saying they are focusing on advancing the president\u8217\'20\'19s coronavirus relief package and the rest of his agenda.\par \par \uc2 5.58pm GMT\par \par \uc2 White House press secretary \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2  was asked whether \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  would consider sharing the US coronavirus vaccine supply with Mexico.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CNo,\u8221\'20\'1D Psaki replied, saying the president is prioritizing the vaccination of Americans right now.\par \par \uc2 The question comes hours before Biden is scheduled to virtually meet with the president of Mexico, who is expected to raise the issue of vaccine-sharing as well.\par \par \uc2 5.54pm GMT\par \par \uc2 White House says it does not intend to overrule Senate parliamentarian\par \par \uc2 White House press secretary \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2  was asked about the Senate parliamentarian\u8217\'20\'19s ruling that the $15 minimum wage provision did not meet the requirements for passage by reconciliation.\par \par \uc2 A group of House progressives has called on \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  to overrule the Senate parliamentarian by having Vice-President \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , the leader of the Senate, approve the inclusion of the minimum wage provision in the coronavirus relief package.\par \par \uc2 Psaki said having Harris overrule the parliamentarian is \u8220\'20\'1Cnot a simple decision,\u8221\'20\'1D and she noted the president and the vice-president both \u8220\'20\'1Crespect the history of the Senate\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThat is not an action that we intend to take,\u8221\'20\'1D Psaki said.\par \par \uc2 The press secretary reiterated Biden\u8217\'20\'19s commitment to raising the minimum wage, which would require a separate bill if it is not included in the relief package.\par \par \uc2 5.48pm GMT\par \par \uc2 White House press secretary \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2  has taken over the briefing, and she was asked about \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s decision not to sanction the Saudi crown prince over the murder of journalist Jamal Khashoggi.\par \par \uc2 Psaki defended the decision, claiming the administration had \u8220\'20\'1Crecalibrated the relationship\u8221\'20\'1D with Saudi Arabia to ensure such violence does not happen again.\par \par \uc2 The press secretary said the president does \u8220\'20\'1Creserve the right to take any action\u8221\'20\'1D against the Saudi crown prince in the future, but she noted that past administrations have not typically sanctioned leaders of nations with which the US has diplomatic relations.\par \par \uc2 5.39pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Alejandro Mayorkas was asked whether he would allow reporters access to the temporary detention facilities for migrant children in Texas.\par \par \uc2 A reporter noted that the \uc2 department of homeland security\uc2  has so far rejected media organizations\u8217\'20\'19 requests to access those facilities, citing the need to limit the risk of coronavirus spread.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m happy to take a look at that,\u8221\'20\'1D Mayorkas said, adding that he would need to check with fellow DHS officials about why the request was rejected.\par \par \uc2 The DHS secretary said he was committed to providing \u8220\'20\'1Copenness and transparency\u8221\'20\'1D during his tenure, and he said that principle would apply to the media.\par \par \uc2 Mayorkas also noted he was once a journalism student, but he said he \u8220\'20\'1Cwasn\u8217\'20\'19t a good enough writer to make it the whole way\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 5.34pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Alejandro Mayorkas was asked by a reporter whether he believes there is a \u8220\'20\'1Ccrisis\u8221\'20\'1D at the US-Mexican border.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe answer is no,\u8221\'20\'1D the DHS secretary replied.\par \par \uc2 Mayorkas acknowledged that there are challenges at the border, but he expressed confidence in his department\u8217\'20\'19s ability to handle those challenges.\par \par \uc2 5.32pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Alejandro Mayorkas took issue with the idea that the Biden administration \u8217\'20\'19s handling of migrant children is similar to that of the Trump administration.\par \par \uc2 The DHS secretary noted that the Trump administration expelled migrant children from the US, which the Biden administration is not doing.\par \par \uc2 The Biden White House has received criticism on the right and the left for reopening a detention center for migrant children that was used under the Trump administration.\par \par \uc2 5.27pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Alejandro Mayorkas offered some updates on the Biden administration \u8217\'20\'19s task force to reunite migrant families who were separated as a result of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Czero tolerance\u8221\'20\'1D immigration policies.\par \par \uc2 Mayorkas announced that Michelle Bran\u233\'00\'E9 will serve as the executive director of the task force. \u8220\'20\'1CShe is an extraordinary talent that will bring justice,\u8221\'20\'1D the DHS secretary said.\par \par \uc2 Mayorkas added that the administration will \u8220\'20\'1Cexplore lawful pathways\u8221\'20\'1D to allow separated families to be reunited in the US, if they want to do so.\par \par \uc2 5.20pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Alejandro Mayorkas said the \uc2 department of homeland security\uc2  is working on processing those in the \u8220\'20\'1CRemain in Mexico\u8221\'20\'1D program that was implemented during \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s presidency.\par \par \uc2 The DHS secretary emphasized that this is not the time for migrants to attempt to enter the US.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThey need to wait,\u8221\'20\'1D Mayorkas said. \u8220\'20\'1CIt takes time to rebuild the system from scratch.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Mayorkas noted that those who attempt to enter the US may be returned to Mexico in order to observe guidelines on limiting the spread of coronavirus.\par \par \uc2 5.14pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Trump 'dismantled our nation\u8217\'20\'19s immigration system in its entirety,' DHS secretary says\par \par \uc2 The daily White House press briefing is underway, and Alejandro Mayorkas, the secretary of homeland security, is speaking to reporters in the briefing room.\par \par \uc2 Mayorkas, who was confirmed by the Senate last month, said the \uc2 department of homeland security\uc2  will \u8220\'20\'1Creplace the cruelty of the past administration with an orderly, humane and safe immigration process\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The cabinet secretary accused the Trump administration of having \u8220\'20\'1Cdismantled our nation\u8217\'20\'19s immigration system in its entirety\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Mayorkas pledged to rebuild that system, saying, \u8220\'20\'1CIt is hard, and it will take time, but rest assured: it will get done.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 4.53pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Jeff Zients acknowledged that coronavirus vaccine scheduling remains \u8220\'20\'1Ctoo frustrating\u8221\'20\'1D for \u8220\'20\'1Cfar too many people\u8221\'20\'1D in the US.\par \par \uc2 The White House coronavirus response team coordinator said the Biden administration is committed to helping states improve their scheduling systems, but he made no mention of a possible national scheduling portal.\par \par \uc2 The coronavirus response team\u8217\'20\'19s press briefing has now concluded.\par \par \uc2 4.31pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Jeff Zients, the coordinator of the White House coronavirus response team, announced the country distributed an average of 1.7 million doses a day over the past week.\par \par \uc2 Zients said vaccine distribution has rebounded after last month\u8217\'20\'19s winter storm, which impacted deliveries across the central US.\par \par \uc2 According to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bloomberg.com/graphics/covid-vaccine-tracker-global-distribution/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Bloomberg}}}\uc2 , about 2.4 million vaccine doses were administered in the US yesterday.\par \par \uc2 4.25pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Jeff Zients, the coordinator of the White House coronavirus response team, said the \uc2 Johnson & Johnson\uc2  vaccine will be delivered \u8220\'20\'1Cas early as tomorrow\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 According to Zients, \uc2 Johnson & Johnson\uc2  is ready to distribute 3.9 million vaccine doses over the coming days.\par \par \uc2 But Zients added, \u8220\'20\'1CJ&J has indicated that the supply will be limited for the next couple of weeks.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Johnson & Johnson\uc2  is expected to deliver 16 million additional doses by the end of March, but the White House coronavirus response team has warned governors that those deliveries will occur \u8220\'20\'1Cpredominantly in the back half of the month\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Zients assured Americans that the federal government is ready to deliver the vaccine as soon as doses become available, saying, \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19ve done the planning. We have the distribution channels in place.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 4.20pm GMT\par \par \uc2 CDC director warns of potential 'fourth surge' in coronavirus cases\par \par \uc2 The White House coronavirus response team is now holding a briefing to provide an update on case numbers and vaccine distribution.\par \par \uc2 Dr Rochelle Walensky\uc2 , the director of the Centers for Disease Control and Prevention, warned that a recent uptick in coronavirus cases indicates another surge of cases could occur before a majority of the country is vaccinated.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe have the ability to stop a potential fourth surge of cases in this country.\u8221\'20\'1D \u8212\'20\'14 CDC Director \uc2 Rochelle Walensky{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/uVWtMBgLJn"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/uVWtMBgLJn}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Recount (@therecount) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/therecount/status/1366420996975116290?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 March 1, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAt this level of cases, with variants spreading, we stand to completely lose the hard-earned ground we have gained,\u8221\'20\'1D Walensky said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CNow is not the time to relax the critical safeguards that we know can stop the spread of Covid-19 in our communities, not when we are so close. We have the ability to stop a potential fourth surge of cases in this country.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Updated at 4.26pm GMT\par \par \uc2 4.07pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The White House has released a video, featuring \uc2 Dr Anthony Fauci\uc2 , that encourages Americans to get the \uc2 Johnson & Johnson\uc2  vaccine.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI would definitely take the \uc2 Johnson & Johnson\uc2  vaccine,\u8221\'20\'1D Fauci says in the video. \u8220\'20\'1CThis is a vaccine that works, and it only requires one dose.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 On Saturday, the \uc2 FDA\uc2  issued an emergency use authorization for the Johnson & Johnson COVID-19 vaccine. Dr. Fauci sat down to answer your questions. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/KJQ2SrVclp"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/KJQ2SrVclp}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 President Biden (@POTUS) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/POTUS/status/1366404049252347904?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 March 1, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Food and Drug Administration\uc2  approved an emergency use authorization for the \uc2 Johnson & Johnson\uc2  vaccine on Saturday, making it the third vaccine to be approved for distribution in the US.\par \par \uc2 While the \uc2 Johnson & Johnson\uc2  vaccine has a lower efficacy rate than the \uc2 Pfizer\uc2  and Moderna vaccines, it has a couple distinct advantages. Namely, the \uc2 Johnson & Johnson\uc2  vaccine can be administered in one dose, rather than two, and it can be stored in a regular refrigerator, unlike the \uc2 Pfizer\uc2  and Moderna vaccines.\par \par \uc2 3.41pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The White House has signaled that \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  will not attempt to overrule the Senate parliamentarian on including the minimum wage provision in the coronavirus relief bill.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CPresident Biden is disappointed in this outcome, as he proposed having the $15 minimum wage as part of the American Rescue Plan,\u8221\'20\'1D White House press secretary \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2  said in a statement on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHe respects the parliamentarian\u8217\'20\'19s decision and the Senate\u8217\'20\'19s process. He will work with leaders in Congress to determine the best path forward because no one in this country should work full time and live in poverty.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Psaki added that Biden was urging Congress to pass the coronavirus relief package as quickly as possible, indicating he believed Democrats should try to pass the $15 minimum wage proposal in a separate bill.\par \par \uc2 But unless Democrats eliminate the Senate filibuster, they will need to attract the support of 10 Senate Republicans to pass such a bill, which seems very unlikely.\par \par \uc2 3.24pm GMT\par \par \uc2 House progressives urge Biden to overrule parliamentarian on $15 minimum wage\par \par \uc2 A group of progressive House members has sent a letter to \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , urging the president to overrule the Senate parliamentarian on including a $15 minimum wage increase in the coronavirus relief package.\par \par \uc2 The House members argued that Vice-President \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , as the leader of the Senate, has the authority to make a final decision on whether the minimum wage provision is allowed to be included in a bill being passed using reconciliation.\par \par \uc2 The letter comes four days after the Senate parliamentarian, \uc2 Elizabeth MacDonough\uc2 , ruled that the minimum wage proposal did not meet the strict budgetary requirements attached to reconciliation bills.\par \par \uc2 In our democracy, the Vice President as leader of the Senate, or whoever is Chair, has the final say, not the parliamentarian.\par \par \uc2 Many of my colleagues and I believe we can and must deliver a $15 wage through reconciliation. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/heBR4DjCEp"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/heBR4DjCEp}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Rep. Ro Khanna\uc2  (@RepRoKhanna) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RepRoKhanna/status/1366389050597400577?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 March 1, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CEighty-one million people cast their ballots to elect you on a platform that called for a $15 minimum wage,\u8221\'20\'1D the progressives told Biden in their letter.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe urge you to keep that promise and call on the Presiding Officer of the Senate to refute the Senate Parliamentarian\u8217\'20\'19s advice on a Byrd Rule point of order and maintain the $15 minimum wage provision in the American Rescue Plan.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The letter is signed by Representatives \uc2 Ro Khanna\uc2 , Alexandria Ocasio-Cortez and \uc2 Cori Bush\uc2 , as well as 20 other lawmakers.\par \par \uc2 Khanna added in a statement, \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19ve been asked, politely but firmly, to compromise on nearly all of our principles & goals. Not this time. If we don\u8217\'20\'19t overrule the Senate parliamentarian, we are condoning poverty wages for millions of Americans.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 3.04pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Former French president \uc2 Nicolas Sarkozy\uc2  sentenced to jail\par \par \uc2 A court has found {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/nicolas-sarkozy"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Nicolas Sarkozy}}}\uc2  guilty of corruption and influence peddling and sentenced the former French president to three years in prison with two of them suspended.\par \par \uc2 France\u8217\'20\'19s president from 2007 to 2012 was accused of forging a \u8220\'20\'1Ccorruption pact\u8221\'20\'1D with his lawyer and a senior magistrate. Judges said there was \u8220\'20\'1Cserious evidence\u8221\'20\'1D of collaboration {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2020/dec/08/nicolas-sarkozy-graft-trial-prosecutors-call-for-four-year-sentence"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 between the three men}}}\uc2  to break the law.\par \par \uc2 The court had heard how Sarkozy instructed his lawyer, Thierry Herzog, to offer the magistrate a cushy job on the C\u244\'00\'F4te d\u8217\'20\'19Azur in return for information on a separate investigation centred on the rightwing politician.\par \par \uc2 It is unlikely the former president will spend a day in jail. The one-year prison sentence can be served with certain conditions, including the wearing of an electronic bracelet, or limited home confinement.\par \par \uc2 Sarkozy is expected to appeal against the conviction.\par \par \uc2 The verdict, delivered on Monday afternoon, will quash his hopes of returning to public life in time for next year\u8217\'20\'19s presidential election. His centre-right Les R\u233\'00\'E9publicains party has been struggling to come up with a credible candidate since Sarkozy\u8217\'20\'19s former prime minister \uc2 Fran\u231\'00\'E7ois Fillon\uc2  was engulfed in scandal during the 2017 presidential race, opening the way for \uc2 Emmanuel Macron\uc2  to win.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/mar/01/former-french-president-nicolas-sarkozy-sentenced-to-three-years-for-corruption"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Former French president Nicolas Sarkozy sentenced to jail for corruption}}}\par \par \uc2 2.48pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  used his speech at the Conservative Political Action Conference yesterday to once again lie about the results of the 2020 presidential election and attack \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s agenda.\par \par \uc2 But the former president spent almost no time addressing the $1.9 trillion coronavirus relief package that the House passed this weekend, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/meet-the-press/trump-mostly-avoided-covid-relief-his-cpac-speech-speaks-volumes-n1259123"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 NBC News notes}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18The Democrats now say we have to pass their $1.9 trillion boondoggle to open schools, but a very small part of it has to do with that,\u8217\'20\'19 [Trump] said. \u8216\'20\'18You know where it\u8217\'20\'19s going \u8212\'20\'14 it\u8217\'20\'19s going to bailout badly-run Democrat cities, so much of it.\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 That\u8217\'20\'19s it. In almost 90 minutes of remarks, Trump devoted just two sentences of criticism to Biden\u8217\'20\'19s first legislative priority as president.\par \par \uc2 And it says a lot about the state of GOP opposition to the Covid relief bill, which remains {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.pollingreport.com/budget.htm"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 popular in polls}}}\uc2  : While House Republicans uniformly {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://clerk.house.gov/evs/2021/roll049.xml"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 voted against it on Saturday}}}\uc2 , it hasn\u8217\'20\'19t been an animating issue for Republicans.\par \par \uc2 2.30pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The White House press secretary, \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2 , will hold her daily briefing for reporters in about three hours.\par \par \uc2 Psaki said Alejandro Mayorkas, the new secretary of homeland security, would also attend the briefing, ahead of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s virtual meeting with the president of Mexico this afternoon.\par \par \uc2 Looking forward to welcoming {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SecMayorkas?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @SecMayorkas}}}\uc2  to the briefing today at 12pm. And follow him at his new government \uc2 Twitter\uc2  account\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2  (@PressSec) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/PressSec/status/1366391721672790019?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 March 1, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 Mayorkas, who was confirmed by the Senate last month, is the first immigrant and the first Latino American to lead the \uc2 department of homeland security\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Mayorkas {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.usatoday.com/story/news/nation/2021/02/05/alejandro-mayorkas-prosecutor-latino-immigrant-biden-homeland-security/4374767001/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has pledged}}}\uc2  to reform America\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Cbroken immigration system\u8221\'20\'1D and enforce immigration laws \u8220\'20\'1Cin a way that is humane, respects due process, and strengthens our nation and its economy\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 2.14pm GMT\par \par \uc2 This is Joan Greve in Washington, taking over for Martin Belam.\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is scheduled to virtually meet with Mexican President \uc2 Andr\u233\'00\'E9s Manuel L\u243\'00\'F3pez Obrador\uc2  today, marking the first official meeting between the neighboring leaders.\par \par \uc2 The AP {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/joe-biden-global-trade-mexico-coronavirus-pandemic-immigration-edb25cf298b7c9a83d15ff4f6c7ea95f"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has more details}}}\uc2  on the agenda of the meeting:\par \par \uc2 Mexico\u8217\'20\'19s president has said he intends during the meeting to propose to Biden a new Bracero-style immigrant labor program that could bring 600,000 to 800,000 Mexican and Central American immigrants a year to work legally in the United States.\par \par \uc2 A senior Biden administration official declined to say whether the U.S. president would back or oppose the proposal, saying only that both countries agree on the need to expand legal pathways for migration. The official insisted on anonymity to discuss private conversations.\par \par \uc2 The original Bracero program allowed Mexicans to work temporarily in the United States to fill labor shortages during World War II and for a couple of decades after the war. \uc2 L\u243\'00\'F3pez Obrador\uc2  said the U.S. economy needs Mexican workers because of \u8216\'20\'18their strength, their youth.\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 The Biden official said the meeting will enable Biden begin to institutionalize the relationship with Mexico, rather than let it be determined by tweets \u8212\'20\'14 a preferred form of diplomacy by his predecessor, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The blog will have more updates on that meeting and the other news of the day coming up, so stay tuned.\par \par \uc2 1.48pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  will hear a case tomorrow that could allow the court\u8217\'20\'19s conservative majority to deal a major blow to the most powerful remaining provision of the Voting Rights Act, the 1965 law designed to prevent racial discrimination in voting.\par \par \uc2 The case, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.scotusblog.com/case-files/cases/brnovich-v-democratic-national-committee/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Brnovich v Democratic National Committee}}}\uc2 , involves a dispute over two Arizona measures. One is a 2016 law that bans anyone other than a close family member or caregiver from collecting absentee ballots, sometimes called ballot harvesting. The second is a measure that requires officials to reject ballots cast in the wrong precinct, even if the voter has cast a vote in statewide races.\par \par \uc2 Arizona rejected more than {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.supremecourt.gov/DocketPDF/19/19-1257/166166/20210113151530581_19-1257%20-1258%20DNC%20Resps%20BOM.pdf#page=23"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 38,335 ballots}}}\uc2  cast in the wrong precinct between 2008 and 2016 and minority voters were twice as likely than white voters to have their ballots rejected, the DNC noted in its brief. Minority voters, including the state\u8217\'20\'19s Native American population, are disproportionately harmed by the ballot collection ban because they are more likely to lack reliable mail service.\par \par \uc2 The DNC argues that the policies violated section 2 of the Voting Rights Act, which prohibits voting laws that discriminate based on race. A trial court ruled in 2018 that the policies did not violate the law, and a three-judge panel on the US court of appeals for the ninth circuit later upheld that ruling. But the full circuit voted to rehear the case and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.courtlistener.com/pdf/2020/01/27/dnc_v._katie_hobbs.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  last year found}}}\uc2  that the policies did violate the Voting Rights Act. Now, Arizona attorney general \uc2 Mark Brnovich\uc2 , a Republican, and the Arizona Republican party are appealing that ruling to the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 And though the facts in the case are about Arizona, the stakes could extend far beyond it. Brnovich and the Arizona Republican party are urging the court to use the case as a vehicle for announcing a narrower view of section 2 than the one currently in use.\par \par \uc2 Such a ruling would take away one of most powerful tools that voting rights groups have to challenge discriminatory voting laws. Section 2 was elevated after the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s 2013 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/2013/jun/25/supreme-court-voting-rights-act-live"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 decision in Shelby County v Holder}}}\uc2  that struck down another Voting Rights Act provision requiring certain places with a history of voting discrimination, including Arizona, to submit voting laws to the federal government for pre-clearance before they went into effect.\par \par \uc2 Read more of Sam Levine\u8217\'20\'19s report: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/mar/01/us-supreme-court-voting-rights-act-provision"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US supreme court could deal blow to provision protecting minority voters}}}\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/mar/01/us-supreme-court-voting-rights-act-provision"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US supreme court could deal blow to provision protecting minority voters}}}\par \par \uc2 1.42pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Johnson & Johnson\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Covid-19 vaccine to roll-out to Americans within 48 hours\par \par \uc2 Americans should be able to receive \uc2 Johnson & Johnson\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Covid-19 vaccine within the next 24 to 48 hours, its chief executive said this morning after regulators approved the vaccine, making it the country\u8217\'20\'19s third available one for the coronavirus, report Reuters.\par \par \uc2 The drugmaker was still on track to deliver 4 million vaccine doses this week, and 100 million doses by June, CEO \uc2 Alex Gorsky\uc2  told NBC News\u8217\'20\'19 Today program in an interview.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWithin the next 24 to 28 hours, Americans should start receiving shots in arms. They\u8217\'20\'19re literally rolling out with the trucks as we speak,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 Pfizer\uc2 -BioNTech and Moderna have FDA-approved two-dose vaccines. Unlike those vaccines, the \uc2 Johnson &Johnson\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s version requires no refrigeration and only a single dose is needed, potentially facilitating wider use.\par \par \uc2 1.35pm GMT\par \par \uc2 A former digital strategist for \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2  has demanded an end to big tech\u8217\'20\'19s profit-driven optimization of outrage and called for regulators to curb online disinformation and division.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://michaelslaby.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Michael Slaby}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 author of a new book, For All the People: Redeeming the Broken Promises of Modern Media and Reclaiming Our Civic Life \u8211\'20\'13 described tech giants \uc2 Facebook\uc2  and \uc2 Google\uc2  as \u8220\'20\'1Ctwo gorillas\u8221\'20\'1D crushing the very creativity needed to combat conspiracy theories spread by former US president \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and others.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe systems are not broken,\u8221\'20\'1D Slaby, 43, told \uc2 the Guardian\uc2  by phone from his home in Rhinebeck, New York. \u8220\'20\'1CThey are working exactly as they were designed for the benefit of their designers. They can be designed differently. We can express and encourage a different set of public values about the public goods that we need from our public sphere.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Slaby believes \uc2 Facebook\uc2  and \uc2 Twitter\uc2  were too slow to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/tech/tech-news/how-facebook-twitter-decided-take-down-trump-s-accounts-n1254317"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 remove Trump from their platforms.}}}\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1CThis is where I think they hide behind arguments like the first amendment,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CThe first amendment is about government suppression of speech; it doesn\u8217\'20\'19t have anything to do with your access to \uc2 Facebook\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Slaby calls for a combination of moral leadership, public advocacy, engagement by politicians, new regulatory frameworks and collective action by users to rein in a few private companies that currently wield massive influence over the public sphere.\par \par \uc2 Read more of David Smith\u8217\'20\'19s interview with Michael Slaby here here: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2021/mar/01/facebook-google-big-tech-regulation-michael-slaby-interview"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Optimizing for outrage \u8211\'20\'13 ex-Obama digital chief urges curbs on big tech}}}\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2021/mar/01/facebook-google-big-tech-regulation-michael-slaby-interview"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Optimizing for outrage: ex-Obama digital chief urges curbs on big tech}}}\par \par \uc2 1.30pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Calls for a boycott of Goya beans, chickpeas and other foodstuffs have grown louder after chief executive \uc2 Robert Unanue\uc2  made a series of false claims about the presidential election in a speech to the Conservative Political Action Conference, or {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://viewer.gutools.co.uk/us-news/cpac"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 CPAC}}}\uc2 , in Florida on Sunday.\par \par \uc2 Unanue has previously {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://viewer.gutools.co.uk/us-news/2020/jul/16/ivanka-trump-goya-foods-ethics-rules"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 courted controversy}}}\uc2  with praise for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , which last year prompted \uc2 Ivanka Trump\uc2  to pose, infamously, with a can of Goya beans.\par \par \uc2 If it\u8217\'20\'19s Goya, it has to be good.\par \par \uc2 Si es Goya, tiene que ser bueno. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/9tjVrfmo9z"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/9tjVrfmo9z}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Ivanka Trump\uc2  (@IvankaTrump) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/IvankaTrump/status/1283221019684110337?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 15, 2020}}}\par \par \uc2 Onstage in Orlando, Unanue called {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://viewer.gutools.co.uk/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1Cthe real, legitimate and still actual president of the United States\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 He also falsely claimed the presidential election that Trump lost conclusively to \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and the state contest in Georgia, which Biden won narrowly, were \u8220\'20\'1Cnot legitimate\u8221\'20\'1D, and claimed mail-in ballots were fraudulent.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe still have faith,\u8221\'20\'1D Unanue said, \u8220\'20\'1Cthat the majority of the people of the United States voted for the president \u8230\'20\'26 I think a great majority of the people in the United States voted for President Trump, and even a few Democrats.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Biden won more than 81m votes, or 51.3% of the total cast, to more than 74m for Trump. The Democrat won the electoral college 306-232, a margin Trump called a landslide when it was in his favour over \uc2 Hillary Clinton\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 1.27pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Last night president \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  tweeted out his support of \uc2 Amazon\uc2  warehouse workers in Bessemer, Alabama who are attempting to get union recognition, saying that \u8220\'20\'1CEvery worker should have a free and fair choice to join a union.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Workers in Alabama \u8211\'20\'13 and all across America \u8211\'20\'13 are voting on whether to organize a union in their workplace. It\u8217\'20\'19s a vitally important choice \u8211\'20\'13 one that should be made without intimidation or threats by employers.\par \par \uc2 Every worker should have a free and fair choice to join a union. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/2lzbyyii1g"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/2lzbyyii1g}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 President Biden (@POTUS) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/POTUS/status/1366191901196644354?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 March 1, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 The Retail, Wholesale and Department Store Union president \uc2 Stuart Appelbaum\uc2  issued a statement of thanks for the president\u8217\'20\'19s support last night, saying:\par \par \uc2 Thank you, president Biden, for sending a clear message of support for the BAmazon Union workers in Alabama seeking to bring the \uc2 first union\uc2  to an \uc2 Amazon\uc2  warehouse with the RWDSU. As President Biden points out, the best way for working people to protect themselves and their families is by organizing into unions. And that is why so many working women and men are fighting for a union at the \uc2 Amazon\uc2  facility in Bessemer, Alabama.\par \par \uc2 The retail giant has been heavily criticised for {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2021/feb/03/amazon-intensifies-severe-effort-discourage-first-warehouse-union"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 heavy-handed tactics}}}\uc2  in an attempt to sway workers to vote no to union representation.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2021/feb/23/amazon-bessemer-alabama-union"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 'We deserve more': an Amazon warehouse\u8217\'20\'19s high-stakes union drive}}}\par \par \uc2 1.21pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Across {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/california"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 California}}}\uc2 , hundreds of thousands of people armed with signs and clipboards are gathering outside of local Walmarts, in shopping center parking lots, and on beachside boardwalks, trying to convince their neighbors that the governor needs to go.\par \par \uc2 An effort to recall \uc2 Gavin Newsom\uc2  has gained momentum in recent weeks, as the California governor\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://igs.berkeley.edu/sites/default/files/release_2021-01_governor_newsom.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 approval ratings dipped}}}\uc2  amid mounting frustration over how the state has handled the Covid pandemic, and the economic slump caused by closures.\par \par \uc2 So far, the campaign appears on track to get the signatures they need by a deadline of 17 March. If their efforts succeed, a recall election could be held before the end of the year.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe knew this was going to be big. We didn\u8217\'20\'19t know it was going to be this big\u8221\'20\'1D said Randy Economy, a spokesperson and political adviser for the RecallGavin2020 campaign.\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s still extremely unlikely that a majority of Californians would choose to oust Newsom. State records show {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.sos.ca.gov/elections/recalls/complete-list-recall-attempts"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  almost every California governor since 1960}}}\uc2  has faced recall efforts, but only one \u8211\'20\'13 Gray Davis in 2003 \u8211\'20\'13 has been successfully removed. Newsom, who defeated his Republican opponent by 24 points in 2018, has largely retained enough support from the Democratic base needed to keep him in power, despite the challenges of 2020.\par \par \uc2 Though his popularity has waned in recent months, analysts say the success of the recall movement is more of a reflection of a political polarization in the state that has widened during the pandemic and the 2020 election. The campaign has catered to conservative Californians who feel unheard by the Democratic supermajority who run the state, and the recall has gained traction and resources from a small but vocal but Republican electorate.\par \par \uc2 By early February, the effort {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cal-access.sos.ca.gov/PDFGen/pdfgen.prg?filingid=2559985&amendid=0"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  had raised more than $2.5m}}}\uc2  according to financial disclosures filed with the State, and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://rescuecalifornia.org/about/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  Rescue California}}}\uc2 , the organization created to remove Gray Davis from office in 2003 has been a major contributor. The recall {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.fppc.ca.gov/transparency/top-contributors/recall-election-Newsom.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  has also been bankrolled}}}\uc2  the former Arkansas governor and ardent Trump supporter \uc2 Mike Huckabee\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s political action committee, and the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://news.yahoo.com/california-gop-pumps-125k-recall-222919142.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  California Republican party}}}\uc2 . There was also a contribution of $500,000 from a company called Prov. 3:9 LLC, which {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.latimes.com/california/story/2021-01-04/california-campaign-watchdog-complaint-newsom-recall"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  triggered a \u8220\'20\'1Cdark money\u8221\'20\'1D complaint}}}\uc2  by the former chair of the Federal Election Commission over accusations that the organization is a shell company to disguise donors.\par \par \uc2 Read more of Gabrielle Canon\u8217\'20\'19s report: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/mar/01/gavin-newsom-california-push-recall"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Push to recall California governor Gavin Newsom gains steam \u8211\'20\'13 but who\u8217\'20\'19s behind it?}}}\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/mar/01/gavin-newsom-california-push-recall"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Push to recall California governor Gavin Newsom gains steam \u8211\'20\'13 but who's behind it? }}}\par \par \uc2 12.58pm GMT\par \par \uc2 One thing that was widely expected with \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  taking control of the White House was a return to pre-Trump norms. That hasn\u8217\'20\'19t happened in all cases \u8211\'20\'13 and one of those is the way that the public can track who has visited or spoken to the president. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2021/03/01/biden-white-house-transparency-trump-obama-471868"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Anita Kumar writes for Politico}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 Five weeks into office, Biden has fallen short of his former boss, \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2 , in several areas, and is under pressure to do more to restore confidence in the federal government following Trump\u8217\'20\'19s chaotic term in the White House.\par \par \uc2 Among the critiques: The schedules for the president and vice president aren\u8217\'20\'19t posted online. The White House comment line is shut down. There are no citizen petitions on the White House\u8217\'20\'19s website. The White House has committed to releasing visitor logs. But it doesn\u8217\'20\'19t plan to divulge the names of attendees of virtual meetings, which are the primary mode of interaction until the coronavirus pandemic eases.\par \par \uc2 And while Biden has received kudos for keeping the American public informed, primarily by resuming the daily White House press briefings, he has yet to hold a news conference of his own.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe steps they\u8217\'20\'19ve taken are welcome, but insufficient to the moment and the need,\u8221\'20\'1D said Alex Howard, an open government advocate who directs the Digital Democracy Project at the Demand Progress Educational Fund, an arm of a left-leaning group. \u8220\'20\'1CThey need to keep \u8216\'20\'18showing their work\u8217\'20\'19 by opening Cabinet meetings, disclosing information and using political capital to emphasize that being \u8216\'20\'18open by default\u8217\'20\'19 isn\u8217\'20\'19t just an option but an obligation across the government.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Read more here: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2021/03/01/biden-white-house-transparency-trump-obama-471868"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Politico \u8211\'20\'13 Biden won\u8217\'20\'19t release White House visitor logs}}}\par \par \uc2 12.35pm GMT\par \par \uc2 David Sirota {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2021/mar/01/joe-biden-minimum-wage-democrats"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 writes for us today}}}\uc2  on that minimum wage issue:\par \par \uc2 When a Republican is president, Democratic politicians, pundits and activists will tell you that the presidency is an all-powerful office that can do anything it wants. When a Democrat is president, these same politicians, pundits and activists will tell you that the presidency has no power to do anything. In fact, they will tell you a Democratic president cannot even use the bully pulpit and other forms of pressure to try to shift the votes of senators in his own party.\par \par \uc2 A tale from history proves this latter myth is complete garbage \u8211\'20\'13 and that tale is newly relevant in today\u8217\'20\'19s supercharged debate over a $15 minimum wage.\par \par \uc2 In that debate so far, we have seen Democratic senators prepare to surrender the $15 minimum wage their party {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wwlp.com/news/biden-pushes-for-increasing-minimum-wage-to-15-an-hour/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 promised}}}\uc2  by insisting they are powerless in the face of a non-binding advisory opinion of a parliamentarian they can {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.dailyposter.com/p/breaking-secret-memo-shows-how-harris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ignore}}}\uc2  or {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/nation/2021/02/26/senate-parliamentarian-minimum-wage-overrule/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 fire}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 That explanation is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/davidsirota/status/1366107871419621377?s=20"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 patently ridiculous}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.dailyposter.com/p/breaking-secret-memo-shows-how-harris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 factually false}}}\uc2 , so Democratic apologists are starting to further justify the surrender by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/billscher/status/1365016024207269890?s=20"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 suggesting}}}\uc2  that even if the party kept a $15 minimum wage in the Covid relief bill, conservative Democrats such as \uc2 Joe Manchin\uc2  and \uc2 Kyrsten Sinema\uc2  would block it anyway.\par \par \uc2 The White House itself is now falling back on the idea that it {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/jeneps/status/1365098078529675264?s=20"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 doesn\u8217\'20\'19t}}}\uc2  have the votes to do much of anything, insinuating that \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 who occupies the world\u8217\'20\'19s most powerful office \u8211\'20\'13 somehow has no power to try to change the legislative dynamic. And this spin is being predictably amplified {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/JamesSurowiecki/status/1364205145064697858"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 across}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/drvolts/status/1365759988342300672"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 social media}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 To be sure, there is no guarantee that Manchin or Sinema could be moved. Maybe they couldn\u8217\'20\'19t, but maybe they could, considering they have both {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/story/2014/02/joe-manchin-minimum-wage-104056"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 previously}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.congress.gov/bill/113th-congress/house-bill/1010/cosponsors?searchResultViewType=expanded"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 supported}}}\uc2  bills to increase the minimum wage. And we know they may be sensitive to pressure. After all, Manchin recently {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.usatoday.com/story/news/politics/2021/02/03/joe-manchin-and-kamala-harris-sparred-over-west-virginia-interviews/4370364001/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 freaked out}}}\uc2  and whined that \u8220\'20\'1Cno one called me\u8221\'20\'1D when vice president \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  dared to do one straightforward interview with a West Virginia television station.\par \par \uc2 Whether such would pressure works, the point is indisputable: it is laughable and preposterous to argue that a newly elected president has zero power to even try to shift the dynamic.\par \par \uc2 Read more here: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2021/mar/01/joe-biden-minimum-wage-democrats"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 David Sirota \u8211\'20\'13 Joe Biden says his hands are tied on a $15 minimum wage. That\u8217\'20\'19s not true}}}\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2021/mar/01/joe-biden-minimum-wage-democrats"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Joe Biden says his hands are tied on a $15 minimum wage. That's not true | David Sirota}}}\par \par \uc2 12.27pm GMT\par \par \uc2 There\u8217\'20\'19s a solid group of Democrats who thing the way forward for the minimum wage policy is to overturn the decision of the Senate parliamentarian, and there is a #Keep15In movement rapidly forming. They are planning a digital meeting at 9am EST today (that\u8217\'20\'19s 1400 GMT).\par \par \uc2 Reps Ro Khanna, \uc2 Rashida Tlaib\uc2  and Andy Level Levin will be joining a women of color-led coalition who have set up the event, which will call on the Biden-Harris administration to disregard the Senate parliamentarian advisory opinion and press ahead.\par \par \uc2 The members of Congress will be unveiling a public letter signed by around 20 additional members of Congress they have organized to call on the administration to proceed in this manner. This is on top of a letter of petition signed by 150,000 people asking the White House \u8220\'20\'1Cto do what it takes to pass the Raise the Wage Act\u8221\'20\'1D. The letter opens:\par \par \uc2 We are women of color, people of color, women, low-wage workers and organizations that represent and support them. We are writing to urge you to use the full power of your office to bring essential financial relief to all working people in America, by ensuring that a $15 federal minimum wage is included in the budget reconciliation process, regardless of the opinion of the parliamentarian.\par \par \uc2 As president of the Senate, vice president Harris has the constitutional power to disregard the recommendation of the Senate parliamentarian and include this provision in the Covid relief legislation.\par \par \uc2 The vast bipartisan majority of Americans support this policy. President Biden simply must rise up for the communities who turned out in record numbers to elect him and support the vice president in taking this action on behalf of his administration.\par \par \uc2 12.11pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Jeff Stein reports overnight for the Washington Post on the news that senior Democrat lawmakers appear to have abandoned a potential \u8220\'20\'1Cplan B\u8221\'20\'1D for getting a $15 per hour minimum federal wage through the Senate in its existing form. Last week the Senate parliamentarian, \uc2 Elizabeth MacDonough\uc2 , ruled that its inclusion in the Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 $1.9 trillion Covid recovery plan breached Senate procedure. Stein writes:\par \par \uc2 Last week Senate finance chair Ron Wyden and Senate budget chair Bernie Sanders said they would instead seek to add tax penalties on large corporations that fail to pay $15 an hour \u8212\'20\'14 an idea viewed as less likely to be struck down by the parliamentarian and still helpful to some minimum-wage workers.\par \par \uc2 But now senior Democrats \u8212\'20\'14 including Wyden and Sanders \u8212\'20\'14 are walking away from that backup effort. Economists and tax experts have said that the tax outlined by Sanders and Wyden could be easily avoided and difficult to implement, with large corporations able to reclassify workers as contractors to avoid potential penalties. \u8220\'20\'1CI would be extremely nervous about trying out a brand new idea like this with virtually no vetting,\u8221\'20\'1D \uc2 Jason Furman\uc2 , a former Obama administration economist, said on Friday.\par \par \uc2 Wyden and Sanders were also expected to face an uphill battle in persuading the entire Senate Democratic caucus to support a proposal they would have only days to draft. The White House has not indicated support for the corporate tax penalty idea.\par \par \uc2 The Covid relief package has been passed by the House, but is yet to go through the Senate, who, according to the parliamentarian\u8217\'20\'19s ruling, will have to strip out the provision on the minimum wage increase. The level has been set at $7.25 since 2009. The White House has indicated it is unwilling to go against the parliamentarian\u8217\'20\'19s ruling.\par \par \uc2 Read more here: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/us-policy/2021/02/28/minimum-wage-backup-plan-biden-stimulus/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Washington Post \u8211\'20\'13 Senior Democrats abandon backup plan on $15 minimum wage}}}\par \par \uc2 12.05pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Welcome to our live coverage of US politics on Monday, the day after \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  made a return to public life with his talk at CPAC. Here\u8217\'20\'19s a catch up on where we are, and what we might expect from today\u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 * Democrats remain divided over how to proceed on the $15 minimum wage issue \u8211\'20\'13 some senior lawmakers appear to have given a backup plan to increase the minimum wage through a corporate tax penalty.\par \par \uc2 * Progressive Democrats however plan a #Keep15In event today, designed to pressure the Biden-Harris administration to disregard the Senate parliamentarian\u8217\'20\'19s advisory ruling and keep the measure in the Covid relief package, as it was passed in the House.\par \par \uc2 * {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/feb/28/white-house-defends-not-sanction-saudi-crown-prince-khashoggi-killing"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The White House has defended its decision not to directly sanction Saudi Arabia\u8217\'20\'19s crown prince Mohammed bin Salman}}}\uc2  over the killing of the journalist Jamal Khashoggi, as criticism grew before Washington\u8217\'20\'19s unveiling of a new policy towards Riyadh today.\par \par \uc2 * Twice-impeached ex-president \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  used {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/feb/28/donald-trump-cpac-speech-republican-party-2024-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 his speech at the rightwing CPAC event}}}\uc2  to propagate the lie of a \u8220\'20\'1Crigged\u8221\'20\'1D 2020 election and hinted at 2024 run.\par \par \uc2 * Grasping for continued relevance, Trump returned to his political comfort zone by fearmongering about immigrants and unleashing angry tirades against \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , his Republican critics and the media.\par \par \uc2 * Despite the teasing of another run to the White House, Louisiana Republican senator {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/feb/28/trump-republican-party-election-2024"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Bill Cassidy predicted that Trump will not be the party\u8217\'20\'19s nominee for president in 2024}}}\uc2 , pointing to the number of seats lost by Republicans in the House and Senate over the four years Trump was in office.\par \par \uc2 * The \uc2 Hyatt Hotels Corporation\uc2  called symbols of hate \u8220\'20\'1Cabhorrent\u8221\'20\'1D on Sunday after {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/mar/01/cpac-2021-stage-design-nazi-sign-odal-othala-rune-hyatt-hotels-hate-symbol-abhorrent"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the design of a stage at CPAC at one of its hotels drew comparisons to a Norse rune used by Nazis}}}\uc2  during the second world war.\par \par \uc2 * {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/feb/28/andrew-cuomo-sexual-harassment-allegations-charlotte-bennett"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The crisis enveloping New York governor Andrew Cuomo deepened}}}\uc2  as the state\u8217\'20\'19s attorney general demanded he grant her the authority to investigate claims he sexually harassed at least two women who worked for him. The governor admitted his behaviour may have been \u8220\'20\'1Cmisinterpreted as an unwanted flirtation\u8221\'20\'1D and offered a qualified apology.\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  will return to Washington DC from Delaware this morning. At 4.30 EST (2130 GMT) he will meet virtually with president \uc2 Andr\u233\'00\'E9s Manuel L\u243\'00\'F3pez Obrador\uc2  of Mexico\par \par \uc2 * Also today, \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2  delivers her press briefing at noon, and the coronavirus response team will brief the media at 1pm.\par \par \uc2 2021-03-01T12:05:56Z2021-03-02T01:45:37Z{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://media.guim.co.uk/16e3d9a719baa82b897c996e0f6d3b080041fb01/0_0_6892_4137/500.jpgThe"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://media.guim.co.uk/16e3d9a719baa82b897c996e0f6d3b080041fb01/0_0_6892_4137/500.jpgThe}}}\uc2  White House press secretary, \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2 , talks to reporters at the White House in Washington DC Monday.It\u8217\'20\'19s getting hot in here. Giuliani in the Republican National Committee Headquarters in Washington, DC, USA, 19 November 2020.The U.S. Capitol Building and the Washington Monument are reflected in the Lincoln Memorial reflecting pool as people enjoy the weather outdoors on the National Mall on Saturday, Feb. 27, 2021.Merrick Garland testifies before a \uc2 Senate Judiciary Committee\uc2  hearing on his nomination to be U.S. Attorney General on Capitol Hill last week.Robert Unanue, owner of \uc2 Goya Foods\uc2 , addresses CPAC.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020210301eh31001ut\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
