\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Republicans push 'blue-collar comeback' \u8211\'20\'13 but is the party a true friend of the worker?\b0\par\par\uc2 Richard Luscombe in Miami \par \uc2 1,053 \uc2 words\par \uc2 27 February 2021\par 19:44 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2021.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Multimillionaire Trump ally and senators who oppose $15 wage rise among those promoting idea that party is for working people\par \par \uc2 Amid the resurrection of \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/feb/27/cpac-republicans-trump-election-lie"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the big lie}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D about an election stolen from \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , another deceptive theme has emerged at this weekend\u8217\'20\'19s rightwing gathering of the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/feb/25/donald-trump-cpac-republicans-allies"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Conservative Political Action Conference}}}\uc2  : Republicans as the true party of the blue-collar worker.\par \par \uc2 It was a concept promoted variously over CPAC\u8217\'20\'19s first two days by, among others, a multimillionaire former governor who made a fortune in healthcare; the son of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , who lives in his own exclusive Florida club; and two firebrand US senators with law degrees from Ivy League universities who oppose a universal hike in the minimum wage to $15 an hour.\par \par \uc2 One of them, the Texas senator Ted Cruz, earlier this month flew his family to a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/feb/19/ted-cruz-texas-outrage-cancun"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 sunshine vacation}}}\uc2  at a five-star resort in Mexico to escape the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/feb/20/texas-boy-dies-suspected-hypothermia"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 deadly winter blast}}}\uc2  back in his home state. At CPAC he asserted his alignment with America\u8217\'20\'19s working men and women.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe Republican party is not the party just of the country clubs; the Republican party is the party of steel workers and construction workers, and pipeline workers and taxi cab drivers, and cops and firefighters, and waiters and waitresses, and the men and women with calluses on their hands who are working for this country,\u8221\'20\'1D Cruz told the nation\u8217\'20\'19s biggest annual gathering of grassroots conservatives, just days after cutting short his Cancun holiday when the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/feb/23/ted-cruz-press-cancun-trip-texas-freeze"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 scandal came to light}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThat is our party, and these deplorables are here to stay.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The CPAC positioning to try to represent the Republican party as a champion of the working class comes as Democratic president \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s effort to raise the minimum wage {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/feb/27/us-minimum-wage-senate-explainer"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 faces significant congressional roadblocks}}}\uc2 , including opposition from many senior Republican figures.\par \par \uc2 Cruz, a Harvard-educated lawyer and the beneficiary of substantial corporate campaign donations, at least until many {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2021/01/11/business/corporate-donations-politics.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 halted contributions}}}\uc2  in the wake of the 6 January Capitol riots, is a long-time opponent of what he has called the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.msnbc.com/rachel-maddow-show/cruz-sees-the-minimum-wage-bad-policy-msna835396"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1Cbad policy\u8221\'20\'1D concept}}}\uc2  of a minimum wage, and has said legislation to enforce it would \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cruz.senate.gov/?p=press_release&id=1160"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 kill American jobs}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Josh Hawley\uc2 , the Missouri senator who last month joined his fellow Trump loyalist Cruz in attempting to block the certification of Biden\u8217\'20\'19s victory, was another prominent CPAC speaker espousing working-class roots while opposing the new president\u8217\'20\'19s wage proposals.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhere I come from in Missouri, I grew up in rural Missouri, [a] small town right in the middle of Missouri, it\u8217\'20\'19s a working-class town full of good folks, working hard to make it every day,\u8221\'20\'1D said Hawley, a Yale law school graduate.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAnd I can just tell you, where I grew up, we believe in citizenship because we\u8217\'20\'19re proud of it. We\u8217\'20\'19re proud to be Americans,\u8221\'20\'1D he added in an address {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.rev.com/blog/transcripts/josh-hawley-2021-cpac-speech-transcript-february-26"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 condemning \u8220\'20\'1Cpowerful corporations\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2  and \u8220\'20\'1Coligarchs\u8221\'20\'1D he accused of imposing a \u8220\'20\'1Cradical left agenda\u8221\'20\'1D on the United States.\par \par \uc2 Hawley, considered a possible candidate in the race for the Republican Party\u8217\'20\'19s 2024 presidential nomination if Trump does not run again, has also suffered {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.forbes.com/sites/jemimamcevoy/2021/01/11/hallmark-asks-republicans-involved-in-challenging-bidens-win-to-return-donations/?sh=252fdf6d57d8"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 corporate backlash}}}\uc2  for his support of the former president\u8217\'20\'19s election lies. He proposed legislation this month that would {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.hawley.senate.gov/hawley-announces-legislation-require-15-minimum-wage-billion-dollar-corporations"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 exempt small businesses}}}\uc2  from paying their employees a \u8220\'20\'1Cburdensome\u8221\'20\'1D minimum wage.\par \par \uc2 On Saturday at CPAC, the fealty continued to Trump, who was honored at the conference venue this week by the installation of a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/feb/26/trump-golden-statue-cpac-conference"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 large, gaudy statue}}}\uc2  that sparked the \uc2 Twitter\uc2  hashtag #goldencalf.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe blue-collar comeback was the theme of our administration,\u8221\'20\'1D the Republican Tennessee senator \uc2 Bill Hagerty\uc2  said in a panel discussion on industry during which he praised \u8220\'20\'1CPresident Trump\u8217\'20\'19s leadership\u8221\'20\'1D for job growth.\par \par \uc2 KT McFarland, a conservative commentator who was briefly Trump\u8217\'20\'19s deputy national security adviser at the start of his administration, said she had a telephone call with the former president on Friday night in which he allegedly outlined the theme of his scheduled CPAC speech on Sunday.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI think that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is not finished with this revolution,\u8221\'20\'1D she said, describing how she called his Mar-a-Lago resort in Palm Beach and claiming Trump himself picked up the phone.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHe said: \u8216\'20\'18I\u8217\'20\'19m going to talk about the future. I\u8217\'20\'19m going to talk about how we win in 2022, how we take the White House back in 2024.\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s son, Donald Jr, told CPAC attendees earlier in the gathering that Biden\u8217\'20\'19s relaxation of Trump-era immigration measures and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2021/feb/24/biden-is-locking-up-migrant-children-will-the-world-still-care-with-trump-gone"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reopening of camps for migrant youth}}}\uc2  would affect the very blue-collar workers Republicans are attempting to covet.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhere is the outrage about an asinine immigration policy that is encouraging people to bring children unaccompanied and otherwise into a country?\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CGuess who gets hurt? Our low-wage earners, who for the first time in modern history under \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  started seeing real wage growth.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Rick Scott\uc2 , Florida\u8217\'20\'19s junior senator and former governor, and a staunch Trump ally, cautioned Republicans that abandoning the ex-present would alienate the party\u8217\'20\'19s base.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe will not win the future by trying to go back to where the Republican party used to be. If we do, we will lose the working base that President Trump so animated,\u8221\'20\'1D said Scott, a former healthcare executive whose personal net worth has been estimated {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/states/florida/story/2018/07/27/federal-disclosure-scotts-net-worth-upwards-of-500m-533760"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 above half a million dollars}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re gonna lose elections across the country and ultimately we\u8217\'20\'19re gonna lose our nation.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Analysts say there is nothing unusual in Republicans courting the working vote, even if the choice of messenger might be questionable.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CFrom a scholarly perspective, we\u8217\'20\'19re really watching what seems to be a realignment of the coalitions that are supporting each party, and particularly among working-class white individuals,\u8221\'20\'1D said Dr Susan MacManus, emeritus professor of political science at the University of South Florida.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAll you have to do is to go look at the exit poll for the presidential election and look at who are the largest supporters of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , non-college educated, working whites, pretty much.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIs there a disconnect between the wealth and education of leaders in both parties? Yes, but this is where it\u8217\'20\'19s coming from.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020210227eh2r0025t\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
