\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Raising the US minimum wage: what just happened and what comes next?\b0\par\par\uc2 Ed Pilkington in New York \par \uc2 772 \uc2 words\par \uc2 27 February 2021\par 13:02 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2021.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 A Senate official has ruled that the plan for a $15 minimum cannot be passed with only a simple majority but the fight is far from over\par \par \uc2 It was a major plank of the Democratic plan to \u8220\'20\'1Cbuild back better\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 raising the federal minimum wage from $7.25 to $15 an hour as a way of boosting the economy during the pandemic and tackling poverty and income inequality. But on Thursday the much-vaunted plan hit a roadblock in the \uc2 US Senate\uc2 , which has knocked the proposal sideways.\par \par \uc2 So what happened, and is this game over for the $15 minimum wage?\par \par \uc2 What happened\par \par \uc2 ?\par \par \uc2 The idea of pushing up the minimum wage in stages to $15 in 2025 was included in \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s $1.9tn stimulus package that seeks to support vaccine distribution and an extension of unemployment benefit among other pandemic provisions.\par \par \uc2 The minimum wage element of the bill was a very big deal. It would increase the incomes of 27 million Americans, with almost 1 million people lifted out of poverty, according to the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cbo.gov/publication/56975"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Congressional Budget Office}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The Democrats have decided to fast-track the bill as a way of avoiding Republican opposition through a channel known as \u8220\'20\'1Cbudget resolution\u8221\'20\'1D. That would provide for a simple majority vote in the Senate, avoiding the dreaded filibuster where 60 votes have to be attained \u8211\'20\'13 an impossible task given Republican intransigence within the new evenly split 50-50 Senate.\par \par \uc2 The snag is that budget resolution is subject to strict limits on how it is applied, designed to prevent political leaders packing the bill with all sorts of goodies entirely unrelated to federal revenue or spending. The unelected keeper of those restrictions is Elizabeth MacDonough, the grandly titled {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2021/02/23/us/politics/stimulus-senate-parliamentarian.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Senate parliamentarian}}}\uc2 , who announced on Thursday that in her reading of the rules the $15 minimum wage was extraneous to budget legislation and thus had to be removed.\par \par \uc2 How did that go down?\par \par \uc2 Advocates of raising the minimum wage were incensed. Bernie Sanders, a longtime champion, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SenSanders/status/1365106926804156425"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  he strongly disagreed with the decision, which he blamed on \u8220\'20\'1Carchaic and undemocratic rules\u8221\'20\'1D. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SenWarren/status/1365101872294604800"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Elizabeth Warren}}}\uc2  and many {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/CoriBush/status/1365148181185654788"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 others}}}\uc2  said it was time to end the filibuster so that the provision could pass the Senate regardless, while the idea of firing MacDonough was also {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/nation/2021/02/26/senate-parliamentarian-minimum-wage-overrule/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 floated}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 By contrast, the top Republican on the Senate budget committee, \uc2 Lindsey Graham\uc2 , said he was \u8220\'20\'1Cvery pleased\u8221\'20\'1D by MacDonough\u8217\'20\'19s intervention.\par \par \uc2 Would it have passed in any case?\par \par \uc2 There were some doubts that the stimulus bill would have passed with the minimum wage increase contained in it. Two Democratic senators on the right of the party, \uc2 Joe Manchin\uc2  from West Virginia and Kyrsten Sinema from Arizona, had both put up resistance, and even Biden himself openly expressed {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2021/02/05/politics/biden-minimum-wage-covid-proposal/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 skepticism}}}\uc2  that the provision would \u8220\'20\'1Csurvive\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The irony is that a $15 minimum wage is hugely popular among Americans of all political persuasions, with two-thirds supporting it, according to a 2019 poll by the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.pewresearch.org/fact-tank/2019/07/30/two-thirds-of-americans-favor-raising-federal-minimum-wage-to-15-an-hour/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Pew Research Center}}}\uc2 . Take {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2020/nov/23/fight-for-15-minimum-wage-florida-biden"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Florida}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 the state voted for Trump in November, but it also backed by 60% a ballot initiative raising the minimum wage to $15 over the next five years.\par \par \uc2 So what\u8217\'20\'19s next?\par \par \uc2 There are several directions in which the tussle could now go. \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , as president of the Senate and the final arbiter on the chamber\u8217\'20\'19s rules, has the authority to overrule the parliamentarian. But such a power has not been wielded since {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://thehill.com/blogs/blog-briefing-room/news/81273-healthcare-reform-and-reconciliation-a-bad-mix-ex-parliamentarian-says"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Nelson Rockefeller}}}\uc2  in 1975, and, besides, the White House has indicated that the vice-president will not take that route.\par \par \uc2 An alternative \u8220\'20\'1Cplan B\u8221\'20\'1D is emerging whereby the Democrats would replace the minimum wage provision in the stimulus bill with a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://thehill.com/homenews/senate/540668-plan-b-for-15-minimum-wage-unveiled"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 tax penalty}}}\uc2  on large corporations paying workers less than $15 an hour. Democratic leaders think that such a tax mechanism might be more resilient in meeting the requirements of budget resolution.\par \par \uc2 Working against that will be the desire of the White House to pass the stimulus bill quickly and not experience any further delays. A crunch deadline is fast approaching \u8211\'20\'13 on 14 March the existing jobless benefits start to expire and the Biden administration is keen to prevent unemployed workers falling into even greater hardship.\par \par \uc2 Amid the plethora of possible next steps, one thing is certain: the fight for $15 is not over. In the past eight years the push for a decent minimum wage has snowballed across the US and around the world into a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/feb/13/fight-for-15-minimum-wage-workers-labor-rights"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 formidable movement}}}\uc2 , and no number of objections from unelected rules-keepers will hold it back for long.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020210227eh2r001ba\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
