\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 'We need $15': US minimum wage ruling a personal blow for millions of workers\b0\par\par\uc2 Michael Sainato \par \uc2 772 \uc2 words\par \uc2 26 February 2021\par 18:01 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2021.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Workers have criticized setback and are pushing elected officials to figure out a way to still pass a $15 federal minimum wage\par \par \uc2 Bill Thompson, 50, has worked in food service in Independence, Missouri, for over 30 years. He currently works at \uc2 Burger King\uc2 , making $10.30 an hour. With his current wages, he avoids seeking medical care because of the costs, and explained his family has struggled to afford basic necessities.\par \par \uc2 He\u8217\'20\'19s one of many low-wage workers around the US who have been organizing and fighting for a $15 minimum wage at the federal level and at local and state levels since the Fight for $15 and a Union movement {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/feb/13/fight-for-15-minimum-wage-workers-labor-rights"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 began}}}\uc2  in 2012.\par \par \uc2 In a setback for the movement, on 25 February the Senate parliamentarian {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/us-policy/2021/02/25/minimum-wage-increase-imperiled-covid-relief-bill-by-senate-officials-ruling/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ruled}}}\uc2  the minimum wage increase as written currently cannot remain in the coronavirus relief bill under Senate rules, and the White House {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/jeneps/status/1365098078529675264"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 noted}}}\uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , in her role presiding over the Senate, will not attempt to overrule the parliamentarian.\par \par \uc2 For Thompson \u8211\'20\'13 and millions of American workers like him \u8211\'20\'13 the news is a personal blow.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf we made $15 an hour, that would be a night and day difference. It doesn\u8217\'20\'19t mean I\u8217\'20\'19m going to have savings, it just means I\u8217\'20\'19m going to have more financial resources to afford to have food on the table and my drug prescriptions,\u8221\'20\'1D said Thompson. \u8220\'20\'1CI have to choose between going to the doctor and buying medicine or putting food on my table, or buying a new pair of shoes.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Democrats have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2021/02/20/politics/sanders-minimum-wage-covid-relief-package/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pushed}}}\uc2  to include a $15-an-hour federal minimum wage by 2025 in the coronavirus relief bill, though Joe Biden {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2021/02/18/biden-governors-minimum-wage-469898"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 expressed}}}\uc2  skepticism the $15 minimum wage will make it into the final coronavirus relief bill and noted he is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/us-policy/2021/02/16/covid-relief-biden/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 open to delaying}}}\uc2  the phased increase.\par \par \uc2 Workers have criticized the ruling and are pushing elected officials to figure out a way to still pass a $15 federal minimum wage.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe will not be deterred by an archaic Senate process that throughout history has been used to delay or deny progress for Black and brown communities while allowing multitrillion-dollar tax cuts for corporations,\u8221\'20\'1D said Maribel Cornejo, a \uc2 McDonald\u8217\'20\'19s\uc2  worker and Fight for $15 and a Union leader in Houston, Texas, in a statement.\par \par \uc2 Cornejo added: \u8220\'20\'1CWinning elections means talking to voters about the issues that matter to their lives and then delivering on those promises. Voters don\u8217\'20\'19t want to hear excuses about process, procedures or parliamentarians. We want a job that pays us a living wage. We want dignity at work. We want and we need $15.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Cynthia Murray, a \uc2 Walmart\uc2  associate for nearly 20 years and United for Respect leader in Maryland who testified in front of the Senate on 25 February, added: \u8220\'20\'1CWhen are they going to stand up and stand for the workers and change the minimum wage? It\u8217\'20\'19s been 12 years.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The president of SEIU International, the leading organization behind the Fight for $15 movement, \uc2 Mary Kay Henry\uc2 , argued the ruling was no excuse to delay increasing the minimum wage.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CEssential workers have put their lives on the line throughout the pandemic and now elected leaders must meet their demands to be respected, protected and paid,\u8221\'20\'1D Henry said in a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.seiu.org/2021/02/seius-henry-parliamentarian-ruling-no-excuse-to-delay-15"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 statement}}}\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CEvery single healthcare provider, fast-food worker, janitor, security officer and public servant who have kept our communities afloat for the past year needs real Covid relief that includes $15 \u8211\'20\'13 and Congress needs to get it done.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In response to the parliamentarian ruling, the Vermont senator Bernie Sanders {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SenSanders/status/1365106926804156425"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 announced}}}\uc2  his intention to include an amendment in the relief bill to take away tax deductions from large, profitable corporations that do not pay a $15 an hour minimum wage.\par \par \uc2 House Democratic leaders have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SpeakerPelosi/status/1365120843039277058"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 announced}}}\uc2  the $15 minimum wage bill will remain in the coronavirus relief package that is expected to pass today and be sent to the Senate.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.pewresearch.org/fact-tank/2019/07/30/two-thirds-of-americans-favor-raising-federal-minimum-wage-to-15-an-hour/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Two-thirds}}}\uc2  of Americans support a $15 minimum wage according to 2019 polls conducted by the \uc2 Pew Research Center\uc2 , and more recent surveys have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.brookings.edu/blog/the-avenue/2020/11/13/even-a-divided-america-agrees-on-raising-the-minimum-wage/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 shown seven in 10 Americans}}}\uc2  support raising the minimum wage.\par \par \uc2 Republicans and business industry groups have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonexaminer.com/opinion/a-15-minimum-wage-would-hurt-workers-and-small-businesses#:~:text=A%20minimum%20wage%20hike%20would,tipped%20minimum%20wage%20for%20servers."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 argued}}}\uc2  increases to minimum wage results in job losses and hurts small businesses, but data over 22 previous federal minimum wage increases since 1938 show there is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nelp.org/wp-content/uploads/NELP-Data-Brief-Raise-Wages-Kill-Jobs-No-Correlation.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 no correlation}}}\uc2  between minimum wage increases and job losses. Raising the federal minimum wage to $15 an hour by 2026 would provide a raise to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.epi.org/press/epi-applauds-the-introduction-of-the-raise-the-wage-act-32-million-u-s-workers-would-benefit-from-a-15-federal-minimum-wage/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 32 million workers}}}\uc2  who otherwise {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnbc.com/2021/02/21/15-minimum-wage-wont-cover-living-costs-for-many-americans.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 struggle to meet basic living expenses.}}}\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020210226eh2q002gx\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
