\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Ilhan Omar leads calls to fire Senate official who scuppered $15 wage rise\b0\par\par\uc2 Dominic Rushe \par \uc2 560 \uc2 words\par \uc2 26 February 2021\par 14:51 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2021.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Parliamentarian Elizabeth MacDonough ruled provision in $1.9tn Covid stimulus bill did not qualify for budget reconciliation\par \par \uc2 The progressive Democrat \uc2 Ilhan Omar\uc2  has called for the firing of the government official who effectively blocked the party\u8217\'20\'19s plans to raise the minimum wage.\par \par \uc2 Democratic plans to include a gradual raise to $15 in \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s $1.9tn coronavirus stimulus bill were effectively ended on Thursday when the Senate parliamentarian ruled it should not be part of the package.\par \par \uc2 The decision by Elizabeth MacDonough, who has held the nonpartisan position since 2012, dashed hopes of including the raise in the bill \u8211\'20\'13 the first increase in over a decade.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAbolish the filibuster. Replace the parliamentarian,\u8221\'20\'1D Omar {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/IlhanMN/status/1365113547848634370?s=20"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said in a tweet}}}\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CWhat\u8217\'20\'19s a Democratic majority if we can\u8217\'20\'19t pass our priority bills? This is unacceptable.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Abolish the filibuster.\par \par \uc2 Replace the parliamentarian.\par \par \uc2 What\u8217\'20\'19s a Democratic majority if we can\u8217\'20\'19t pass our priority bills? This is unacceptable.\u8212\'20\'14 Ilhan Omar (@IlhanMN) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/IlhanMN/status/1365113547848634370?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 February 26, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 Biden campaigned on a pledge to increase the minimum wage to $15. Low-wage workers and unions have campaigned for a rise since 2012, and its inclusion in the coronavirus stimulus bill had been seen as a major victory.\par \par \uc2 While the proposal faced universal opposition by Republican senators and skepticism from some Democrats, senator Bernie Sanders and others were confident that it could be pushed through with a simple majority in the Senate, where the Democrats hold a slim majority.\par \par \uc2 In order to achieve this, the proposal would have to be passed by \u8220\'20\'1Cbudget reconciliation\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 a mechanism that allows legislation to bypass the 60% vote bills need to get through the Senate.\par \par \uc2 Late on Thursday, MacDonough ruled that the wage increase did not meet the standards for budget reconciliation.\par \par \uc2 The parliamentarian acts as an impartial judge and has only been removed from office once. MacDonough is well respected by many members of both parties, and the Biden administration seems unlikely to push for her removal.\par \par \uc2 Other progressive Democrats have proposed a less drastic solution \u8211\'20\'13 overruling her.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe Senate parliamentarian issues an advisory opinion,\u8221\'20\'1D congresswoman \uc2 Pramila Jayapal{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/PramilaJayapal/status/1365071827920441345?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw%7Ctwcamp%5Etweetembed%7Ctwterm%5E1365071827920441345%7Ctwgr%5E%7Ctwcon%5Es1_&ref_url=about%3Asrcdoc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said in a tweet}}}\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CThe VP can overrule them \u8211\'20\'13 as has been done before. We should do EVERYTHING we can to keep our promise, deliver a $15 minimum wage, and give 27 million workers a raise.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Sanders, one of the most ardent supporters of a minimum-wage increase, has proposed an alternative plan \u8211\'20\'13 imposing penalties and incentives to push companies toward higher wages.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI will be working with my colleagues in the Senate to move forward with an amendment to take tax deductions away from large, profitable corporations that don\u8217\'20\'19t pay workers at least $15 an hour, and to provide small businesses with the incentives they need to raise wages,\u8221\'20\'1D Sanders {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SenSanders/status/1365106926804156425?s=20"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said in a statement}}}\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CThat amendment must be included in this reconciliation bill.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Sanders\u8217\'20\'19 comments come after a Senate hearing on Thursday where he {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/feb/25/bernie-sanders-mcdonalds-walmart-workers-congress-minimum-wage"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 lambasted the low wages }}}\uc2  paid by \uc2 McDonald\u8217\'20\'19s\uc2 , \uc2 Walmart\uc2  and others. Sanders pointed to a government report that found nearly half of workers who make less than $15 an hour rely on public assistance programs that cost taxpayers $107bn each year.\par \par \uc2 The American people are \u8220\'20\'1Csick and tired\u8221\'20\'1D of subsidizing \u8220\'20\'1Cstarvation wages\u8221\'20\'1D at these companies, Sanders said.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020210226eh2q00232\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
