\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Republicans unveil two minimum wage bills in response to Democrats' push\b0\par\par\uc2 Lauren Aratani \par \uc2 708 \uc2 words\par \uc2 26 February 2021\par 10:02 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2021.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Senators \uc2 Mitt Romney\uc2  and Tom Cotton set $10-an-hour target while \uc2 Josh Hawley\uc2  promotes tax credit scheme\par \par \uc2 Republican lawmakers have been vocal about their opposition to \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s coronavirus relief bill, particularly to Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 inclusion of a provision that would raise the federal minimum wage from $7.25 an hour to $15 an hour.\par \par \uc2 But two sets of Republicans from opposite sides of the party have now introduced bills that show what they believe are more palatable policies that address criticism of America\u8217\'20\'19s current minimum wage.\par \par \uc2 The moves come amid a major push by leftwing Democrats, unions and progressive pressure groups to raise the minimum wage \u8211\'20\'13 a push that appears to have a higher chance of success than ever before. The campaign \u8211\'20\'13 often spearheaded by walkout worker protests \u8211\'20\'13 has put pressure on the Republican party to respond.\par \par \uc2 In keeping with the party\u8217\'20\'19s deep division between its dominant Trumpist faction and its more traditionalist party elites, the twin responses seem aimed at appealing on one hand to its corporate-friendly allies and on the other hand to its populist rightwing base. Both have an anti-immigrant element.\par \par \uc2 Senators \uc2 Mitt Romney\uc2  and Tom Cotton unveiled on Tuesday a proposal for a $10 federal minimum wage, to be implemented over the course of four years with a slower, phased approach for small businesses. Their bill also requires employers to use the federal government\u8217\'20\'19s E-Verify program to ensure they are not hiring undocumented workers.\par \par \uc2 Currently, 29 states, including Arkansas, Cotton\u8217\'20\'19s home state, have minimum wages above the federal level. A few states have already passed a $15 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ncsl.org/research/labor-and-employment/state-minimum-wage-chart.aspx#:~:text=Saige%20Draeger-,Summary,wage%20below%20%247.25%20per%20hour."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 minimum wage}}}\uc2 , including California, Massachusetts and Colorado.\par \par \uc2 In a statement about the bill, Cotton railed against \u8220\'20\'1Cmillions of illegal immigrants\u8221\'20\'1D who compete with American workers \u8220\'20\'1Cfor too few jobs with wages that are too low\u8221\'20\'1D. Meanwhile, Romney said the legislation \u8220\'20\'1Cwould raise the floor for workers without costing jobs\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 While immigration has largely been left out of the debate over a $15 minimum wage, Republicans when arguing against the wage hike have cited a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cbo.gov/publication/56975"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 report}}}\uc2  from the \uc2 Congressional Budget Office\uc2  that 1.4m jobs could be lost with the increase.\par \par \uc2 The same report also says that 17 million workers would see increases in their wages and 900,000 Americans could be lifted out of poverty with the policy. Romney and Cotton\u8217\'20\'19s plan would affect the wages of 3.5 million workers, according to a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.romney.senate.gov/sites/default/files/2021-02/higher%20wages%20for%20american%20workers%20act_one%20pager.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 fact sheet}}}\uc2  by Romney\u8217\'20\'19s office.\par \par \uc2 Subtly referring to the bill on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/AOC/status/1364301601486364678?s=20"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Twitter}}}\uc2 , the Democratic representative Alexandria Ocasio-Cortez called a $10 minimum wage \u8220\'20\'1Clegislated poverty\u8221\'20\'1D on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the far-right Republican senator \uc2 Josh Hawley\uc2  of Missouri released his alternative to an increase in the minimum wage: a tax credit for those who make less than $16.50 an hour. The credit would be applied based on the number of hours a person worked and would be available only to those with an American social security number, barring non-US citizens and undocumented workers. A full-time worker could get up to $4,680 in tax credits a year, according to the bill.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s time we give blue-collar workers some respect and a pay raise. This plan would deliver meaningful relief for families and working Americans through higher pay while incentivizing and promoting work,\u8221\'20\'1D Hawley said in a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.hawley.senate.gov/senator-hawley-announces-blue-collar-bonus-pay-raise-american-workers"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 statement}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 According to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.axios.com/hawley-minimum-wage-tax-credits-2087ac1e-a007-4095-b2b8-c0aa6d202dc2.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Axios}}}\uc2 , Hawley\u8217\'20\'19s team estimated his plan would cost the government $200bn, a figure traditional Republicans would eschew. Hawley has also split off from traditional Republicans by saying on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/HawleyMO/status/1364331554277883904"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Twitter}}}\uc2  he would support a $15 minimum wage for workers of big corporations that make at least $1bn in annual revenue.\par \par \uc2 The two bills have little chance of getting any serious consideration as Democrats are focused on internal debates over their $15 minimum wage proposal. Two of the more conservative members of the party, Joe Manchin of West Virginia and Kyrsten Sinema of Arizona, indicated that they will not support the bill if it includes the wage hike.\par \par \uc2 Manchin {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/feb/22/us-15-dollar-minimum-wage-joe-manchin-west-virginia"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  that he would support an $11 minimum wage, telling reporters that \u8220\'20\'1Cthrowing $15 out there right now just makes it very difficult in rural America\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020210226eh2q001e7\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
