\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Biden warns Americans 'this is not the time to relax' as vaccinations ramp up \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Maanvi Singh, Joan E Greve and Martin Belam \par \uc2 14,449 \uc2 words\par \uc2 26 February 2021\par 01:26 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2021.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Millions of pages of documents receivedHouse holds hearing on Capitol riot security failuresFauci urges \u8216\'20\'18if a vaccine is available, regardless of which one, take it\u8217\'20\'19Jennifer Granholm confirmed as energy secretarySign up to receive First Thing \u8211\'20\'13 our daily briefing by email\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.00am GMT\par \par \uc2 Summary\par \par \uc2 From Joan E Greve and me:\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  celebrated the distribution of 50m coronavirus vaccine doses since he took office last month. At an event this afternoon, the president emphasized Americans must remain vigilant about limiting their risk of contracting coronavirus. \u8220\'20\'1CThis is not the time to relax,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said. \u8220\'20\'1CThe worst thing we can do now is let our guard down.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 * The \uc2 US Food and Drug Administration\uc2  today announced that the \uc2 Pfizer\uc2 -BioNTech vaccine could be stored and transported at conventional freezer temperatures, rather than the ultra-cold temps that were initially recommended. \uc2 Pfizer\uc2  submitted data showing that the vaccine stays stable at regular freezer temperatures last week. The new \uc2 FDA\uc2  rules will make it easier for states to move and distribute the vaccine without the need for specialized cold storage equipment.\par \par \uc2 * The Senate parliamentarian has ruled that the minimum wage increase cannot be included with the coronavirus relief bill if it is to pass through the fillibuster-free reconciliation process. The prospect of increasing the minimum wage to $15 per hour has faced stiff opposition from Republicans.\par \par \uc2 * The House passed the Equality Act in a vote of 224 to 206. The legislation, which would prohibit discrimination on the basis of someone\u8217\'20\'19s sexual orientation or gender identity, faces an uncertain future in the evenly divided Senate.\par \par \uc2 * Biden spoke to Saudi Arabia\u8217\'20\'19s King Salman today, the White House announced moments ago. The call comes as the \uc2 US government\uc2  prepares to release an unclassified report on the murder of journalist Jamal Khashoggi, which has been blamed on the Saudi crown prince, \uc2 Mohammed bin Salman\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 * The Manhattan district attorney\u8217\'20\'19s office has obtained \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s financial records. The news comes three days after the supreme court rejected Trump\u8217\'20\'19s request to block Cy Vance \u8217\'20\'19s office from gaining access to the records as part of an investigation into the former president\u8217\'20\'19s business dealings.\par \par \uc2 * The Senate confirmed \uc2 Jennifer Granholm\uc2  as the next secretary of energy. Granholm, a former governor of Michigan, was confirmed in a vote of 64 to 35. She is expected to play a major role in Biden\u8217\'20\'19s promises to expand renewable energy sources.\par \par \uc2 * The House held a hearing on the security failures that occurred during the Capitol insurrection. Members of a House appropriations subcommittee pressed the acting chief of the the \uc2 US Capitol Police\uc2 , Yogananda Pittman, and the acting House sergeant at arms, Timothy Blodgett, on the insufficient preparation for the attack, despite many warning signs that Trump supporters could turn violent.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.25am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.38am GMT\par \par \uc2 Senate parliamentarian rules that the minimum wage hike may not pass with simple majority\par \par \uc2 The Senate parliamentarian has ruled that the minimum wage increase cannot be included with the coronavirus relief bill if it is to pass through the fillibuster-free reconciliation process.\par \par \uc2 enltrThe Senate parliamentarian has ruled that the minimum wage will not be included in the covid bill. I\u8217\'20\'19m already working on a bipartisan solution that can pass through Congress, ensure livable wages, job growth, and thriving small businesses. Got an idea? Please share it with me. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/iBpXPVP6tI"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/iBpXPVP6tI}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Rep. Dean Phillips\uc2  ???? (@RepDeanPhillips) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RepDeanPhillips/status/1365096321607229441?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 February 26, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 The prospect of increasing the minimum wage to $15 per hour has faced stiff opposition from Republicans. Most bills in the Senate need to get 60-vote supermajority support in order to overcome the filibuster. But some budget-related legislation, including the bulk of the relief bill, can be passed with just 51 votes through a process called reconciliation.\par \par \uc2 But a hike to the minimum wage does not qualify to pass through reconciliation, the parliamentarian ruled. Democrats hopes of squeezing through a minimum wage increase with a simple majority vote have been dashed.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.26am GMT\par \par \uc2 What the arrests of Beverly Hills residents say about the US Capitol attack\par \par \uc2 Beverly Hills has seen more residents arrested for participating in the US Capitol insurrection than any other city in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/california"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 California}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Three of the 14 California residents charged in connection with the pro-Trump riot in Washington on 6 January so far are from the wealthy Los Angeles county enclave: Gina Bisignano, a salon owner, and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/jan/22/coronavirus-misinformation-simone-gold-americas-frontline-doctors"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Simone Gold and John Strand}}}\uc2 , two rightwing activists who have spread coronavirus misinformation through their roles in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/jan/22/coronavirus-misinformation-simone-gold-americas-frontline-doctors"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 America\u8217\'20\'19s Frontline Doctors}}}\uc2 , an organization that Gold, an emergency room physician, founded.\par \par \uc2 The 11 other Californians who have been charged in the riot are scattered across the state, from San Diego to San Francisco, with three clustered in towns around Sacramento, the state capital, and two from towns in the notoriously conservative Orange county, south of Los Angeles.\par \par \uc2 The prominence of Beverly Hills and the profile of the three residents who have been charged reflects what experts say are broader trends in the backgrounds of the more than 250 people charged so far in connection with the Capitol riot.\par \par \uc2 More than 90% of the people charged in the riots so far are white, researchers at the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://d3qi0qp55mx5f5.cloudfront.net/cpost/i/docs/americas_insurrectionists_online_2021_02_05.pdf?mtime=1612585947"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Chicago Project on Security and Threats }}}\uc2  found. About 40% are business owners or have white-collar jobs, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://d3qi0qp55mx5f5.cloudfront.net/cpost/i/docs/americas_insurrectionists_online_2021_02_05.pdf?mtime=1612585947"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the researchers found}}}\uc2 , and compared with previous rightwing extremists, relatively few of them were unemployed.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere\u8217\'20\'19s been this assumption that the most reactionary folks on the frontlines would be what\u8217\'20\'19s often referred to as white working-class, but that\u8217\'20\'19s of course not what we saw,\u8221\'20\'1D said Vanessa Wills, a political philosopher who studies the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://nplusonemag.com/online-only/online-only/from-the-lockdown-protests-to-the-capitol/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 intersections of race and class}}}\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CThe people who showed up are disproportionately small business owners.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The people charged in the attack so far also did not come exclusively from Republican states or conservative enclaves. In fact, a majority lived in counties that Biden won, like Beverly Hills, nestled next to Hollywood in liberal Los Angeles county.\par \par \uc2 Only 10% of the people charged so far had identifiable ties to rightwing militias or other organized violent groups, the Chicago researchers found. Many more were people who had identified as mainstream Trump supporters.\par \par \uc2 Read more:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/feb/25/beverly-hills-arrests-us-capitol-attack"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 What the arrests of Beverly Hills residents say about the US Capitol attack}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.02am GMT\par \par \uc2 FDA\uc2  allows \uc2 Pfizer\uc2  vaccine to be stored and transported at normal freezer temps\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 US Food and Drug Administration\uc2  today announced that the \uc2 Pfizer\uc2 -BioNTech vaccine could be stored and transported at conventional freezer temperatures, rather than the ultra-cold temps of -80C to -60C that was initially recommended.\par \par \uc2 Pfizer\uc2  submitted data showing that the vaccine stays stable at regular freezer temperatures last week. The new \uc2 FDA\uc2  rules will make it easier for states to move and distribute the vaccine without the need for specialized cold storage equipment.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis alternative temperature for transportation and storage of the undiluted vials is significant and allows the vials to be transported and stored under more flexible conditions,\u8221\'20\'1D said Peter Marks, director FDA\u8217\'20\'19s Center for Biologics Evaluation and Research, in a statement.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.47pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The US has reportedly carried out an airstrike in Syria, Reuters reports.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://news.trust.org/item/20210225222527-e5w1r/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 From Reuters: }}}\par \par \uc2 The United States on Thursday carried out an airstrike in Syria against a structure belonging to what it said were Iran-backed militia, two officials told Reuters.\par \par \uc2 The strike comes after a series of recent rocket attacks against U.S. targets in Iraq.\par \par \uc2 The officials, speaking on the condition of anonymity, said the strike was approved by President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2  has not confirmed this reporting.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.43pm GMT\par \par \uc2 On Fox News, \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2  evaded questions about \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 but said he\u8217\'20\'19d \u8220\'20\'1Cabsolutely\u8221\'20\'1D support the former president if Trump were the party\u8217\'20\'19s presidential nominee in 2024.\par \par \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18There\u8217\'20\'19s a lot to happen between now and \u8216\'20\'1824,\u8221\'20\'1D he added, noting that at least four Senate Republicans were vying for the nomination. McConnell voted to acquit Trump on the charge of inciting the Capitol attack but nevertheless said that the former president was \u8220\'20\'1Cpractically and morally responsible\u8221\'20\'1D for the deadly riot, and hinted that Trump\u8217\'20\'19s actions should be open to criminal prosecution.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more on McConnell\u8217\'20\'19s contradictory statements on Trump following the impeachment trial:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/feb/13/mitch-mcconnell-trump-republicans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Mitch McConnell savages Trump \u8211\'20\'13 minutes after voting to acquit}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.43pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.26pm GMT\par \par \uc2 What we know about the California coronavirus variant\par \par \uc2 Two new studies suggest that a Covid-19 variant first discovered in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/california"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 California}}}\uc2  has been spreading rapidly through the state.\par \par \uc2 The findings come as the US ramps up its efforts to track and catalogue various forms of the mutating virus, and raise fresh questions about the circulation of the coronavirus in the country.\par \par \uc2 What is the California variant?\par \par \uc2 The variant, which is called B.1.427/B.1.429, first caught the attention of scientists in November 2020 and belongs to a lineage \u8211\'20\'13 a branch of the coronavirus family tree carrying similar mutations \u8211\'20\'13 that is thought to have emerged in May.\par \par \uc2 The variant has been detected in 19 countries, and all across the US, though limited {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://outbreak.info/situation-reports?country=United%20States&division=California&pango=B.1.429&selected=California&selectedType=division"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 surveillance}}}\uc2  has found it concentrated in California.\par \par \uc2 The variant has three mutations that alter the shape of a protein, called spike, on the surface of the coronavirus. Other variants, including the ones first discovered in the UK, South Africa, and Brazil, also have mutations on their spike proteins. Researchers are concerned that these changes could make it harder for the immune system to quickly recognize and block the virus.\par \par \uc2 Why are we talking about it now?\par \par \uc2 Scientists around the world have been tracking Covid-19 variants by scanning samples taken from people infected with the virus. The US has been {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/feb/02/us-covid-variants-tracking-cdc-research"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  lagging behind other countries}}}\uc2  in doing this kind of monitoring \u8211\'20\'13 and still is. But some labs, including at the \uc2 University of San Francisco\uc2 , California, have recently redoubled efforts to figure out which variants are most common in the state.\par \par \uc2 While looking through samples from positive coronavirus tests to see if B.1.1.7 \u8211\'20\'13 the variant first detected in the UK \u8211\'20\'13 was circulating in the state, the USCF researchers realized that a different, homegrown variant actually accounted for a growing proportion of infections. Another team in Los Angeles found that that variant was spreading there as well.\par \par \uc2 Read more about the latest research, and what it all means, here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/feb/25/california-coronavirus-variant-covid-vaccine"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 What we know about the California coronavirus variant}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.54pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  spoke at the National Governor\u8217\'20\'19s Association meeting.\par \par \uc2 US President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  speaks during a virtual \uc2 National Governors Association\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Winter Meeting. Photograph: Saul Loeb/AFP/Getty Images\par \par \uc2 Governor \uc2 Andrew Cuomo\uc2  of New York spoke prior to Biden, welcoming the president to the Zoom meeting. Cuomo, who has been under fire for excluding thousands from the state\u8217\'20\'19s nursing home death toll, said to Biden: \u8220\'20\'1CYou reached out to us right after your election... Your promise of an ongoing functional partnership has already come to fruition.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe understand the difficult situation you inherited upon taking office,\u8221\'20\'1D he continued. \u8220\'20\'1CWhen you went to the cupboard, it was all but bare.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Biden\u8217\'20\'19s remarks focused on the monumental task of distributing vaccines and coordinating an economic recovery plan.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis cruel winter is not over,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden told the governors in attendance. But he signaled that \u8220\'20\'1Ca hopeful spring\u8221\'20\'1D was coming.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe need to be more ambitious right now,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said of his Covid-19 relief plans. \u8220\'20\'1CRed state, blue state, millions of Americans are hurting badly.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The president has been working closely with governors of both major parties \u8211\'20\'13 with a special focus on Republicans \u8211\'20\'13 to raise political support for recovery plans. Facing resistance from Republicans in the Senate and Congress, Biden has focused on courting governors in hopes they might pressure national representatives from their states to help secure much-needed economic relief.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.51pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Outrage as \uc2 Marjorie Taylor Greene\uc2  displays transphobic sign in Congress\par \par \uc2 The Republican extremist congresswoman {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/feb/06/who-is-marjorie-taylor-greene-republican-qanon"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Marjorie Taylor Greene}}}\uc2  attracted widespread condemnation \u8211\'20\'13 from transgender groups, Democrats and her own party \u8211\'20\'13 after she hung a transphobic sign outside her office in response to fellow congresswoman Marie Newman raising a transgender pride flag.\par \par \uc2 The Georgia congresswoman put up the poster \u8211\'20\'13 which read \u8220\'20\'1CThere are TWO genders: Male & Female. Trust The Science!\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 after Newman, whose daughter is transgender and whose office is opposite Greene\u8217\'20\'19s, hung the flag on Wednesday following an impassioned debate on the Equality Act, which Greene tried to block.\par \par \uc2 She has also called the bill \u8220\'20\'1Can attack on God\u8217\'20\'19s creation\u8221\'20\'1D and refused to refer to Newman\u8217\'20\'19s daughter as female.\par \par \uc2 Despite Greene\u8217\'20\'19s attempts to delay a vote on the legislation, which would extend civil rights protections to LGBTQ+ people, it is expected to pass in the House, after which it will move on to the Senate, where it could face a filibuster. \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has said if it passes he will sign it into law.\par \par \uc2 Speaking on the House floor this week, Newman, who represents Illinois, said: \u8220\'20\'1CThe best time to pass this act was decades ago. The second best time is right now. I\u8217\'20\'19m voting yes on the Equality Act for Evie Newman, my daughter and the strongest, bravest person I know.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 After the debate, Newman {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RepMarieNewman/status/1364658561809346564"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 tweeted}}}\uc2  a video of herself putting out the flag. She wrote: \u8220\'20\'1COur neighbour, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RepMTG"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @RepMTG}}}\uc2 , tried to block the Equality Act because she believes prohibiting discrimination against trans Americans is \u8216\'20\'18disgusting, immoral, and evil\u8217\'20\'19. Thought we\u8217\'20\'19d put up our Transgender flag so she can look at it every time she opens her door.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Greene, who has a history of supporting dangerous conspiracy theories, including QAnon, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RepMTG/status/1364719403498164226"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 wrote}}}\uc2  in response: \u8220\'20\'1COur neighbour, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RepMarieNewman"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @RepMarieNewman}}}\uc2 , wants to pass the so-called \u8216\'20\'18Equality\u8217\'20\'19 Act to destroy women\u8217\'20\'19s rights and religious freedoms. Thought we\u8217\'20\'19d put up ours so she can look at it every time she opens her door.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The incident was widely condemned, with the Illinois Democrat Sean Casten branding the poster \u8220\'20\'1Csickening, pathetic, unimaginably cruel\u8221\'20\'1D. He {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RepCasten/status/1364777447745597443?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw%7Ctwcamp%5Etweetembed%7Ctwterm%5E1364777447745597443%7Ctwgr%5E%7Ctwcon%5Es1_&ref_url=about%3Asrcdoc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 added}}}\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1CThis hate is exactly why the #EqualityAct is necessary.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Read more:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/feb/25/marjorie-taylor-greene-transgender-sign"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Outrage as Marjorie Taylor Greene displays transphobic sign in Congress}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.01pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.14pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Bernie Sanders: US sick of subsidizing 'starvation wages' at \uc2 Walmart\uc2  and \uc2 McDonald's\par \par \uc2 US taxpayers should not be \u8220\'20\'1Cforced to subsidize some of the largest and most profitable corporations in America\u8221\'20\'1D, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/bernie-sanders"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Bernie Sanders}}}\uc2  told a Senate hearing on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 As Congress debates the first rise in the minimum wage in over a decade, the Vermont senator said he had \u8220\'20\'1Ctalked to too many workers in this country who, with tears in their eyes, tell me the struggles they have to provide for their kids on starvation wages\u8221\'20\'1D even as the chief executives of companies including \uc2 McDonald\u8217\'20\'19s\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/wal-mart"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Walmart}}}\uc2  and others take home multi-million dollar pay packages.\par \par \uc2 Executives from \uc2 Walmart\uc2  and \uc2 McDonald\u8217\'20\'19s\uc2  were invited to the hearing, titled Should Taxpayers Subsidize Poverty Wages at Large Profitable Corporations?They declined to appear.\par \par \uc2 The senators heard from low-wage workers from \uc2 McDonald\u8217\'20\'19s\uc2  and \uc2 Walmart\uc2 . Terence Wise, a \uc2 McDonald\u8217\'20\'19s\uc2  employee from Kansas City, Missouri, said his low pay had led to his family becoming homeless.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMy family has been homeless despite two incomes. We\u8217\'20\'19ve endured freezing temperatures in our purple minivan. I\u8217\'20\'19d see my daughter\u8217\'20\'19s eyes wide open, tossing and turning, in the back seat. Try waking up in the morning and getting ready for work and school in a parking lot with your family of five,\u8221\'20\'1D said Wise.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThat\u8217\'20\'19s something a parent can never forget and a memory you can never take away from your children. You should never have multiple jobs in the United States and nowhere to sleep.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Read more:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/feb/25/bernie-sanders-mcdonalds-walmart-workers-congress-minimum-wage"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Bernie Sanders: US sick of subsidizing 'starvation wages' at Walmart and McDonald's}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.00pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Today so far\par \par \uc2 That\u8217\'20\'19s it from me today. My west coast colleague, Maanvi Singh, will take over the blog for the next few hours.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s where the day stands so far:\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  celebrated the distribution of 50 million coronavirus vaccine doses since he took office last month. At an event this afternoon, the president emphasized Americans must remain vigilant about limiting their risk of contracting coronavirus. \u8220\'20\'1CThis is not the time to relax,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said. \u8220\'20\'1CThe worst thing we can do now is let our guard down.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 * The House passed the Equality Act in a vote of 224 to 206. The legislation, which would prohibit discrimination on the basis of someone\u8217\'20\'19s sexual orientation or gender identity, faces an uncertain future in the evenly divided Senate.\par \par \uc2 * Biden spoke to Saudi Arabia\u8217\'20\'19s King Salman today, the White House announced moments ago. The call comes as the \uc2 US government\uc2  prepares to release an unclassified report on the murder of journalist Jamal Khashoggi, which has been blamed on the Saudi crown prince, \uc2 Mohammed bin Salman\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 * The Manhattan district attorney\u8217\'20\'19s office has obtained \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s financial records. The news comes three days after the supreme court rejected Trump\u8217\'20\'19s request to block Cy Vance \u8217\'20\'19s office from gaining access to the records as part of an investigation into the former president\u8217\'20\'19s business dealings.\par \par \uc2 * The Senate confirmed \uc2 Jennifer Granholm\uc2  as the next secretary of energy. Granholm, a former governor of Michigan, was confirmed in a vote of 64 to 35. She is expected to play a major role in Biden\u8217\'20\'19s promises to expand renewable energy sources.\par \par \uc2 * The House held a hearing on the security failures that occurred during the Capitol insurrection. Members of a House appropriations subcommittee pressed the acting chief of the the \uc2 US Capitol Police\uc2 , Yogananda Pittman, and the acting House sergeant at arms, Timothy Blodgett, on the insufficient preparation for the attack, despite many warning signs that Trump supporters could turn violent.\par \par \uc2 Maanvi will have more coming up, so stay tuned.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.58pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Biden speaks with Saudi Arabia's King Salman\par \par \uc2 President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  spoke to Saudi Arabia\u8217\'20\'19s King Salman today, the White House just announced.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CTogether they discussed regional security, including the renewed diplomatic efforts led by the United Nations and the United States to end the war in Yemen, and the U.S. commitment to help Saudi Arabia defend its territory as it faces attacks from Iranian-aligned groups,\u8221\'20\'1D the White House said in a readout of the call.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe President noted positively the recent release of several Saudi-American activists and Ms. Loujain al-Hathloul from custody, and affirmed the importance the United States places on universal human rights and the rule of law. The President told King Salman he would work to make the bilateral relationship as strong and transparent as possible. The two leaders affirmed the historic nature of the relationship and agreed to work together on mutual issues of concern and interest.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The call comes as the \uc2 US government\uc2  prepares to release an unclassified report on the murder of journalist Jamal Khashoggi, which has been blamed on the Saudi crown prince, \uc2 Mohammed bin Salman\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/feb/24/jamal-khashoggi-murder-us-report-saudi-arabia-mbs-king-salman-complicit"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Saudi heir complicit in Khashoggi murder, US assessment reportedly finds}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.42pm GMT\par \par \uc2 House passes Equality Act in nearly party-line vote\par \par \uc2 The House has passed the Equality Act in a vote of 224 to 206, with three Republicans joining all Democrats in supporting the bill.\par \par \uc2 Republicans \uc2 Brian Fitzpatrick\uc2 , \uc2 John Katko\uc2  and \uc2 Tom Reed\uc2  broke with their party to vote in favor of the legislation.\par \par \uc2 enltrH.R. 5 - Equality Act passed by a vote of 224-206.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 House Press Gallery (@HouseDailyPress) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/HouseDailyPress/status/1365051536653639683?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 February 25, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 If enacted, the Equality Act would prohibit discrimination on the basis of sexual orientation or gender identity.\par \par \uc2 But the bill faces an uncertain future in the evenly divided Senate, where Democrats will need 60 votes to break a filibuster on the legislation.\par \par \uc2 President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has already said he would sign the Equality Act if it can make it through the Senate. \u8220\'20\'1CEvery person should be treated with dignity and respect, and this bill represents a critical step toward ensuring that America lives up to our foundational values of equality and freedom for all,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said in a statement last week.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.48pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.27pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Trans doctor Rachel Levine testifies in historic Senate confirmation hearing\par \par \uc2 Dr Rachel Levine, a pediatrician and health official from Pennsylvania, faced a Senate confirmation hearing on Thursday as \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s nominee for assistant health secretary. The process could see her become the first openly transgender federal official to be confirmed by the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/us-senate"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US Senate}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 If confirmed, Levine, 63, would make history and break several glass ceilings. In a country which still only has a handful of openly trans public officials, she would be the most high-profile, occupying a senior position in the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/biden-administration"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Biden administration}}}\uc2  with major responsibilities in the pandemic response.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/feb/25/sgender-assistant-health-secretary"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Announcing}}}\uc2  her nomination last month, Biden said Levine would bring \u8220\'20\'1Csteady leadership and essential expertise we need to get through this pandemic \u8230\'20\'26 She is a historic and deeply qualified choice to help lead our administration\u8217\'20\'19s health efforts.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 As the confirmation hearing got under way on Thursday Levine faced hostile questioning from some of the Republican members of the Senate. \uc2 Rand Paul\uc2 , senator from Kentucky, compared transgender surgery misleadingly to genital mutilation and accused Levine of supporting \u8220\'20\'1Csurgical destruction of a minor\u8217\'20\'19s genitalia\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Levine replied by saying that transgender medicine was very complex. \u8220\'20\'1CIf I am fortunate enough to be confirmed, I will look forward to working with you and your office on the standards of care\u8221\'20\'1D in this field, she said.\par \par \uc2 Paul was rebuked by the chair of the committee, \uc2 Patty Murray\uc2 , for his \u8220\'20\'1Charmful misrepresentations\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/feb/25/rachel-levine-assistant-health-secretary-senate-confirmation-hearing-historic"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trans doctor Rachel Levine faces historic Senate confirmation hearing}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.02pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  pledged that he would distribute 100m coronavirus vaccine doses over his first 100 days in office.\par \par \uc2 Today, the president celebrated the distribution of 50m shots since he took office last month. \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m here to report we\u8217\'20\'19re halfway there: 50m shots in just 37 days,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said.\par \par \uc2 enltrPresident Biden: "One of my first goals in office...was to get 100 million COVID vaccine shots in people's arms in my first 100 days as president...today, I'm here to report we're half way there. 50 million shots in just 37 days."\par \par \uc2 Full video here: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/KetmVKd0lJ"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/KetmVKd0lJ}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/r9NMhqKaUj"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/r9NMhqKaUj}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 CSPAN (@cspan) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/cspan/status/1365041450963066883?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 February 25, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 The Biden administration has been providing regular updates on its efforts to distribute coronavirus vaccines to states.\par \par \uc2 Jeff Zients, the coordinator of the White House coronavirus response team, said earlier this week that the administration distributed an average of 1.4m doses a day last week.\par \par \uc2 That number was slightly down from the 1.7m average doses a day distributed the week before, likely due to the winter storm that affected deliveries in the central US last week.\par \par \uc2 Regardless, the numbers make clear that the administration is outpacing its goal to distribute 100m shots by late April, which is fortunate given that some health experts have said the White House should set a more ambitious goal.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.25pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.40pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  acknowledged the question on everyone\u8217\'20\'19s mind right now is when the country can return to normal.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI can\u8217\'20\'19t give you a date,\u8221\'20\'1D the president said. \u8220\'20\'1CI can only promise we will work as hard as we can to make that day come as soon as possible.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrPresident Biden: "The question I'm asked most often is, 'When will things get back to normal?' My answer is always honest and straightforward \u8212\'20\'14 I can't give you a date. I can only promise that we'll work as hard as we can to make that day come as soon as possible." {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/Ne8YxNq0q7"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/Ne8YxNq0q7}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 CBS News (@CBSNews) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/CBSNews/status/1365038516720308228?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 February 25, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 Biden previously said that he believed the country would be basically back to normal by Christmastime, but his advisers, such as the press secretary, \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2 , have generally avoided committing to a timeline.\par \par \uc2 The president\u8217\'20\'19s event to celebrate the distribution of 50m vaccine doses since he took office has now concluded. Biden did not respond to shouted questions from reporters as he left the event.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.26pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.35pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Biden says 'this is not the time to relax' as vaccinations ramp up\par \par \uc2 As vaccinations ramp up, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  emphasized that Americans must continue to take every precaution to limit their risk of contracting coronavirus.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is not the time to relax,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said. \u8220\'20\'1CThe worst thing we can do now is let our guard down.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The president encouraged Americans to continue to regularly wash their hands and practice social distancing. Biden added, \u8220\'20\'1CFor God\u8217\'20\'19s sake, for God\u8217\'20\'19s sake, wear a mask.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.53pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.31pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Biden touts 'very promising' data on \uc2 Johnson & Johnson\uc2  vaccine\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  touted the \u8220\'20\'1Cvery promising\u8221\'20\'1D data on the \uc2 Johnson & Johnson\uc2  coronavirus vaccine that was released earlier this week.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Food and Drug Administration\uc2  may approve the vaccine for emergency use as soon as this weekend, and Biden pledged that the agency\u8217\'20\'19s decision would be made without any \u8220\'20\'1Cpolitical pressure from me or anyone else\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf the \uc2 FDA\uc2  approves the use of this new vaccine, we have a plan to roll it out as quickly as \uc2 Johnson & Johnson\uc2  can make it,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said.\par \par \uc2 Administration officials said earlier this week that 3 to 4 million doses of the \uc2 Johnson & Johnson\uc2  vaccine would be ready to distribute next week, assuming the \uc2 FDA\uc2  approves it. That is much less than the 12 million or so doses that the Biden administration initially expected from \uc2 Johnson & Johnson\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.26pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  celebrated the progress his administration has made on coronavirus vaccine distribution and urged Americans to get vaccinated as soon as they are able to.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe more people that get vaccinated, the faster we\u8217\'20\'19re going to beat this pandemic,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said.\par \par \uc2 The president applauded the work his officials have done, despite the Trump administration leaving them with \u8220\'20\'1Cno real plan to vaccinate all Americans\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re halfway there: 50 million shots in just 37 days since I became president,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said. \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re moving in the right direction despite the mess we inherited from the previous administration.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.18pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Biden celebrates distribution of 50m coronavirus vaccine doses\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is now holding an event to celebrate the distribution of 50m coronavirus vaccine doses since he took office last month.\par \par \uc2 Biden has set a goal of administering 100m doses over his first 100 days in office, but his administration has been outpacing that goal in recent weeks.\par \par \uc2 The event began with several people receiving the first dose of the \uc2 Pfizer\uc2  coronavirus vaccine.\par \par \uc2 enltrPresident Biden commemorates 50 millionth COVID-19 Vaccine Shot - LIVE on C-SPAN3 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/tafyvBo7y2"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/tafyvBo7y2}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/FrMC0FLfKw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/FrMC0FLfKw}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 CSPAN (@cspan) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/cspan/status/1365032696917934081?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 February 25, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.24pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.06pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Edward Helmore reports:\par \par \uc2 New York City\u8217\'20\'19s mayor, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/bill-de-blasio"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Bill de Blasio}}}\uc2 , has called for an independent investigation into the New York governor, \uc2 Andrew Cuomo\uc2 , a day after a former aide accused the governor of sexual harassment.\par \par \uc2 In {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://medium.com/@lindseyboylan4NY/my-story-of-working-with-governor-cuomo-e664d4814b4e"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  an essay}}}\uc2  published in Medium on Wednesday, former aide Lindsey Boylan described several problematic episodes with Cuomo, including an unsolicited kiss in his Manhattan office, an invitation to play strip poker on a government airplane, and an internal email from another aide indicating that the governor considered her a \u8220\'20\'1Cbetter looking sister\u8221\'20\'1D of a rumored former girlfriend.\par \par \uc2 enltrNYC Mayor \uc2 Bill de Blasio\uc2  calls for an \u8220\'20\'1Cindependent investigation\u8221\'20\'1D into \uc2 Gov. Andrew Cuomo\uc2  (D-NY) after sexual harassment allegations. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/UIaK3iKEnT"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/UIaK3iKEnT}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Recount (@therecount) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/therecount/status/1364969752943280133?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 February 25, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 The governor\u8217\'20\'19s press office responded to the \u8220\'20\'1Cstrip poker\u8221\'20\'1D element of Boylan\u8217\'20\'19s allegations on Wednesday with flight records. \u8220\'20\'1CMs Boylan\u8217\'20\'19s claims of inappropriate behavior are quite simply false,\u8221\'20\'1D a statement read.\par \par \uc2 In remarks on Thursday, \uc2 De Blasio\uc2 , who has a contentious relationship with the governor, issued a call for an investigation into Cuomo\u8217\'20\'19s behavior. \u8220\'20\'1CThese allegations are really disturbing \u8230\'20\'26 This kind of behavior, if it\u8217\'20\'19s true, is just unacceptable. We\u8217\'20\'19ve got to get the truth about this,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/feb/25/andrew-cuomo-lindsey-boylan-sexual-harassment-claims-bill-de-blasio"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 New York mayor calls for investigation after woman accuses Cuomo of sexual harassment}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.51pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Even senators are impatient to learn whether the Senate parliamentarian will rule that the $15 minimum wage proposal can stay in the coronavirus relief package.\par \par \uc2 On the Senate floor today, Democrat \uc2 Brian Schatz\uc2  was heard asking parliamentarian Elizabeth McDonough, \u8220\'20\'1CSo, how did you rule?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 McDonough replied, \u8220\'20\'1CWe haven\u8217\'20\'19t released anything.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrThe Senate waits for Parliamentarian Elizabeth MacDonough to weigh in on whether Democrats may increase the minimum wage to $15 per hour.\par \par \uc2 Sen. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/brianschatz?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @brianschatz}}}\uc2  (D-HI), on a hot mic, on the Senate floor today: \u8220\'20\'1CSo how did you ruuuuule?\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/1W87OwiIcF"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/1W87OwiIcF}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Recount (@therecount) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/therecount/status/1365022913129287680?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 February 25, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 McDonough\u8217\'20\'19s office is expected to soon release a ruling on whether the minimum wage provision meets the requirements for reconciliation. The announcement could come later today.\par \par \uc2 The House is scheduled to vote on the coronavirus relief package tomorrow. House Democratic leaders have said they will introduce a standalone minimum wage bill if the proposal is stripped out of the relief package.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.32pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Manhattan DA has Trump's tax records, office confirms\par \par \uc2 The office of New York\u8217\'20\'19s Manhattan district attorney, \uc2 Cyrus Vance\uc2 , has confirmed that the prosecutor is indeed in possession of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s relevant tax and financial records.\par \par \uc2 Reuters reports:\par \par \uc2 After a lengthy court battle, the Manhattan DA is in possession of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s tax returns and other financial records as part of a criminal investigation into the former president and his family-run \uc2 Trump Organization\uc2 , a spokesman for the office confirmed today.\par \par \uc2 The New York prosecutor\u8217\'20\'19s office obtained the voluminous records on Monday, the same day the \uc2 U.S. Supreme Court\uc2  rejected Trump\u8217\'20\'19s latest attempt to keep his longtime accounting firm, Mazars USA, from turning over the records.\par \par \uc2 Danny Frost, a spokesman for Manhattan District Attorney \uc2 Cyrus Vance\uc2 , confirmed the office\u8217\'20\'19s receipt of the documents, which came some 18 months after a subpoena was issued for them.\par \par \uc2 The records, which include eight years of tax returns, could boost the district attorney*s investigation into the \uc2 Trump Organization\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 A spokesman for Mazars USA did not immediately respond to a request for comment. On Monday, after the Supreme Court ruling, Trump issued a statement calling Vance\u8217\'20\'19s investigation part of \u8220\'20\'1Cthe greatest political Witch Hunt in the history of our country.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Vance\u8217\'20\'19s investigation initially focused on hush money paid by former Trump lawyer {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/michael-cohen"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Michael Cohen}}}\uc2  before the 2016 election to adult-film actor and producer {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/stormy-daniels"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Stormy Daniels}}}\uc2  and former Playboy model Karen McDougal, who have said they had affairs with Trump in the past.\par \par \uc2 Vance later suggested the probe had broadened and could focus on potential bank, tax and insurance fraud, as well as falsification of business records.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.17pm GMT\par \par \uc2 House Democrats yesterday reintroduced policing legislation, named after {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/george-floyd"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 George Floyd}}}\uc2  , the Black American man whose killing by police in Minneapolis last May sparked a tidal wave of new civil rights protests across the US and beyond.\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has expressed his support for the legislation and will sign if it gets through the Senate and arrives at his desk at the White House.\par \par \uc2 enltrI am pleased that the House will vote next week on the George Floyd Justice in Policing Act. I encourage the House to pass it. Following Senate consideration, I hope to be able to sign into law a landmark police reform bill.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 President Biden (@POTUS) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/POTUS/status/1364984502133657602?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 February 25, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 CNN further {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2021/02/24/politics/police-reform-george-floyd-house-democrats/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported}}}\uc2  that:\par \par \uc2 The bill - titled the George Floyd Justice in Policing Act of 2021 - has provisions to overhaul qualified immunity for law enforcement, prohibitions on racial profiling on the part of law enforcement and a ban on no-knock warrants in federal drug cases.\par \par \uc2 It would also ban chokeholds at the federal level and classify them as a civil rights violation and would establish a national registry of police misconduct maintained by the Department of Justice.\par \par \uc2 The House could vote on this proposal as soon as next week, congressional aides told CNN.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis legislation addresses police misconduct and excessive force, while creating greater transparency within law enforcement, and grants victims more direct avenues for redress.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWith this legislation, the federal government demonstrates its commitment to fully reexamining law enforcement practices and building better relationships between law enforcement and the communities they are sworn to protect and serve,\u8221\'20\'1D House Judiciary Committee Chairman \uc2 Jerry Nadler\uc2  said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhile the issue of policing can\u8217\'20\'19t be solved by Congress alone, the federal government has a responsibility to address this issue. I look forward to working with my colleagues, across the aisle and in both chambers, to ensure this bill becomes law.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Incidentally, the trial of former Minneapolis police officer Derek Chauvin, who kneeled on Floyd\u8217\'20\'19s neck for almost nine minutes while Floyd begged for his life, goes on trial for murder next month, beginning with jury selection on March 8.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.20pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.50pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Unclassified intelligence report on Khashoggi killing delayed - report\par \par \uc2 The release of the report by the US intelligence services into the killing of journalist Jamal Khashoggi in 2018 has been delayed until after \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  speaks with King Salman of Saudi Arabia, according to a new report.\par \par \uc2 enltr {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/BreakingNews?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #BreakingNews}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/CNN?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @CNN}}}\uc2  is reporting the release of the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/Khashoggi?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #Khashoggi}}}\uc2  report has been delayed until after {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/POTUS?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @POTUS}}}\uc2  speaks with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/SaudiArabia?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #SaudiArabia}}}\uc2  's King Salman - no word on when that will happen.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Cindy Saine (@cindysaine) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/cindysaine/status/1365009445474959370?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 February 25, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 The report had been expected as early as today. and the White House said in its press briefing moments ago that the US president\u8217\'20\'19s phone call with the king should take place \u8220\'20\'1C very soon.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 But there is no definitive word on when the two will speak or when the US report will be released or if it has indeed been delayed.\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s believed that the US intel report will {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/feb/24/jamal-khashoggi-murder-us-report-saudi-arabia-mbs-king-salman-complicit"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 single out}}}\uc2  Saudi Arabia\u8217\'20\'19s crown prince, \uc2 Mohammed bin Salman\uc2 , for approving Khashoggi\u8217\'20\'19s death.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more from \uc2 the Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Stephanie Kirchgaessner:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/feb/24/jamal-khashoggi-murder-us-report-saudi-arabia-mbs-king-salman-complicit"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Saudi heir complicit in Khashoggi murder, US assessment reportedly finds}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.01pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.30pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Today so far\par \par \uc2 The White House briefing has now concluded. Here\u8217\'20\'19s where the day stands so far:\par \par \uc2 * The Manhattan district attorney\u8217\'20\'19s office has obtained \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s financial records, according to CNN. The news comes three days after the supreme court rejected Trump\u8217\'20\'19s request to block Cy Vance \u8217\'20\'19s office from gaining access to the records, which include his tax returns.\par \par \uc2 * The Senate confirmed \uc2 Jennifer Granholm\uc2  as the next secretary of energy. Granholm, a former governor of Michigan, was confirmed in a vote of 64 to 35. She is expected to play a major role in \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s promises to expand renewable energy sources.\par \par \uc2 * The House held a hearing on the security failures that occurred during the Capitol insurrection. Members of a House appropriations subcommittee pressed the acting chief of the the \uc2 US Capitol Police\uc2 , Yogananda Pittman, and the acting House sergeant at arms, Timothy Blodgett, on the insufficient preparation for the attack, despite many warning signs that Trump supporters could turn violent.\par \par \uc2 The blog will have more coming up, so stay tuned.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.19pm GMT\par \par \uc2 White House press secretary \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2  was asked why so many migrant children are attempting to enter the United States right now.\par \par \uc2 A reporter noted that some of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s critics have said it\u8217\'20\'19s because his policies on managing the US-Mexican border are too lenient.\par \par \uc2 Psaki said it was actually because the conditions in some of the countries where these children are coming from are so poor that they feel they must flee.\par \par \uc2 The White House press secretary emphasized that the Biden administration would not support sending children back to their home countries without adequately reviewing their cases.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThat is not something that we\u8217\'20\'19re going to do in this administration, and that is not going to be our policy,\u8221\'20\'1D Psaki said.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.05pm GMT\par \par \uc2 White House press secretary \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2  was asked about the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/feb/24/andrew-cuomo-ex-aide-lindsey-boylan-sexual-harassment-claims"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 sexual misconduct allegations}}}\uc2  against New York Governor \uc2 Andrew Cuomo\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 A reporter asked Psaki whether \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  still believes Cuomo is the \u8220\'20\'1Cgold standard\u8221\'20\'1D for leadership amid the coronavirus pandemic, a comment that the president made in April of last year.\par \par \uc2 enltrPsaki does not say whether Pres. Biden still believes New York Gov. Andrew Cuomo was "the gold standard" for COVID leadership, which Biden said in April 2020: "He made some positive comments on Gov. Cuomo and his role in New York at the time, as he did about a range of governors" {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/S8ZEC4qcq2"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/S8ZEC4qcq2}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 CBS News (@CBSNews) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/CBSNews/status/1364998835957682178?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 February 25, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 Psaki said that Biden complimented a number of governors from both parties at the time because they stepped up when there was a \u8220\'20\'1Cvacuum of leadership at the federal level\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHe made some positive comments about Governor Cuomo and his role in New York at the time, as he did about a range of governors,\u8221\'20\'1D Psaki said.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.58pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Back at the White House briefing, \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2  addressed \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s announcement yesterday that he is nominating three people to the \uc2 US Postal Service\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s board of governors.\par \par \uc2 If the nominees are confirmed, the board would be able to fire Postmaster General \uc2 Louis DeJoy\uc2 , who has been criticized over recent delays in mail delivery.\par \par \uc2 Psaki seemed to signal that the White House expected DeJoy to be pushed out after the board vacancies are filled.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe Postal Service needs leadership that can and will do a better job,\u8221\'20\'1D Psaki said.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.55pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Granholm confirmed as energy secretary\par \par \uc2 The Senate has confirmed \uc2 Jennifer Granholm\uc2  as the next secretary of energy, in a vote of 64 to 35.\par \par \uc2 enltrConfirmed, 64-35: Executive Calendar #9, Jennifer Mulhern Granholm, of Michigan, to be Secretary of Energy {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ENERGY?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @ENERGY}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Senate Cloakroom (@SenateCloakroom) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SenateCloakroom/status/1364995357810302976?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 February 25, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 After an initial delay in the Senate, more of Biden\u8217\'20\'19s cabinet nominees are now being confirmed.\par \par \uc2 The confirmation of Granholm, the former governor of Michigan, comes on the heels of the confirmations of \uc2 Linda Thomas-Greenfield\uc2 , the US ambassador to the UN, and Tom Vilsack, the secretary of agriculture, earlier this week.\par \par \uc2 Asked about the delay in confirming his nominees, Biden said yesterday that he did not blame the Senate for the issue.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI blame it on the failure to have a transition that was rational,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.48pm GMT\par \par \uc2 White House press secretary \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2  would not provide a specific timeline for when \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  will speak to Saudi Arabia\u8217\'20\'19s King Salman.\par \par \uc2 Psaki simply said the call between the two leaders will \u8220\'20\'1Chappen very soon\u8221\'20\'1D. Biden was expected to speak to the Saudi king yesterday, but it does not appear that the call occurred yesterday.\par \par \uc2 This comes as the \uc2 US government\uc2  prepares to release its unclassified report on the murder of journalist Jamal Khashoggi, which has been blamed on the crown prince of Saudi Arabia.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.44pm GMT\par \par \uc2 A White House reporter read out some of the caustic tweets that have caused trouble for Neera Tanden \u8217\'20\'19s nomination to lead the Office of Management and Budget.\par \par \uc2 The reporter asked White House press secretary \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2  whether \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  believes those tweets live up to his pledge that his administration would be committed to treating people with respect.\par \par \uc2 Psaki replied by noting that Tanden has apologized for her past comments and has said she will live up to Biden\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Cexpectation for a high bar of civility\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.40pm GMT\par \par \uc2 White House press secretary \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2  is now holding her daily briefing with reporters.\par \par \uc2 Psaki opened the briefing by noting that \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  will participate in an event this evening to mark 50 million vaccine doses administered since he took office.\par \par \uc2 Biden pledged to distribute 100 million vaccine doses across his first 100 days in office, but his administration has been outpacing that goal in recent weeks.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.29pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Sam Levine reports:\par \par \uc2 As of 19 February, there were 253 bills pending across the United States that would restrict access to the ballot, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.brennancenter.org/our-work/research-reports/voting-laws-roundup-appendix-february-2021"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to the latest tally}}}\uc2  by the Brennan Center for Justice.\par \par \uc2 The volume of bills illustrates how aggressively some states have moved to restrict access to voting weeks after an election in which there was record turnout.\par \par \uc2 Just weeks ago, the Brennan Center tallied up that there were {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.brennancenter.org/our-work/research-reports/voting-laws-roundup-february-2021"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 165 restrictive bills}}}\uc2  across 33 states, a major jump from the 35 bills that were pending at the same time a year ago.\par \par \uc2 One of the states where there has been the most activity is Georgia, where the state legislature is considering a wave of proposals to limit absentee and in person early voting after those voting options helped carry \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and two Democratic senators to victory in the state.\par \par \uc2 The Brennan Center also found there were 704 bills pending to expand voter access.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.15pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Vice-President \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  visited a pharmacy in Washington this morning to highlight the Biden administration \u8217\'20\'19s efforts to distribute coronavirus vaccines directly to pharmacies.\par \par \uc2 The Giant pharmacy that Harris visited is one of more than 7,000 across the country where Americans can receive coronavirus vaccine doses.\par \par \uc2 enltrToday I visited a Giant pharmacy in Washington D.C., where local residents are getting vaccinated. It\u8217\'20\'19s one of more than 7,000 pharmacies administering millions of vaccines to Americans directly in their communities. We're making progress - when it's your turn, get vaccinated. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/PoSYcRvCYG"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/PoSYcRvCYG}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Vice President \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  (@VP) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/VP/status/1364978656603422723?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 February 25, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 During the pharmacy visit, Harris described some of the side effects that she experienced after receiving her second dose of the Moderna vaccine.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe first dose, I was fine. The second dose, I thought I was fine. Got up early in the morning, went to work, and then midday, I realized, \u8216\'20\'18Yeah, I might I might need to slow down a bit,\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D Harris said. \u8220\'20\'1CJust that one day, and then it was fine.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Health experts have said that some people may experience mild flu-like symptoms after the second vaccine dose, but that is a normal immune response and should not deter anyone from receiving a vaccine.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.00pm GMT\par \par \uc2 At the House hearing on the Capitol insurrection, Democratic congresswoman Rose DeLauro pressed the acting chief of the \uc2 US Capitol Police\uc2 , Yogananda Pittman, on how many USCP officers are under investigation for their actions on January 6.\par \par \uc2 Pittman told her, \u8220\'20\'1CRight now we have 35 officers that are under investigation, and we do have six police officers that have been suspended with their police powers being revoked, so those investigations are ongoing at this time.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrRep. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/rosadelauro?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @rosadelauro}}}\uc2  : "How many officers are under investigation?"\par \par \uc2 Acting U.S. Capitol Police Chief Yogananda Pittman: "Right now we have 35 officers that are under investigation and we do have six police officers that have been suspended with their police powers being revoked." {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/AWQbcoiJBv"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/AWQbcoiJBv}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 CSPAN (@cspan) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/cspan/status/1364977346252591115?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 February 25, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 The investigations come after footage circulated of law enforcement officers posing for photos with some of the insurrectionists on January 6.\par \par \uc2 Pittman said she expected the investigations to take between 60 and 90 days, and she committed to making the findings of the investigations public once they become available.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.35pm GMT\par \par \uc2 House speaker \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  briefly misidentified Republican Senator Ron Johnson as Don Johnson, as in the actor who starred in \u8220\'20\'1CMiami Vice\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 enltrHouse Speaker Pelosi accidentally calls Sen. Ron Johnson (R-WI) \u8220\'20\'1CDon Johnson\u8221\'20\'1D of Miami Vice.\par \par \uc2 Pelosi says Johnson \u8220\'20\'1Cseems to be taking the lead\u8221\'20\'1D on Republican response to January 6 insurrection. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/c7YDtdonDV"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/c7YDtdonDV}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Recount (@therecount) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/therecount/status/1364973489711689732?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 February 25, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 Pelosi said Johnson, who amplified a baseless conspiracy theory about the Capitol insurrection during a Senate hearing earlier this week, \u8220\'20\'1Cseems to be taking the lead\u8221\'20\'1D on the Republican response to the January 6 attack.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.24pm GMT\par \par \uc2 House speaker \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  voiced confidence that the Senate parliamentarian would allow the $15 minimum wage proposal to stay in the coronavirus relief bill.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe will pass a minimum wage bill,\u8221\'20\'1D Pelosi said. \u8220\'20\'1CWe must pass a minimum wage bill.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 House majority leader \uc2 Steny Hoyer\uc2  has said the chamber will vote on a standalone minimum wage bill if it is stripped out of the relief package, but it\u8217\'20\'19s unclear whether such a bill could make it through the Senate.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.19pm GMT\par \par \uc2 House speaker \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  said she was disappointed by Senate minority leader \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s remarks criticizing Democrats \u8217\'20\'19 proposal for a 9/11 commission-style panel to review the Capitol insurrection.\par \par \uc2 In a Senate floor speech yesterday, McConnell said the draft proposal for the commission was \u8220\'20\'1Cpartisan by design\u8221\'20\'1D because the panel would favor Democrats.\par \par \uc2 Pelosi said she was open to negotiating the exact party breakdown of the commission, and she emphasized the important thing was the scope of the panel\u8217\'20\'19s investigation.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThat\u8217\'20\'19s not the point though. That\u8217\'20\'19s easily negotiated,\u8221\'20\'1D Pelosi said. \u8220\'20\'1CThe point is the scope.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.09pm GMT\par \par \uc2 House speaker \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  is now holding her weekly press conference, a day before the chamber is expected to pass \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s $1.9 trillion coronavirus relief package.\par \par \uc2 The Democratic speaker noted that the Senate parliamentarian could issue a ruling at any moment on whether the $15 minimum wage meets the requirements to be included in the reconciliation bill.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf you hear before I do, let me know,\u8221\'20\'1D Pelosi told reporters, adding that Democrats have a \u8220\'20\'1Cvery, very strong argument\u8221\'20\'1D for including the provision.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.56pm GMT\par \par \uc2 House holds hearing on security failures on January 6\par \par \uc2 A House appropriations subcommittee is now holding a hearing on the security failures that occurred during the Capitol insurrection on January 6.\par \par \uc2 The acting chief of the the \uc2 US Capitol Police\uc2 , Yogananda Pittman, and the acting House sergeant at arms, Timothy Blodgett, are testifying at the hearing.\par \par \uc2 The predecessors of Pittman and Blodgett both resigned in the days after January 6, amid criticism of their handling of the Capitol attack. They testified at a joint Senate hearing earlier this week.\par \par \uc2 In her opening statement, Pittman described some of the failures among the USCP force during the insurrection.\par \par \uc2 For example, Pittman said, some officers were not sure when to use lethal force as the violent insurrectionists stormed the Capitol.\par \par \uc2 The insurrection resulted in five deaths, including one USCP officer.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.25pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Nina Lakhani reports:\par \par \uc2 Latino and Black Americans continue to be vaccinated against Covid at the lowest rate despite political promises to redress inequalities, new analysis reveals.\par \par \uc2 Only 4.6% of Latinos and 5.7% of Black Americans have so far received a vaccine dose, compared with 11.3% of white Americans and 10.5% of Asian Americans, according to analysis {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.apmresearchlab.org/covid/vaccines-by-race"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 by APM Research Lab}}}\uc2  shared exclusively with \uc2 the Guardian\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Pacific Islanders have the highest inoculation rate, according to the limited data available, with 16.3% (about one in six) already having received at least one dose. Maryland has vaccinated 43.4% of this population \u8211\'20\'13 the highest reported proportion of any community in any state.\par \par \uc2 The second-highest rate is among Indigenous Americans, with 12.8% (one in eight) already having received at least one jab.\par \par \uc2 Despite some progress, the available state health data clearly suggests that access to the Covid vaccines \u8211\'20\'13 just like testing and economic aid \u8211\'20\'13 is disproportionately low for Latino and Black Americans, the two largest minority communities in the US.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/feb/25/coronavirus-vaccination-us-latino-black-americans-race"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Latino and Black Americans still face lowest vaccination rates, data reveals}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.03pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The website for DC residents to book vaccine appointments crashed this morning, as the service was flooded with appointment requests.\par \par \uc2 As of today, city residents with certain pre-existing conditions are eligible to receive the vaccine, but it appears the website was not updated to reflect that.\par \par \uc2 From a local WAMU reporter:\par \par \uc2 enltrLoads of D.C. residents aged 16-64 with pre-existing medical conditions who were told they could register for COVID-19 vaccine appointments now are facing busy phone lines and a website that crashes and also wasn't updated to reflect the new categories of people who are eligible.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Martin Austermuhle (@maustermuhle) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/maustermuhle/status/1364943671708307462?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 February 25, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 As the DC vaccine website was crashing, Vice-President \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  was visiting a pharmacy in the city where residents can receive the vaccine.\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and Harris are also holding an event later today to mark 50 million vaccine doses being administered in the US.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.42pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Washington bureau chief, David Smith, wrote earlier this week that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s failure to keep his financial documents away from the Manhattan district attorney may be his most consequential loss yet:\par \par \uc2 The DA has said little about why he wants Trump\u8217\'20\'19s records but, in a court filing last year, prosecutors said they were justified in seeking them because of public reports of \u8216\'20\'18possibly extensive and protracted criminal conduct at the \uc2 Trump Organization\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19 \u8211\'20\'13 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s family business empire \u8211\'20\'13 thought to include bank, tax and insurance fraud.\par \par \uc2 Now that investigation is gathering momentum. Vance, who earlier this month hired a lawyer with extensive experience in white-collar and organised crime cases, will be able to find out whether the public reports were accurate by studying actual financial records, spreadsheets and email correspondence between the \uc2 Trump Organization\uc2  and accounting firm {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.mazars.us/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Mazars USA.}}}\par \par \uc2 If wrongdoing is established, it raises the spectre of Trump some day in the future standing in the dock in a New York courtroom and even facing a potential prison term. No wonder he fought so hard to cling to power and the immunity from prosecution that it conferred.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/feb/23/donald-trump-tax-returns-ruling-analysis"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ruling on Trump tax records could be costliest defeat of his losing streak}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.39pm GMT\par \par \uc2 CNN {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2021/02/25/politics/trump-taxes-mazars-vance/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has more details}}}\uc2  on the financial records that the Manhattan district attorney\u8217\'20\'19s office has received from \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s accounting firm:\par \par \uc2 Prosecutors obtained the records on Monday, according to a source, just hours after the \uc2 US Supreme Court\uc2  denied Trump\u8217\'20\'19s last-ditch effort to keep the records private.\par \par \uc2 The millions of pages of documents, sources say, contain Trump\u8217\'20\'19s tax returns spanning from January 2011 to August 2019, as well as financial statements, engagement agreements, documents relating to the preparation and review of tax returns, and work papers and communications related to the tax returns.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.36pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Manhattan DA receives millions of pages of Trump's financial records - report\par \par \uc2 The Manhattan district attorney\u8217\'20\'19s office has reportedly received \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s financial records as part of their investigation into his business dealings.\par \par \uc2 According to CNN, the records include millions of pages of documents.\par \par \uc2 enltrThe Manhattan District Attorney\u8217\'20\'19s office has obtained former President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s tax returns and related records, according to sources familiar with the matter.\par \par \uc2 The records include millions of pages of documents, the sources say.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Shimon Prokupecz (@ShimonPro) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ShimonPro/status/1364943494884786182?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 February 25, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 The report comes three days after the supreme court rejected Trump\u8217\'20\'19s request to block Cy V ance \u8217\'20\'19s office from obtaining the records.\par \par \uc2 The president has attempted for years to keep his financial records, particularly his tax returns, out of public view.\par \par \uc2 The financial records will be made available to a grand jury, so they will not be publicly released, but Trump launched a series of legal challenges to try to prevent Vance from gaining access to them.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/feb/23/donald-trump-tax-returns-ruling-analysis"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ruling on Trump tax records could be costliest defeat of his losing streak}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.30pm GMT\par \par \uc2 This is Joan Greve in Washington, taking over for Martin Belam.\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  will hold an event today to celebrate 50 million coronavirus vaccine doses being administered in the US.\par \par \uc2 This morning, the vice-president visited a pharmacy in Washington where city residents can receive vaccine shots.\par \par \uc2 enltr. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/VP?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @VP}}}\uc2  stops by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/GiantFood?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @GiantFood}}}\uc2  pharmacy in Southeast DC to highlight one of the pharmacies where local residents can get vaccinated.\par \par \uc2 Mask up and when it\u8217\'20\'19s your turn, get vaccinated. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/xRexjihkuZ"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/xRexjihkuZ}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Sabrina Singh (@SabrinaSingh46) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SabrinaSingh46/status/1364942371528593411?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 February 25, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 Biden initially pledged to distribute 100 million vaccine doses in his first 100 days in office, but his administration has been outpacing that goal in recent weeks.\par \par \uc2 The White House coronavirus response team said yesterday that an average of 1.4 million doses were administrated per day last week.\par \par \uc2 That was slightly down from 1.7 million average doses per day the week before, likely due to the winter storm that disrupted vaccine deliveries and distribution across the central US.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.53pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Rightwing group nearly forced Wisconsin to purge thousands of eligible voters\par \par \uc2 A {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://projects.jsonline.com/news/2017/5/5/hacked-records-show-bradley-foundation-taking-wisconsin-model-national.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 well-connected}}}\uc2  conservative group in Wisconsin nearly succeeded in forcing the state to kick nearly 17,000 eligible voters off its rolls ahead of the 2020 election, new state data reveals.\par \par \uc2 The group, the Wisconsin Institute for Law and \uc2 Liberty\uc2  (Will), caused a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2019/dec/18/wisconsin-rightwing-group-will-voter-purge"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 national uproar}}}\uc2  in late 2019 when it {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2019/dec/14/wisconsin-purge-voter-rolls-judge-ruling"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 successfully convinced a county judge}}}\uc2  to order the state to immediately remove more than 232,000 people Wisconsin suspected of moving homes from the state\u8217\'20\'19s voter rolls. The state, relying on government records, had sent a postcard to all of those voters asking them to confirm their address, and Will sought to remove anyone who had not responded within 30 days.\par \par \uc2 Democrats on the commission {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wpr.org/judge-holds-elections-commissioners-contempt-wisconsins-voter-purge-case"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 refused to comply}}}\uc2  with the order, believing that the underlying data wasn\u8217\'20\'19t reliable, and wanted to give voters until April 2021 to confirm their address before they removed them. Appeals courts intervened and blocked the removals; the case is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wpr.org/wisconsin-supreme-court-hears-arguments-voter-purge-mail-ballot-cases"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 currently pending}}}\uc2  before the Wisconsin supreme court. There were still more than 71,000 voters still on the list at the end of January who did not respond to the mailer (152,524 people on the list updated their registration at a new address).\par \par \uc2 But {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://elections.wi.gov/sites/elections.wi.gov/files/2021-01/February%203%2C%202021%20Commission%20Materials%20-Open%20Session%201.29.pdf#page=33"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 new data}}}\uc2  from the Wisconsin Elections Commission shows how disastrous such a purge could have been. And the dispute underscores the way fights over how states remove people from their voter rolls \u8211\'20\'13 often called purging \u8211\'20\'13 has become a critical part of protecting voting rights in America.\par \par \uc2 Across the country, Republicans and conservative groups have pushed for aggressive purging, saying it helps prevent fraud. Democrats and voting rights groups say the process can be done haphazardly, leaving eligible voters, particularly minority groups and students, at risk of being wrongly purged.\par \par \uc2 Read more here: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/feb/25/wisconsin-voter-purge-data-will-2020-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Rightwing group nearly forced Wisconsin to purge thousands of eligible voters}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.50pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Dr Fauci urges 'if a Covid vaccine is available, regardless of which one, take it'\par \par \uc2 Dr Anthony Fauci\uc2  has said this morning that if a coronavirus vaccine is available, regardless of which one it is, Americans should take it.\par \par \uc2 Associated Press report that the top infectious disease expert told NBC that a third vaccine becoming available \u8220\'20\'1Cis nothing but good news\u8221\'20\'1D and would help control of the pandemic.\par \par \uc2 Regulators announced {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/feb/24/johnson-and-johnson-covid-vaccine-fda-emergency-use"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 yesterday}}}\uc2  that \uc2 Johnson & Johnson\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s single-dose vaccine offers strong protection against severe Covid-19. It\u8217\'20\'19s expected to be approved soon by the \uc2 FDA\uc2 , probably as early as tomorrow.\par \par \uc2 Fauci warned people not to hold off on getting the \uc2 Johnson & Johnson\uc2  vaccine while waiting for the slightly more effective \uc2 Pfizer\uc2  or Moderna shots.\par \par \uc2 He says it\u8217\'20\'19s a race \u8220\'20\'1Cbetween the virus and getting vaccines into people\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Cthe longer one waits not getting vaccinated, the better chance the virus has to get a variant or a mutation.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Fauci says public health officials are always concerned about virus variants and stressed following public health measures of wearing masks and social distancing. The predominant coronavirus variant in the United States is from Britain. Fauci says the vaccines distributed in the US \u8220\'20\'1Cclearly can take care of that particular strain.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.47pm GMT\par \par \uc2 730,000 Americans filed initial jobless claims last week\par \par \uc2 Weekly initial jobless claims fell to 730,000 last week. It is a total that is much lower than at the peak of the coronavirus pandemic impact on the economy, but still way above pre-coronavirus figures, which used to average at around 200,000 per week. Ben Popkin {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/business/economy/latest-weekly-jobless-claims-fall-730-000-vs-845-000-n1258823?cid=sm_npd_ms_tw_ma"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 writes for NBC News}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 While the latest figure snaps the six-week streak of first-time claims above 800,000, it is still the 49th week that the number has been higher than at any time during the Great Recession.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CJobless claims are the one data series that has been trending in the wrong direction of late,\u8221\'20\'1D Brett Ryan, an economist for Deutsche Bank, wrote in a note.\par \par \uc2 The hardest-hit industries are those in the service sectors and those that depend on travel and face-to-face customer engagement, such as restaurants, hospitality, and leisure.\par \par \uc2 Continuing claims fell to 4.419 million, double their pre-pandemic levels, as more Americans burn through their six months of state unemployment benefits and turn to long-term federal unemployment benefits.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.40pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Black Lives Matter Global Network Foundation to launch $3m survival fund\par \par \uc2 The Black Lives Matter Global Network Foundation has launched a $3 million survival fund to provide financial support for marginalised communities.\par \par \uc2 It comes amid the wait for Congress to pass a new round of federal Covid relief funding worth $1.9 trillion. President Biden has pledged to pass an extensive programme of Covid relief in his first 100 days of office - with or without Republican support.\par \par \uc2 Announcing the fund {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://blacklivesmatter.com/survival-fund/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 on their website}}}\uc2 , Black Lives Matter (BLM) said it was part of a \u8220\'20\'1Clong legacy of groups stepping into support those failed by our government\u8230\'20\'26.In the words of the Black Panther Party, this is about \u8216\'20\'18Survival Pending Revolution\u8217\'20\'19.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In the 1960s and 70s, the phrase \u8216\'20\'18Survival Pending Revolution\u8217\'20\'19 was used as a slogan to describe an umbrella of over 60 community programmes run by the Black Panthers, including the Free Breakfast for Children Program which at its height fed over 10,000 children per day.\par \par \uc2 The foundation has said it plans to make up to 3,000 microgrants of $1,000 each available to \u8220\'20\'1Call Black people facing economic hardship\u8221\'20\'1D although there is \u8220\'20\'1Cspecial consideration for members of the trans community, single parents/guardians, and formerly incarcerated people.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The US has the world\u8217\'20\'19s highest incarceration rate with 716 prisoners per 100,000 members of the population. According to US Bureau of Justice statistics, the rate is 5.8 times higher for Black males (2,272 per 100,000) than for white men (392 per 100,000).\par \par \uc2 The foundation raised over $90 million in 2020 and ended the year with a balance of more than $60 million after spending nearly a quarter of its assets on grant funds and other charitable giving.\par \par \uc2 The BLM foundation has already begun asking recipients to apply for the Survival Fund as it plans to use its endowment to mitigate the economic impact of the pandemic on black communities.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.38pm GMT\par \par \uc2 And how will the Congressional Republican party react to that Trump CPAC speech at the weekend? There are some notable absentees from the CPAC agenda, including Senate minority leader \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Jordain Carney {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://thehill.com/homenews/senate/540428-senate-gop-works-to-avoid-having-22-war-with-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 writes for the Hill}}}\uc2  this morning that the Senate Republicans are keen to avoid \u8220\'20\'1Can intraparty bloodbath that would threaten their chances of taking back the majority in 2022.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Tensions within the party have been on full display since the ugly mob attack on the Capitol and the impeachment vote and Senate trial that divided Republicans and left Trump and McConnell trading charges in public.\par \par \uc2 Even on Wednesday, the tensions were evident when House minority leader Kevin McCarthy and \uc2 Rep Liz Cheney\uc2  disagreed over Trump\u8217\'20\'19s attendance at a conservative conference this weekend.\par \par \uc2 Sen John Thune\uc2 , the No. 2 Senate Republican, acknowledged the current signs of disunity but predicted competing factions of the party would unify. \u8220\'20\'1CI think there will be a lot more coordination than it might appear at the moment,\u8221\'20\'1D Thune said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe former president, the NRSC and Sen McConnell and his team, I think, will be realizing that for us to succeed we\u8217\'20\'19ve got to succeed as a team,\u8221\'20\'1D he added, referring to the National Republican Senatorial Committee.\par \par \uc2 Sen Kevin Cramer\uc2 , who aligned himself closely with the former president, said he wasn\u8217\'20\'19t convinced that Trump was ready to \u8220\'20\'1Cblow up\u8221\'20\'1D the party. \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s a pretty pragmatic guy.... I am just not that worried about it,\u8221\'20\'1D Cramer said, predicting that Trump would be \u8220\'20\'1Cteam builder and not a wrecking ball\u8221\'20\'1D within the party.\par \par \uc2 Read more here: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://thehill.com/homenews/senate/540428-senate-gop-works-to-avoid-having-22-war-with-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The Hill \u8211\'20\'13 Senate GOP works to avoid having \u8216\'20\'1822 war with Trump}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.34pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Kristen Holmes, national correspondent at CNN, has a couple of details about \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s CPAC speech at the weekend. She says that it is as yet unfinished, raising the spectre for organisers \u8211\'20\'13 and the rest of the Republican Party \u8211\'20\'13 that he could go in several different directions with it. She says though, per sources, \u8220\'20\'1Cexpect more railing against the election.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrBut ultimately, those around him know the speech Trump gives Sunday depend on what speech Trump WANTS to give when he arrives at CPAC the day of, despite what might be on paper in front of him. Whatever tone Trump strikes, source says to expect more railing against the election.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Kristen Holmes (@KristenhCNN) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/KristenhCNN/status/1364931180215336963?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 February 25, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.25pm GMT\par \par \uc2 You will hear a lot about \u8220\'20\'1Ccancel culture\u8221\'20\'1D at CPAC over the next few days, and how it is a terrible thing, even as Republicans in Congress try to prevent Neera Tanden taking a role at the Office of Management and Budget at least partially over her past \uc2 Twitter\uc2  output. Dana Milbank {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/opinions/2021/02/24/what-terrible-things-did-neera-tanden-tweet-truth/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 writes forcefully}}}\uc2  at the Washington Post this morning on that hypocrisy:\par \par \uc2 Can you believe that Neera Tanden called \uc2 Hillary Clinton\uc2  the \u8220\'20\'1Canti-Christ\u8221\'20\'1D and the \u8220\'20\'1Creal enemy\u8221\'20\'1D? Oh, wait. It was \uc2 Ryan Zinke\uc2  who said those things. Fifty-one Republican senators (and several Democrats, including \uc2 Joe Manchin\uc2 ) confirmed him as secretary of the interior in 2017.\par \par \uc2 And how about the times Tanden allegedly called the \uc2 NAACP\uc2  a \u8220\'20\'1Cpinko organization\u8221\'20\'1D that \u8220\'20\'1Chates white people\u8221\'20\'1D and used racial epithets? My bad. That was Jeff Sessions. Again, 51 Republican senators (and one Democrat, Manchin) voted to confirm him as attorney general in 2017.\par \par \uc2 Surely Tanden went beyond the pale when she \u8220\'20\'1Cliked\u8221\'20\'1D a tweet calling then-Secretary of State \uc2 John F. Kerry\uc2  a \u8220\'20\'1Ctraitor\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1CVietnam\u8217\'20\'19s worst export,\u8221\'20\'1D and when she suggested Clinton supporters leave the country. Except \uc2 Mike Pompeo\uc2  was the one who did those things. He won confirmation as secretary of state in 2018 with the votes of 50 Republicans and six Democrats, including Manchin.\par \par \uc2 But, Milbank argues, it isn\u8217\'20\'19t the hypocrisy over the tweets that is the worst thing.\par \par \uc2 What really must sting about Tanden\u8217\'20\'19s tweets is not that they were mean, but that, for the most part, they were true. Then-President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  called former aide \uc2 Omarosa Manigault Newman\uc2  a \u8220\'20\'1Ccrazed, lying lowlife\u8221\'20\'1D and a \u8220\'20\'1Cdog,\u8221\'20\'1D Tanden\u8217\'20\'19s now-deleted tweet said: \u8220\'20\'1CTrump just called a black woman a dog and about 80% of the GOP don\u8217\'20\'19t think he\u8217\'20\'19s racist. The whole party needs to be defeated in November.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Read more here: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/opinions/2021/02/24/what-terrible-things-did-neera-tanden-tweet-truth/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 What terrible things did Neera Tanden tweet? The truth}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.17pm GMT\par \par \uc2 That vaccine roll-out is not without hitches, though, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/feb/24/california-coronavirus-vaccine-black-latino"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 as Vivian Ho reports for us}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 Access codes meant to give Californians of color priority access to Covid-19 vaccine slots have been getting passed around among other residents in the state, allowing some to cut the line and get appointments meant for underserved Black and Latino residents.\par \par \uc2 Misuse of these codes was reported at vaccine sites in Los Angeles and the Bay Area, said Brian Ferguson, spokesperson for the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/california"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 California}}}\uc2  office of emergency services, to \uc2 the Guardian\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The codes were one of the tools devised by California leaders to address inequities in vaccine distribution in the state. They were given out to leaders and nonprofits in the Black and Latino communities in LA and the Bay Area to administer to eligible individuals \u8211\'20\'13 those 65 years or older, frontline healthcare workers, longterm care residents, and essential workers in the agriculture, food, education, childcare and emergency services sectors. Individuals then could use the code to book a vaccination appointment on the state\u8217\'20\'19s vaccine scheduling website.\par \par \uc2 Instead, the codes ended up passed on by text message and email, oftentimes with misinformation. \u8220\'20\'1CMy daughter says that the Oakland Coliseum needs to fill up appointment slots in the next few days to prevent spoilage of excess vaccines!\u8221\'20\'1D read an email that Oakland resident Jhumpa Bhattacharya received from a friend on Monday. \u8220\'20\'1CIf you are interested in getting a vaccine before this Wednesday, the link and access code are pasted below. They\u8217\'20\'19ll schedule appointments for both shots at the same time.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The friend who forwarded Bhattacharya the email had gotten it from a mother at a preschool cooperative for families of color. That mother had received it from a woman who worked at a racial justice nonprofit. \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s not quite the same story about the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.latimes.com/california/story/2021-02-22/why-rich-spots-beverly-hills-get-more-covid-vaccines"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 white affluent people in LA}}}\uc2 ,\u8221\'20\'1D Bhattacharya said, referencing {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.latimes.com/california/story/2021-02-22/vaccine-access-codes-for-hard-hit-communities-of-color-circulate-widely-in-affluent-l-a"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a Los Angeles Times investigation}}}\uc2  about the codes getting passed around by the \u8220\'20\'1Cwealthier, work-from-home set in Los Angeles\u8221\'20\'1D. \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t think any of these people were ill-intentioned. Some of these people are essential workers and just aren\u8217\'20\'19t eligible yet. People just want to get vaccinated so they can live their lives.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Read more of Vivian Ho\u8217\'20\'19s report here: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/feb/24/california-coronavirus-vaccine-black-latino"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 California vaccine sites see misuse of codes meant to prioritize Black and Latino residents}}}\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/feb/24/california-coronavirus-vaccine-black-latino"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 California vaccine sites see misuse of codes meant to prioritize Black and Latino residents}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.15pm GMT\par \par \uc2 White House chief of staff Ronald Klain is in a buoyant mood over the latest vaccination numbers.\par \par \uc2 enltrSix weeks ago, 14% of people over 75 in the US had gotten one COVID vaccine shot.\par \par \uc2 Today, that number stands at nearly 60%.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Ronald Klain (@WHCOS) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/WHCOS/status/1364922853326540806?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 February 25, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.58pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 New York Times\uc2  reports this morning that nursing homes, for so long a dangerous place to be during the coronavirus pandemic, have seen a steep fall, in new cases and deaths, outpacing national declines as vaccinations begin to take effect. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2021/02/25/us/nursing-home-covid-vaccine.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The paper writes}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 The coronavirus has raced through some 31,000 long-term care facilities in the United States, killing more than 163,000 residents and employees and accounting for more than a third of all virus deaths since the late spring. But for the first time since the American outbreak began roughly a year ago the threat inside nursing homes may have finally reached a turning point.\par \par \uc2 From late December to early February, new cases among nursing home residents fell by more than 80 percent, nearly double the rate of improvement in the general population. The trendline for deaths was even more striking: Even as fatalities spiked over all this winter, deaths inside the facilities have fallen, decreasing by more than 65 percent.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m almost at a loss for words at how amazing it is and how exciting,\u8221\'20\'1D said Dr. David Gifford, the chief medical officer for the American Health Care Association, which represents thousands of long-term care facilities across the country.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf we are seeing a robust response with this vaccine with the elderly with a highly contagious disease,\u8221\'20\'1D he said, \u8220\'20\'1CI think that\u8217\'20\'19s a great sign for the rest of the population.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 New York Times\uc2  notes that about 4.5 million residents and employees in long-term care facilities have received at least one dose of a Covid vaccine now, and that new cases in American nursing homes are at their lowest point since May 2020.\par \par \uc2 Read more here: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2021/02/25/us/nursing-home-covid-vaccine.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 New York Times \u8211\'20\'13 Nursing homes, once hotspots, far outpace US in Covid declines}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.54pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Astra Taylor, author of Democracy May Not Exist, but We\u8217\'20\'19ll Miss It When It\u8217\'20\'19s Gone, and an organizer with the Debt Collective, writes for us today to say that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2021/feb/25/joe-biden-student-debt-american-students"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Joe Biden is already backtracking on his promises to provide student debt relief}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 At his recent town hall, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/joebiden"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Joe Biden}}}\uc2  made a series of convoluted and condescending comments about American student debt. His remarks cast doubt on his ability, or willingness, to confront this country\u8217\'20\'19s ballooning student loan crisis. Within hours, #cancelstudentdebt was trending on \uc2 Twitter\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Biden\u8217\'20\'19s rambling justification of the status quo was peppered with straw men, invocations of false scarcity and non-solutions. He pitted working-class Americans against each other, implying that people who attend private schools aren\u8217\'20\'19t worthy of relief, as though poor students don\u8217\'20\'19t also attend such schools. He said that money would be better spent on early childhood education instead of debt cancellation, as if educators aren\u8217\'20\'19t themselves drowning in student debt, and as if we can\u8217\'20\'19t address both concerns at once. He suggested relying on parents or selling a home at a profit to settle your debt, a luxury those without intergenerational wealth or property cannot afford. And he touted various programs, including Public Service Loan Forgiveness (PSLF), that have totally failed borrowers: over 95% of PSLF applicants have been denied.\par \par \uc2 In contrast to Biden\u8217\'20\'19s smug comments, Congresswoman \uc2 Ayanna Pressley{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://finance.yahoo.com/news/ayanna-pressley-student-loan-debt-default-experience-204802776.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 recently}}}\uc2  revealed that she defaulted on her student loans. Similarly, at a recent Debt Collective event, congressional hopeful Nina Turner {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/astradisastra/status/1363264134717014017"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  that she and her son owe a combined $100,000. Former Georgia gubernatorial candidate \uc2 Stacey Abrams\uc2  has, of course, proudly confessed to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://sports.yahoo.com/stacey-abrams-im-running-governor-200000-debt-191600455.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 being in debt}}}\uc2 , and Alexandria Ocasio-Cortez has said that becoming a congressperson {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnbc.com/2019/06/25/aoc-it-was-easier-to-get-elected-than-to-pay-off-my-student-loans.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 was easier}}}\uc2  than paying off her debt. Philadelphia councilmember Kendra Brooks (who is planning to introduce a city resolution calling on the Biden administration to cancel all student debt) has also {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/now/video/will-president-biden-cancel-student-loan-debt-99821125638"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 spoken out}}}\uc2  about her own struggles as a borrower. Their experience and candor \u8211\'20\'13 and commitment to real solutions including cancellation \u8211\'20\'13 demonstrate why we need debtors, not millionaires, in our public offices.\par \par \uc2 Let\u8217\'20\'19s be clear about another thing. Biden absolutely has the legal authority to use executive power to cancel all federal student debt. Congress granted this authority decades ago as part of the Higher Education Act. It\u8217\'20\'19s even been put to the test: in response to the Covid pandemic, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and his former education secretary, \uc2 Betsy DeVos\uc2 , used that authority three times to suspend payments and student loan interest.\par \par \uc2 Read more here: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2021/feb/25/joe-biden-student-debt-american-students"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Astra Taylor \u8211\'20\'13 Biden is already backtracking on his promises to provide student debt relief}}}\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2021/feb/25/joe-biden-student-debt-american-students"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Biden is already backtracking on his promises to provide student debt relief | Astra Taylor}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.18pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The coronavirus pandemic has been having an effect on the way that the Biden administration has been carrying out its foreign diplomacy. In stark contrast to the previous administration, which frequently eschewed Covid precautions in the White House, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  hosted his first foreign leader virtually this week, in the shape of a large-screen version of Canadian prime minister \uc2 Justin Trudeau\uc2 , leading to some highly unusual photographs of the two together.\par \par \uc2 US President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and Canada\u8217\'20\'19s Prime Minister \uc2 Justin Trudeau\uc2 , appearing via video conference call, give closing remarks at the end of their virtual bilateral meeting. Photograph: Jonathan Ernst/Reuters\par \par \uc2 Antony Blinken\uc2  has tweeted this morning that he is making his first visits this week as secretary of state to Canada and Mexico. That would be a lot of travel to fit into one day, but he\u8217\'20\'19ll also be doing it virtually.\par \par \uc2 enltrIt is a great privilege to make my first visits, virtually, to Canada and Mexico tomorrow. These visits underscore the importance of our relationships. Together we can make great progress to defeat the pandemic, increase regional security, and grow prosperity for our citizens.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Secretary \uc2 Antony Blinken\uc2  (@SecBlinken) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SecBlinken/status/1364909744197140485?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 February 25, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.45am GMT\par \par \uc2 The lineup at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/cpac"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 CPAC}}}\uc2  2021 \u8211\'20\'13 switched to Florida from Maryland because of coronavirus safety constraints \u8211\'20\'13 suggest that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s dominance of the Republican Party is entirely undiminished by his loss of the White House and Republican setbacks in Congress.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cpac.conservative.org/speakers/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Speakers include}}}\uc2  his allies such as \uc2 Mike Pompeo\uc2 , the former secretary of state; Ben Carson, the ex-housing secretary; \uc2 Sarah Sanders\uc2 , a former White House press secretary; \uc2 Kristi Noem\uc2 , the governor of South Dakota; Pete Hegseth, a Fox News host; Jon Voight, an ardently pro-Trump actor; and \uc2 Donald Trump Jr\uc2 , the 45th president\u8217\'20\'19s son.\par \par \uc2 There are also slots for Senate Republicans including Ted Cruz, \uc2 Josh Hawley\uc2 , \uc2 Cynthia Lummis\uc2  and \uc2 Rick Scott\uc2 , and House Republicans such as Kevin McCarthy, Mo Brooks, Madison Cawthorn, \uc2 Matt Gaetz\uc2  and Jim Jordan, all of whom {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2021/01/07/us/elections/electoral-college-biden-objectors.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 voted to challenge Joe Biden\u8217\'20\'19s victory}}}\uc2 . The \u8220\'20\'1Cbig lie\u8221\'20\'1D of a stolen election is expected to thrive at CPAC.\par \par \uc2 That is not least because the conference will culminate on Sunday with Trump himself. In his first post-presidential speech, he is expected to promise to back Maga candidates in next year\u8217\'20\'19s midterm elections, condemn Biden\u8217\'20\'19s reversal of his immigration policies and reserve particular venom for his foes within the Republican party.\par \par \uc2 Matt Schlapp\uc2 , chairman of the American Conservative Union, which hosts CPAC, told {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.reuters.com/article/us-usa-trump-cpac/trump-likely-to-dangle-possibility-of-a-2024-run-in-first-post-white-house-speech-activist-says-idUSKBN2AM2LR"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Reuters news agency}}}\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is going to stay in the game and will be involved in primaries and he\u8217\'20\'19s going to opine and he\u8217\'20\'19s going to give speeches, and for establishment Republicans it puts shivers down their spine. They\u8217\'20\'19re very concerned he\u8217\'20\'19s going to continue to have an impact. My advice to them is to get used to it.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Among the talking points will be a straw poll of attendees on their preferences for the Republican nomination in 2024. Given the section of the party that now rules CPAC, there is little doubt that Trump will emerge the winner.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://thebulwark.com/author/tim-miller/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Tim Miller}}}\uc2 , former political director of Republican Voters Against Trump, said: \u8220\'20\'1CHe\u8217\'20\'19s gonna speak right after the 2024 straw poll, which presumably will show him with a landslide victory, and so I think it\u8217\'20\'19s set up for him speak in a way that will signal that he sees himself as the leader of the party, as the frontrunner for 2024. He will attack those who have questioned him in that regard.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m sure he\u8217\'20\'19ll be received overwhelmingly positively by the crowd in those appeals. The Republicans are doing this to themselves. They had an opportunity to put a stake in his heart, they didn\u8217\'20\'19t take it and he\u8217\'20\'19s in charge of the party right now.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Read more of David Smith\u8217\'20\'19s report here: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/feb/25/donald-trump-cpac-republicans-allies"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18The base is solidly behind him\u8217\'20\'19: Trumpism expected to thrive at CPAC}}}\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/feb/25/donald-trump-cpac-republicans-allies"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18The base is solidly behind him\u8217\'20\'19: Trumpism expected to thrive at CPAC}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.30am GMT\par \par \uc2 Republican protests about some of the elements in the proposed economic package have cut no ice with \uc2 Rep Ilhan Omar\uc2 . She said of a tweet by \uc2 Sen Marsha Blackburn\uc2  outlining the costs of some of the items she was objecting to that \u8220\'20\'1CThey are not even trying anymore.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrThey are not even trying anymore. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/ZLKazrmK5Y"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/ZLKazrmK5Y}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Ilhan Omar (@IlhanMN) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/IlhanMN/status/1364784679417769991?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 February 25, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 Blackburn had highlighted Planned Parenthood among things that would be funded by money directed to healthcare services, and was also objecting to $335m out of $1.9 trillion dollars going to support museums and libraries which have been forced to close their doors during the pandemic.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.26am GMT\par \par \uc2 Democrats have been keen to paint their Covid relief proposals as having bipartisan support among the public. \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has said \u8220\'20\'1CThe vast majority of the American people \u8212\'20\'14 more than 70% of the American people, with all the polls you all conduct, including a majority of Republicans \u8212\'20\'14 want us to act, and act big and quickly and support the plan.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Not every poll suggests there is a majority of public support for the plans among Republicans, and one place there definitely isn\u8217\'20\'19t is Washington DC.\par \par \uc2 Alan Fram reports for the Associated Press this morning on the GOP pushback. By late Wednesday, not one Republican in either chamber had publicly said he or she would back the legislation. Republican leaders were honing attacks on the package as a job killer that does too little to reopen schools or businesses shuttered for the coronavirus pandemic and that was not only wasteful but also even unscrupulous.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI haven\u8217\'20\'19t seen a Republican yet that\u8217\'20\'19s found something in there that they agree with,\u8221\'20\'1D said House minority leader Kevin McCarthy. \u8220\'20\'1CI think all Republicans believe in three simple things: They want a bill that puts us back to work, back to school and back to health. This bill is too costly, too corrupt and too liberal.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The hardening opposition suggested that Biden\u8217\'20\'19s first major legislative initiative could encounter unanimous Republican opposition. That was a counterpoint to the new president\u8217\'20\'19s refrain during his campaign about bringing the country together and a replay of the Republican wall that new President \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2  encountered in 2009 and most of his administration.\par \par \uc2 Democrats showed no signs of backing down, citing the assistance the measure would spread to people, businesses and state and local governments. \u8220\'20\'1CIf congressional Republicans want to oppose all that, my response is: Good luck,\u8221\'20\'1D Senate majority leader Chuck Schumer said on the Senate floor.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.13am GMT\par \par \uc2 Erin McCormick reports for us that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/feb/25/us-healthcare-workers-died-covid-since-december-vaccine"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 at least one in eight health workers lost in the pandemic died after the vaccine became available}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 As healthcare workers in the US began lining up for their first coronavirus vaccines on 14 December, Esmeralda Campos-Loredo was already fighting for oxygen.\par \par \uc2 The 49-year-old nursing assistant and mother of two had started having breathing problems just days earlier. By the time the first of her co-workers were getting shots, she was shivering in a tent in the parking lot of a Los Angeles hospital, because no medical beds were available. When she gasped for air, she had to wait all day for relief because there was a critical shortage of oxygen tanks.\par \par \uc2 Campos-Laredo died of Covid-19 on 18 December, one of at least 400 health workers identified by the Guardian/KHN\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2020/aug/11/lost-on-the-frontline-covid-19-coronavirus-us-healthcare-workers-deaths-database"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Lost on the frontline}}}\uc2  investigation who have died since the vaccine became available in mid-December, narrowly missing the protection that might have saved their lives.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI told her to hang in there, because they are releasing the vaccine,\u8221\'20\'1D said her daughter Joana Campos. \u8220\'20\'1CBut it was just a little too late.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In California, which became the center of the national coronavirus surge following Thanksgiving, 40% of all healthcare worker deaths came after the vaccine was being distributed to medical staff.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://interactive.guim.co.uk/uploader/embed/2021/02/archive-zip/giv-3902CiEhk8Ha6I0C"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Bar chart of healthcare worker deaths in California}}}\par \par \uc2 An analysis of the Guardian/KHN\u8217\'20\'19s Lost on the Frontline database indicates that at least one in eight health workers lost in the pandemic died after the vaccine became available. Unlike California, many states do not require a thorough reporting of the deaths of nurses, doctors, first responders and other medical staff. The analysis did not include federally reported deaths where the name was not released and may be missing numerous recent deaths that have not yet been detected by the Guardian/KHN.\par \par \uc2 The vaccine is now widely available to healthcare workers around the country and since mid-January, Covid-19 cases have been trending downward in the US.\par \par \uc2 Read more of Erin McCormick\u8217\'20\'19s report here: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/feb/25/us-healthcare-workers-died-covid-since-december-vaccine"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 At least 400 US healthcare workers have died of Covid since December}}}\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/feb/25/us-healthcare-workers-died-covid-since-december-vaccine"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 At least 400 US healthcare workers have died of Covid since December}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.55am GMT\par \par \uc2 Number of people hospitalized with Covid in US falls below 55,000\par \par \uc2 There were 74,502 new cases of coronavirus recorded in the US yesterday. The total caseload, according to the numbers collected by the \uc2 Johns Hopkins University\uc2  stands at 28,309,566.\par \par \uc2 There were 3,230 deaths, with the total US death toll now at 505,529.\par \par \uc2 The data from the CDC indicates that over 20 million people in the US have now been fully vaccinated with two doses of a Covid vaccine. That\u8217\'20\'19s around 6% of the population.\par \par \uc2 The number of people hospitalised in the US fell below 55,000 for the first time since 5 November.\par \par \uc2 default\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.50am GMT\par \par \uc2 Yesterday \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  announced increased plans to distribute masks in the US to help combat the spread of Covid. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.whitehouse.gov/briefing-room/statements-releases/2021/02/24/fact-sheet-president-biden-announces-new-actions-to-deliver-masks-to-communities-hit-hard-by-the-pandemic/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 A White House statement said}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 The Administration will deliver more than 25 million masks to over 1,300 Community Health Centers across the country as well as 60,000 food pantries and soup kitchens, reaching some of the nation\u8217\'20\'19s most vulnerable populations.\par \par \uc2 Recipients will be encouraged to take an individually wrapped package of two masks for each person in their household. These masks will be no cost, high-quality, washable, and consistent with the mask guidance from the CDC. All of these masks will be made in America, and will not impact availability of masks for health care workers.\par \par \uc2 Biden also took action yesterday to formally {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.whitehouse.gov/briefing-room/presidential-actions/2021/02/24/notice-on-the-continuation-of-the-national-emergency-concerning-the-coronavirus-disease-2019-covid-19-pandemic/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 continue the national emergency}}}\uc2  initially declared over the coronavirus by his predecessor \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  on 1 March 2020.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.46am GMT\par \par \uc2 Overnight the Washington Post has reported that a coronavirus variant detected in California this winter rapidly became dominant in the state over five months and now makes up more than half of the infections in 44 counties. One of the risks to vaccination roll-out globally is that mutations in the coronavirus may evade the vaccine. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/health/california-covid-variant/2021/02/24/0fb75550-76a3-11eb-948d-19472e683521_story.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Joel Achenbach and Carolyn Johnson write}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 The United States has been ramping up scrutiny of the shape-shifting virus, and scientists have identified many genetically distinct variants, but there is continued uncertainty and debate over which of these mutations are significant and to what extent. The variant identified in California has emerged as potentially the first homegrown \u8220\'20\'1Cvariant of concern\u8221\'20\'1D in the United States, though it has not yet been designated that by the \uc2 Centers for Disease Control and Prevention\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The variant contains a mutation that scientists suspect is enhancing the virus\u8217\'20\'19s ability to bind to human receptor cells. If truly more transmissible, as the new study contends, the California variant joins a growing list of virus variants circulating in the United States.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CFundamentally, it doesn\u8217\'20\'19t change the direction we are going, which is we want to hold cases down to where we can get the pandemic under control. Simply having a more infectious variant circulating is not going to be the end of the world,\u8221\'20\'1D said \uc2 Charles Chiu\uc2 , a professor of laboratory medicine and infectious diseases at the University of California at San Francisco School of Medicine, and the senior scientist behind the new research.\par \par \uc2 Read more here: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/health/california-covid-variant/2021/02/24/0fb75550-76a3-11eb-948d-19472e683521_story.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Washington Post \u8211\'20\'13 New research shows California coronavirus variant is more transmissible}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.30am GMT\par \par \uc2 Welcome to our coverage of US politics for Thursday, on a day when the Biden administration will once again try and throw the spotlight onto their coronavirus response.\par \par \uc2 * President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and vice president \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  will participate in a White House event today celebrating the 50 millionth shot of a Covid vaccine in the US. He has promised to deliver 100 million shots by his first 100 days. The event is at 2.30pm EST (1930 GMT).\par \par \uc2 * There were 73,386 new coronavirus cases recorded yesterday in the US, with 3,148 further deaths.\par \par \uc2 * {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/feb/24/johnson-and-johnson-covid-vaccine-fda-emergency-use"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The FDA declared Johnson & Johnson\u8217\'20\'19s one-shot Covid vaccine to be safe and effective}}}\uc2 , paving the way for emergency use approval tomorrow.\par \par \uc2 * We are expecting the US at some point \u8211\'20\'13 possibly today \u8211\'20\'13 to declassify information about the killing of journalist Jamal Khashoggi. The release is expected to be preceded by a call between Biden and Saudi Arabia\u8217\'20\'19s King Salman. Yesterday press secretary \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2  said \u8220\'20\'1CThe president\u8217\'20\'19s intention, as is the intention of this government, is to recalibrate our engagement with Saudi Arabia.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 * A former member of embattled Governor Andrew Cuomo \u8217\'20\'19s administration who previously accused him of sexual harassment offered new details, saying {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/feb/24/andrew-cuomo-ex-aide-lindsey-boylan-sexual-harassment-claims"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 he once kissed her on the lips without consent}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 * A \uc2 US navy\uc2  veteran who was experiencing a mental health crisis died after a police officer called out to help him {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/feb/24/angelo-quinto-us-navy-veteran-mental-health-crisis-died-officer-knelt-neck"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 knelt on his neck for several minutes}}}\uc2 , asphyxiating him, lawyers for his family have said.\par \par \uc2 * The American Conservative Union annual CPAC event will feature \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s first major post-presidency speech on Sunday. The event gets underway tonight with a welcome reception \u8211\'20\'13 the speeches start in earnest on Friday.\par \par \uc2 * Also on Biden\u8217\'20\'19s agenda for today: lunch with \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , the president\u8217\'20\'19s daily briefing, and he\u8217\'20\'19ll take part in the \uc2 National Governors Association\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Winter Meeting. Psaki will give the White House press briefing at noon (1700 GMT).\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020210225eh2p001mg\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
