\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Bernie Sanders: US sick of subsidizing 'starvation wages' at \uc2 Walmart\uc2  and \uc2 McDonald's\b0\par\par\uc2 Dominic Rushe \par \uc2 583 \uc2 words\par \uc2 25 February 2021\par 21:40 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2021.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Lawmakers hear from low-wage workers as Congress debates first rise in the minimum wage in over a decade\par \par \uc2 US taxpayers should not be \u8220\'20\'1Cforced to subsidize some of the largest and most profitable corporations in America\u8221\'20\'1D, Bernie Sanders told a Senate hearing on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 As Congress debates the first rise in the minimum wage in over a decade, the Vermont senator said he had \u8220\'20\'1Ctalked to too many workers in this country who, with tears in their eyes, tell me the struggles they have to provide for their kids on starvation wages\u8221\'20\'1D even as the chief executives of companies including \uc2 McDonald\u8217\'20\'19s\uc2 , \uc2 Walmart\uc2  and others take home multi-million dollar pay packages.\par \par \uc2 Executives from \uc2 Walmart\uc2  and \uc2 McDonald\u8217\'20\'19s\uc2  were invited to the hearing, titled Should Taxpayers Subsidize Poverty Wages at Large Profitable Corporations?They declined to appear.\par \par \uc2 The senators heard from low-wage workers from \uc2 McDonald\u8217\'20\'19s\uc2  and \uc2 Walmart\uc2 . Terence Wise, a \uc2 McDonald\u8217\'20\'19s\uc2  employee from Kansas City, Missouri, said his low pay had led to his family becoming homeless.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMy family has been homeless despite two incomes. We\u8217\'20\'19ve endured freezing temperatures in our purple minivan. I\u8217\'20\'19d see my daughter\u8217\'20\'19s eyes wide open, tossing and turning, in the back seat. Try waking up in the morning and getting ready for work and school in a parking lot with your family of five,\u8221\'20\'1D said Wise.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThat\u8217\'20\'19s something a parent can never forget and a memory you can never take away from your children. You should never have multiple jobs in the United States and nowhere to sleep.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Sanders cited a government accountability office (GAO) report that found nearly half of workers who make less than $15 an hour rely on public assistance programs that cost taxpayers $107bn each year.\par \par \uc2 Walmart\uc2  spent $8.3bn on stock buybacks in 2017, the Walton family, the chain\u8217\'20\'19s founders, are worth over $200bn and have increased their wealth by $50bn since the start of the pandemic, said Sanders. And yet the company \u8220\'20\'1Ccannot afford to pay its workers at least $15 an hour\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf \uc2 Walmart\uc2  thinks they\u8217\'20\'19re going to avoid answering that question because they\u8217\'20\'19re not here today, they\u8217\'20\'19re deeply mistaken. The American people are sick and tired of subsidizing the wealthiest family in America,\u8221\'20\'1D said Sanders.\par \par \uc2 The hearing comes at a tense moment for minimum wage advocates. \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  campaigned on a pledge to increase the minimum wage to $15 an hour from its current level of $7.25. The proposal is part of his $1.9tn Covid stimulus package.\par \par \uc2 But that package faces stiff opposition from in the Senate with the Republican minority set to vote against it and some Democrats opposing the wage rise.\par \par \uc2 A recent {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cbo.gov/publication/56975"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Congressional Budget Office}}}\uc2  concluded 27 million Americans would be affected by an increase in the minimum wage to $15, and that 900,000 would be lifted out of poverty. But the CBO also said the increase would lead to 1.4m job losses and increase the federal budget deficit by $54bn over the next 10 years. The \uc2 Economic Policy Institute\uc2 , and others, have called the report {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.epi.org/blog/cbo-analysis-confirms-that-a-15-minimum-wage-raises-earnings-of-low-wage-workers-reduces-inequality-and-has-significant-and-direct-fiscal-effects-large-progressive-redistribution-of-income-caused/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1Cwrong, and inappropriately inflated\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Republican Senator Mike Bruin told the hearing that an increase would be unfair on states with a lower cost of living and would hurt small businesses.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe need to slow it down,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CThe main result is you are going to hurt Main Street,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020210225eh2p002pj\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
