\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Sanders confident of raising minimum wage as part of $1.9tn Covid package\b0\par\par\uc2 Martin Pengelly in New York \par \uc2 550 \uc2 words\par \uc2 20 February 2021\par 15:34 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2021.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Senate budget chair says reconciliation process will applyRepublicans have vowed to oppose raising wage to $15 an hour\par \par \uc2 Bernie Sanders said on Saturday he was confident Senate Democrats will be able to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/feb/13/fight-for-15-minimum-wage-workers-labor-rights"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 raise the US minimum wage to $15}}}\uc2 , a step firmly opposed by Republicans but a key part of the Biden administration\u8217\'20\'19s $1.9tn coronavirus relief package.\par \par \uc2 In a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ryanobles/status/1363131222482968578"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 statement}}}\uc2 , the Vermont independent who caucuses with Democrats and chairs the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.budget.senate.gov/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Senate budget committee}}}\uc2  said he was \u8220\'20\'1Cvery proud of the strong arguments our legal team is making to the parliamentarian that raising the minimum wage to $15 an hour is not \u8216\'20\'18incidental\u8217\'20\'19 to the federal budget and is permissible under the rules of reconciliation\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Reconciliation allows legislators to bypass the 60-vote majority needed for most Senate legislation, for items linked to spending and taxation. When Donald Trump held the White House, Republicans used it to force through tax cuts. Under \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2 , Democrats used it to help pass the Affordable Care Act.\par \par \uc2 Sanders is championing moves to more than double the federal minimum wage from $7.25 an hour, its level since 2009, over a five-year period. The move is a key part of the Biden coronavirus relief package, meant to tackle the devastating impact of a pandemic in which nearly 500,000 have died and unemployment has rocketed.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHalf of our workers are living paycheck to paycheck and millions of people are working for starvation wages,\u8221\'20\'1D Sanders wrote on \uc2 Twitter\uc2  on Friday. \u8220\'20\'1CWe need the minimum wage to be a living wage and that\u8217\'20\'19s why we\u8217\'20\'19re going to raise it to $15 an hour.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Public opinion is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.pewresearch.org/fact-tank/2019/07/30/two-thirds-of-americans-favor-raising-federal-minimum-wage-to-15-an-hour/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 heavily in favour of the rise}}}\uc2  but Republicans are ranged against it, arguing that it would damage small businesses. Sanders counters that the gradual rise over five years should allay such concerns.\par \par \uc2 The Vermont senator is an experienced operator. After a coordinated if symbolic Republican move against the wage rise earlier this month, one Sanders staffer {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.businessinsider.com/the-senate-rejects-raising-15-minimum-wage-during-pandemic-2021-2"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1CThis isn\u8217\'20\'19t Bernie\u8217\'20\'19s first rodeo \u8230\'20\'26 we can still try to pass minimum wage through the reconciliation bill.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In his statement on Saturday, Sanders referred to two Republican priorities under Trump which could not reach 60 votes but which were {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.adn.com/politics/2017/10/19/u-s-senate-passes-bill-that-offers-a-chance-to-open-arctic-national-wildlife-refuge-to-drilling/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pursued}}}\uc2  through {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.healthaffairs.org/do/10.1377/hblog20171220.323429/full/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reconciliation}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe [\uc2 Congressional Budget Office\uc2 ] has found that the $15 minimum wage has a much greater impact on the federal budget than opening up the Arctic national wildlife refuge to oil drilling and repealing the [ACA] individual mandate penalties,\u8221\'20\'1D he said, \u8220\'20\'1Ctwo provisions that the parliamentarian advised did not violate the Byrd rule when Republicans controlled the Senate.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The Byrd rule is named for Robert Byrd, a long-serving Democratic senator from West Virginia who died in 2010. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cbpp.org/research/federal-budget/introduction-to-budget-reconciliation"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 According}}}\uc2  to the non-partisan \uc2 Center on Budget and Policy Priorities\uc2 , or CBPP, it \u8220\'20\'1Callows senators to block provisions of reconciliation bills that are \u8216\'20\'18extraneous\u8217\'20\'19 to reconciliation\u8217\'20\'19s basic purpose of implementing budget changes\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The Senate parliamentarian, Elizabeth MacDonough, is the first woman to interpret and manage the rules of Senate procedure. She must decide if a minimum wage raise can be pursued through reconciliation.\par \par \uc2 On Saturday, Sanders said he was confident McDonough would do so next week.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020210220eh2k001p5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
