\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 US workers go on strike in 15 cities to demand $15-an-hour minimum wage\b0\par\par\uc2 Michael Sainato in Florida \par \uc2 803 \uc2 words\par \uc2 16 February 2021\par 22:00 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2021.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 The Biden administration is attempting to push through what would be the first increase since 2009 as part of a pandemic relief bill\par \par \uc2 Workers at fast-food restaurant chains in 15 cities around the US went on strike on Tuesday demanding a raise in their minimum wage to $15 an hour.\par \par \uc2 The workers at \uc2 McDonald\u8217\'20\'19s\uc2 , \uc2 Burger King\uc2  and \uc2 Wendy\u8217\'20\'19s\uc2 , joined by home care and nursing home workers, took action as the Biden administration is attempting to push through an increase in the federal minimum wage from $7.25, in what would be the first increase in since 2009.\par \par \uc2 Strikes occurred in Charleston, South Carolina; Chicago; Flint and Detroit, Michigan; Raleigh and Durham, North Carolina; Houston; Miami, Orlando, and Tampa, Florida; St. Louis; Oakland, Sacramento, and San Jose, California; and Milwaukee.\par \par \uc2 Since 2012, the Fight for $15 movement has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/feb/13/fight-for-15-minimum-wage-workers-labor-rights?CMP=share_btn_tw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 organized}}}\uc2  low-wage workers around the US to push for state and local minimum wage increases and to increase the federal minimum wage to $15 an hour\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe hear you out there applauding essential workers. We see the big show you make of thanking us. But to be honest, that hasn\u8217\'20\'19t translated into changes for my life. We were living on a razor\u8217\'20\'19s edge long before Covid-19 hit South Carolina. And we\u8217\'20\'19re living on it still,\u8221\'20\'1D said Taiwanna Milligan, a \uc2 McDonald\u8217\'20\'19s\uc2  worker in Charleston who makes $8.75 an hour after working at the restaurant chain for eight years, in a recent {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.newsweek.com/i-work-mcdonalds-risking-my-life-every-day-dont-thank-me-pass-15-minimum-wage-opinion-1566544?fbclid=IwAR1q02e7LNIfkmGH8VRt8aRYWMi3X-LhkUMJ6gwwNLsjgDoutlFU7dvtpEw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 op-ed }}}\uc2  demanding a $15-an-hour federal minimum wage increase.\par \par \uc2 Fast-food workers in Durham are on STRIKE for higher pay, safe workplaces, and respect on the job. We're also on Zoom with our allies from across the midsouth in the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/FightFor15?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #FightFor15}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/z69bwt9qMo"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/z69bwt9qMo}}}\uc2  \u8212\'20\'14 Fight For 15 (@fightfor15) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/fightfor15/status/1361729039061323776?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 February 16, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 Workers are conducting the strikes as a proposal to raise the federal minimum wage to $15 an hour by 2025 is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnbc.com/2021/02/11/pelosi-says-15-minimum-wage-will-be-in-house-bill-sent-to-senate-.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 included }}}\uc2  in the coronavirus relief package House Democrats plan to pass and send to the Senate over the next two weeks.\par \par \uc2 In the Senate, the legislation still faces {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://ktla.com/news/nationworld/biden-acknowledges-dim-prospect-of-15-minimum-wage-in-congress-raising-concerns-among-activists/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 potential hurdles}}}\uc2 , including the Democratic senators Joe Manchin of West Virginia and Kyrsten Sinema of Arizona who have opposed including the bill in pandemic relief, and the possibility of the Senate\u8217\'20\'19s parliamentarian ruling a minimum wage measure can\u8217\'20\'19t be included in the relief bill.\par \par \uc2 Ieishia Franceis has worked at Freddy\u8217\'20\'19s Frozen Custards in west Durham, North Carolina since July 2020 and makes $9.20 an hour. She was one of several workers who went on strike on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CA $15 minimum wage would free me up to do a lot of things. My main goal is to be able to save enough money to put a down payment on a house and have home ownership. It would allow me to begin that process. It would allow me to have money left from one paycheck to the next, to provide for my family better as far as food, and allow me to get transportation so I won\u8217\'20\'19t have to take the bus,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 In October 2020, Franceis and her co-workers {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.newsobserver.com/news/business/article246902867.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 went on strike}}}\uc2  after their requests for paid sick leave for Covid-19 quarantining and testing were initially denied. The Families First Coronavirus Response Act passed in March 2020 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.dol.gov/agencies/whd/pandemic/ffcra-employee-paid-leave"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 exempted}}}\uc2  employers with more than 500 employees from granting employees two weeks pay if they needed to quarantine or recover from Covid-19. Now Franceis and her co-workers are fighting for a $15 minimum wage, hazard pay while they continue working during the pandemic, health benefits and ultimately a union.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSometimes businesses get so caught up in doing business that they forget who runs their businesses. We\u8217\'20\'19re going to keep fighting and not going to stop until we get all the equality we\u8217\'20\'19re fighting for,\u8221\'20\'1D added Franceis. \u8220\'20\'1CCongress needs to put our money where their mouth is. During their campaigns, they said they were going to raise the minimum wage to $15 an hour. Live up to what you said. We shouldn\u8217\'20\'19t have to wait until next year or the next year. The bill is there. Just pass it and be done with it.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Based on a recent analysis by the \uc2 Brookings Institution\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.brookings.edu/blog/the-avenue/2021/02/05/essential-workers-deserve-minimum-wage-increase/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 47% of essential workers}}}\uc2  are in occupations where the median wage is currently less than $15 an hour. Gradually raising it to $15 an hour would increase pay for {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.epi.org/publication/why-america-needs-a-15-minimum-wage/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 32 million workers in the US}}}\uc2 , including 59% of workers with a total family income below the poverty line. With the federal minimum wage increase, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.epi.org/publication/why-america-needs-a-15-minimum-wage"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 31% of Black workers}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.epi.org/publication/why-america-needs-a-15-minimum-wage/#_note6"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 26% of Latino workers}}}\uc2  in the US would receive a raise.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020210216eh2g0038q\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
