\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 US fast food workers hold Black History Month strikes to demand $15 an hour\b0\par\par\uc2 Dominic Rushe \par \uc2 636 \uc2 words\par \uc2 12 February 2021\par 13:09 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2021.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Workers call for \uc2 McDonald\u8217\'20\'19s\uc2 , \uc2 Burger King\uc2  and \uc2 Wendy\u8217\'20\'19s\uc2  to increase pay as Congress prepares to debate federal minimum wage\par \par \uc2 Fast-food workers in 15 cities will hold a Black History Month strike on Tuesday to demand that the \uc2 McDonald\u8217\'20\'19s\uc2 , \uc2 Burger King\uc2  and \uc2 Wendy\u8217\'20\'19s\uc2  restaurant chains pay them $15 an hour.\par \par \uc2 The action comes as Congress prepares to debate a federal rise in the minimum wage to $15 from its current rate of $7.25, the first federal raise since 2009.\par \par \uc2 Workers in cities including Atlanta, Charleston, Chicago, Detroit, Houston and St Louis will be joined by home care and nursing home workers in support of a $15 minimum wage and the right to join a union.\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  pledged to increase the minimum wage during his election campaign but has recently suggested the increase may not make it into the $1.9tn coronavirus relief package he is trying to push through Congress. Biden has said the increase is central to his pledge to narrow racial economic inequality.\par \par \uc2 Progressive senators including Bernie Sanders, a longtime supporter of the union-backed Fight for $15 movement, which has campaigned for the rise, and others are working to ensure the federal raise remains in the package.\par \par \uc2 On Thursday \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2 , the House speaker, confirmed the wage rise will be part of the House bill but it faces a tougher fight in the Senate where Democrats have only a slight majority. Democrats hope to pass the bill through a process known as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/jan/31/biden-coronavirus-stimulus-package-republicans-lowball-offer"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1Cbudget reconciliation\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2  which would require only a simple majority in the Senate.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis Black History Month, we have a chance to make our own history by winning a living wage of at least $15 an hour and lifting millions of families out of poverty,\u8221\'20\'1D said Taiwanna Milligan, a \uc2 McDonald\u8217\'20\'19s\uc2  worker from Charleston, South Carolina.\par \par \uc2 Milligan added: \u8220\'20\'1CFor decades, \uc2 McDonald\u8217\'20\'19s\uc2  has made billions in profit off the backs of workers like me, paying us starvation wages. I\u8217\'20\'19m striking today because I need at least $15 an hour to survive and because I know the only way to make change is to stand up, speak out and demand it.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The eight-year Fight for $15 movement has made significant progress in recent years with states including California, Florida and New York voting to increase their minimum wages to $15 an hour.\par \par \uc2 While {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://poll.qu.edu/national/release-detail?ReleaseID=3688"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 polling shows}}}\uc2  the increase is favored by the majority of Americans, opposition remains from most Republican politicians, some Democrats and lobby groups.\par \par \uc2 A {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cbo.gov/publication/56975"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Congressional Budget Office report}}}\uc2  published this week calculated 27 million Americans would benefit from a raise and 900,000 people would be lifted out of poverty. But the report also cautioned the raise would cost 1.4m jobs and add significantly to the nation\u8217\'20\'19s debt. The findings have been disputed by other economists with the left leaning Economics Policy Institute calling them {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.epi.org/blog/cbo-analysis-confirms-that-a-15-minimum-wage-raises-earnings-of-low-wage-workers-reduces-inequality-and-has-significant-and-direct-fiscal-effects-large-progressive-redistribution-of-income-caused/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1Cwrong and inappropriately inflated\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Gloria Machuca, a 20-year \uc2 McDonald\u8217\'20\'19s\uc2  worker from Houston, Texas, said she was currently making $9.50 an hour. \u8220\'20\'1CIt is not nearly enough,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CFifteen dollars would mean I could spend more time with my children, not worry about going hungry, paying bills.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 She said passing the bill was even more important during the coronavirus pandemic. \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s been very worrying,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s very stressful thinking about how I can pay doctor\u8217\'20\'19s bills, having to work when I could get sick.\u8221\'20\'1D Missing just one day of work would be a \u8220\'20\'1Cmajor setback\u8221\'20\'1D for her financially she said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMy message to President Biden is it\u8217\'20\'19s very important to pass this, it would make a big difference not just for me but for all the others that are struggling.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020210212eh2c001s0\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
