\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Bernie Sanders in new push for $15 minimum wage under Biden: 'For me, it's morally imperative'\b0\par\par\uc2 Steven Greenhouse \par \uc2 1,294 \uc2 words\par \uc2 26 January 2021\par 19:27 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2021.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Leftwing senator tells Guardian the chances of raising the federal minimum are better than ever with new president in White House\par \par \uc2 Senator Bernie Sanders says the widespread suffering caused by the pandemic-induced economic crisis has made it \u8220\'20\'1Cmorally imperative\u8221\'20\'1D to increase the US\u8217\'20\'19s minimum wage to $15 an hour. And in an interview with the Guardian, Sanders and other lawmakers pushing for a higher minimum wage say the chances of enacting a $15 minimum are better than ever before now that President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has called for a $15 federal minimum as part of his emergency Covid legislative package.\par \par \uc2 Raising the minimum to $15 would more than double the current $7.25-an-hour federal minimum wage, but many Republicans oppose the move, saying it would hurt business.\par \par \uc2 In an interview, Sanders, who championed a $15 minimum wage as a presidential candidate in 2016 and 2020, voiced excitement about the prospects of raising the minimum wage, which hasn\u8217\'20\'19t increased since 2009, the longest stretch without an increase since Congress first enacted a minimum wage in 1938.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis country faces an enormous economic crisis that is aggravated by the pandemic,\u8221\'20\'1D Sanders said. \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re looking at terrible levels of unemployment. We\u8217\'20\'19re looking at growing income and wealth inequality. What concerns me as much as anything is that half our people are living paycheck to paycheck. Millions of people are trying to survive on starvation wages. For me, it\u8217\'20\'19s morally imperative that we raise the minimum wage to a living wage that\u8217\'20\'19s at least $15 an hour.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.reuters.com/article/us-usa-congress-minimum-wage/house-passes-bill-to-raise-federal-minimum-wage-to-15-an-hour-idUSKCN1UD2DV"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The House voted last July to raise the minimum}}}\uc2  wage to $15 in steps through 2025, but then Senate majority leader \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2  blocked a vote on it. With the White House, Senate and House under Democratic control, Sanders said the chances are good to enact a $15 minimum, although he said it would be hard to attract 10 Republican Senators to support it, making it hard to overcome a filibuster.\par \par \uc2 Sanders, the incoming chairman of the Senate Budget Committee, sees another route to passage, saying it could be done under the \u8220\'20\'1Cbudget reconciliation\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 a process where measures deemed to have budgetary impact can be approved by simple majority vote.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt clearly has to be done by reconciliation. That\u8217\'20\'19s something I\u8217\'20\'19m working very hard on,\u8221\'20\'1D said Sanders.\par \par \uc2 Mary Kay Henry\uc2 , president of the Service Employees International Union (SEIU), which played a pivotal role in backing the Fight for $15, sees considerable momentum behind a $15 minimum.\par \par \uc2 That push has come a long way since the Fight for $15 began in 2012, when {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/30/nyregion/fast-food-workers-in-new-york-city-rally-for-higher-wages.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 200 fast-food workers in New York went on a one-day strike}}}\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CWe are incredibly proud that the momentum around $15 solidified as part of the presidential campaign, and that the Biden-Harris administration is so committed to get it done that they\u8217\'20\'19ve put it in the first action of Congress for Covid emergency relief,\u8221\'20\'1D Henry said. \u8220\'20\'1CThere is wind at our backs.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Henry noted that Raphael Warnock and \uc2 John Ossoff\uc2  campaigned for a $15 minimum in their successful Senate races in Georgia. Moreover, Florida voters, while backing \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , voted overwhelmingly \u8211\'20\'13 61% to 39% \u8211\'20\'13 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.huffpost.com/entry/florida-approves-minimum-wage-15_n_5f97122dc5b63fd49ceeef95"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 to raise that state\u8217\'20\'19s minimum to $15 }}}\uc2  by 2026.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CA $15 minimum is the single most concrete way to reduce racial inequality, put money in people\u8217\'20\'19s pockets and make material change in people\u8217\'20\'19s lives,\u8221\'20\'1D Henry said. The \uc2 Economic Policy Institute\uc2 , a progressive thinktank, found that raising {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.epi.org/publication/minimum-wage-15-by-2025/#:~:text=Fact%20Sheet-,Raising%20the%20federal%20minimum%20wage%20to%20%2415%20by%202025%20would,for%20over%2033%20million%20workers&text=On%20Thursday%2C%20July%2018%2C%20the,per%20hour%20by%20October%202025."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the minimum to $15 would help 25% of Black workers,}}}\uc2  19.1% of Hispanic workers, 13.1% of White workers and 10.8% of Asian workers.\par \par \uc2 A Pew poll found that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.pewresearch.org/fact-tank/2019/07/30/two-thirds-of-americans-favor-raising-federal-minimum-wage-to-15-an-hour/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Americans favor increasing the minimum to $15, by 67% to 33}}}\uc2  %. Henry warned that \u8220\'20\'1Cany elected official in Congress who dares to stand against us on this is going to pay a big political price\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Rita Blalock, a McDonald\u8217\'20\'19s cook in Raleigh, North Carolina, prays for a $15 minimum. Blalock, who earns $10 an hour after nearly 10 years at \uc2 McDonald\u8217\'20\'19s\uc2 , said she often relies on food pantries and can\u8217\'20\'19t afford her $200 rent every two weeks at a rooming house. \u8220\'20\'1CFortunately, I can eat free at work,\u8221\'20\'1D said Blalock, whose work schedule has been cut to 20 hours many weeks.\par \par \uc2 Asked what a $15 minimum would mean, Blalock, 54, said: \u8220\'20\'1COh my God, I could afford rent. I could eat a little better. I could finally buy me some clothes.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Blalock has participated in many of the Fight for $15\u8217\'20\'19s one-day strikes. \u8220\'20\'1CI feel if it doesn\u8217\'20\'19t pass in [Biden\u8217\'20\'19s] first 100 days, it\u8217\'20\'19s going to be swept under the rug,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 A $15 minimum faces strong Republican opposition from senators including \uc2 Pat Toomey\uc2 , Republican of Pennsylvania, who has said that \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.toomey.senate.gov/newsroom/press-releases/toomey-statement-on-biden-economic-plan"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 if the federal government mandates a universal $15 minimum wage}}}\uc2 , many low-income Americans will lose their current jobs and find fewer job opportunities in the future.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Michael Saltsman, managing director of the Employment Policies Institute, a corporate-backed research group, also said it would be a bad time to enact a $15 minimum.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou\u8217\'20\'19ve got a lot of businesses hanging from a thread,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CA $15 minimum is an irresponsible proposal at any time, and it\u8217\'20\'19s particularly so right now.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Saltsman said the Senate should not vote on a $15 minimum via reconciliation, arguing that its budgetary effect would be minimal. With the Senate divided 50-50, he questioned whether Democrats could muster 50 votes for a $15 minimum, suggesting that centrist Democrats like Joe Manchin of West Virginia might balk at it.\par \par \uc2 Bill Dauster, a top aide to former Senate majority leader Harry Reid, wrote in a recent editorial that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.rollcall.com/2021/01/22/congress-should-use-the-budget-to-raise-the-minimum-wage/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 raising the minimum would have clear budgetary effects}}}\uc2  and could be voted on through reconciliation.\par \par \uc2 Many Republicans say the federal minimum should remain at $7.25, leaving any increases to individual states. Walmart chief Doug McMillon says that if there is a minimum wage increase, it {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bloomberg.com/news/articles/2021-01-19/walmart-ceo-says-wage-hike-should-consider-regional-economics"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 should take \u8220\'20\'1Cgeographic differences\u8221\'20\'1D into account}}}\uc2 , considering the differing costs of living in, say, California and Mississippi.\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cbo.gov/system/files/2019-07/CBO-55410-MinimumWage2019.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Congressional Budget Office forecast that 1.3 million workers}}}\uc2  would become jobless due to an increase to $15. That study also forecast that 27 million workers would receive pay increases thanks to a $15 minimum, and the number of people in poverty would decline by 1.3 million.\par \par \uc2 Arindrajit Dube, an economics professor at the University of Massachusetts, Amherst, said a review of economic studies shows that \u8220\'20\'1Cmore ambitious minimum wage policies have yet to produce any clear impact on jobs, even though it has certainly raised wages and reduced inequality\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COverall, the body of literature shows it has very little effect on low-wage jobs,\u8221\'20\'1D Dube said. \u8220\'20\'1CMy work shows it leads to a reduction in poverty and increased family earnings, and maybe 35\u162\'00\'A2 on the dollar goes back to the government through reduced public assistance.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Differing with Dube, economists {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://epionline.org/wp-content/uploads/2021/01/MW-US-literature-for-NBER-1-1.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 David Neumark and Peter Shirley, in a newly released review of minimum wage research, conclude that \u8220\'20\'1Cmost of the evidence indicates}}}\uc2  the opposite \u8211\'20\'13 that minimum wages reduce low-skilled employment,\u8221\'20\'1D with the strongest effects on teens, young adults and the less-educated.\par \par \uc2 Senator Sanders said it\u8217\'20\'19s outrageous that the purchasing power of the minimum wage has declined 30% since the late 1960s. \u8220\'20\'1CThe fact that President Biden moved aggressively on this is important to the workers who will benefit,\u8221\'20\'1D Sanders said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt signals to the entire country that workers cannot continue to live on starvation wages, and I hope that message gets out to employers all across the country.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020210126eh1q001p7\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
