\par\par \uc2 Opinion\par \b \uc2 As \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  moves to double the US minimum wage, Australia can't be complacent\b0\par\par\uc2 Van Badham \par \uc2 884 \uc2 words\par \uc2 24 January 2021\par 16:32 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2021.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 If the proposals pass, the US minimum will leapfrog Australia\u8217\'20\'19s, in real terms and purchasing power\par \par \uc2 When I was writing about minimum wages for the Guardian six years ago, the United States only guaranteed workers US$7.25 an hour as a minimum rate of pay, dropping to a shocking US$2.13 for workers in industries that expect customers to tip (some states have higher minimum wages).\par \par \uc2 It is now 2021, and yet those federal rates remain exactly the same.\par \par \uc2 They\u8217\'20\'19ve not moved since 2009. Meaningfully, America\u8217\'20\'19s minimum wages have been in decline since their relative purchasing power peaked in 1968. Meanwhile, America\u8217\'20\'19s cost of living has kept going up; the minimum wage is worth less now than it was half a century ago.\par \par \uc2 Now, new president \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/jan/14/joe-biden-coronavirus-stimulus-package"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 $1.9tn pandemic relief plan}}}\uc2  proposes a doubling of the US federal minimum wage to $15 an hour.\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s a position advocated both by economists who have studied comprehensive, positive effects of minimum wage increases across the world, as well as American unions of the \u8220\'20\'1CFight for 15\u8221\'20\'1D campaign who\u8217\'20\'19ve been organising minimum-wage workplaces demanding better for their members.\par \par \uc2 The logic of these arguments have been accepted across the ideological spectrum of leadership in Biden\u8217\'20\'19s Democratic party. The majority of Biden\u8217\'20\'19s rivals for the Democratic nomination \u8211\'20\'13 Bernie Sanders, Elizabeth Warren, \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , \uc2 Pete Buttigieg\uc2 , Amy Klobuchar, Cory Booker and even billionaire capitalist \uc2 Mike Bloomberg\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 are all {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/graphics/politics/policy-2020/economic-inequality/minimum-wage/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 on record}}}\uc2  supporting it and in very influential positions to advance it now.\par \par \uc2 In a 14 January speech, Biden {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://qz.com/1959766/why-joe-biden-plans-to-raise-the-federal-minimum-wage/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 made a simple and powerful case}}}\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CNo one working 40 hours a week should live below the poverty line,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CIf you work for less than $15 an hour and work 40 hours a week, you\u8217\'20\'19re living in poverty.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 And yet the forces opposed to minimum wage increases {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://au.finance.yahoo.com/news/tax-and-minimum-wage-bidens-big-battle-with-business-013301890.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 retain the intensity}}}\uc2  that first fought attempts at its introduction, as far back as the 1890s. America did not adopt the policy until {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.dol.gov/agencies/whd/minimum-wage/history/chart"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 1938}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 31 years after Australia\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Harvester_case"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Harvester Decision}}}\uc2  legislated an explicit right for a family of four \u8220\'20\'1Cto live in frugal comfort\u8221\'20\'1D within our wage standards.\par \par \uc2 Seven years of Liberal policy actively corroding standards has resulted in wage stagnation\par \par \uc2 As an Australian, it\u8217\'20\'19s easy to feel smug about our framework. The concept is so ingrained within our basic industrial contract we consume it almost mindlessly, in the manner our cousins might gobble a hotdog in the stands of a Sox game.\par \par \uc2 But in both cases, the appreciation of the taste depends on your level of distraction from the meat. While wage-earning Australians may tut-tut an American framework that presently allows {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bls.gov/opub/reports/working-poor/2018/home.htm"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 7 million people}}}\uc2  to both hold jobs and live in poverty, local agitation persists for the Americanisation of our own established standards.\par \par \uc2 When I wrote about minimum wages six years ago, it was in the context of Australia\u8217\'20\'19s Liberal government attempting to erode and compromise them. That government is still in power and that activism from the Liberals and their spruikers is still present. The \uc2 Australian Chamber of Commerce and Industry\uc2  campaigned against minimum wage increases last year. So did the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.sbs.com.au/news/australia-s-minimum-wage-set-for-staggered-13-a-week-increase"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 federal government}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 using the economic downtown of coronavirus as a foil to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.smh.com.au/politics/federal/look-the-word-crisis-up-in-a-dictionary-businesses-attack-union-minimum-wage-rise-calls-20200515-p54tel.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 repeat American mythologies}}}\uc2  about higher wages causing unemployment increases.\par \par \uc2 They don\u8217\'20\'19t. The \u8220\'20\'1Csupply side\u8221\'20\'1D insistence is that labour is a transactable commodity, and therefore subject to a law of demand in which better-paid jobs equate to fewer employment opportunities \u8230\'20\'26 but a neoclassical economic model is not real life.\par \par \uc2 We know this because some American districts have independently increased their minimum wages over the past few years, and data from places like {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.marketwatch.com/story/the-15-minimum-wage-was-supposed-to-hurt-new-york-city-restaurants-but-both-revenue-and-employment-are-up-2019-10-28#"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 New York}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washington.edu/news/2019/02/06/two-new-studies-published-about-the-seattle-minimum-wage-ordinance/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Seattle}}}\uc2  has reaffirmed what\u8217\'20\'19s been observed in the UK and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cepr.net/documents/publications/min-wage-2013-02.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 internationally}}}\uc2 . There is no discernible impact on employment when minimum wage is increased. An impact on prices is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.upjohn.org/research-highlights/does-increasing-minimum-wage-lead-higher-prices#:~:text=Many%20business%20leaders%20fear%20that,may%20not%20be%20the%20case.&text=They%20also%20observe%20that%20small,and%20may%20actually%20reduce%20prices."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 also fleeting}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 As Biden presses his case, economists, sociologists and even health researchers have years of additional data to back him in. Repeated studies have found that increasing the minimum wage results in communities having {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://obamawhitehouse.archives.gov/sites/default/files/page/files/20160423_cea_incarceration_criminal_justice.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 less crime}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://equitablegrowth.org/minimum-wages-and-the-distribution-of-family-incomes-in-the-us/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 less poverty}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cbo.gov/publication/44995"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 less inequality}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://piie.com/blogs/realtime-economic-issues-watch/higher-wages-low-income-workers-lead-higher-productivity"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 more economic growth}}}\uc2 . One study suggested it helped {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.npr.org/sections/health-shots/2020/01/08/794568118/raising-the-minimum-wage-by-1-may-prevent-thousands-of-suicides-study-shows"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 bring down the suicide rate}}}\uc2 . Conversely, with greater wage suppression comes more smoking, drinking, eating of fatty foods and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bls.gov/opub/reports/working-poor/2018/home.htm"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 poorer health outcomes overall}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Only the threadbare counter-argument remains that improving the income of \u8220\'20\'1Cburger-flippers\u8221\'20\'1D somehow devalues the labour of qualified paramedics, teachers and ironworkers. This is both classist and weak. Removing impediments to collective bargaining and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.epi.org/publication/briefingpapers_bp143/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 unionisation}}}\uc2  is actually what enables workers \u8211\'20\'13 across all industries \u8211\'20\'13 to negotiate an appropriate pay level.\par \par \uc2 Australians have been living with the comparative benefits of these assumptions for decades, and have been {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.washingtonpost.com/blogs/wonkblog/wp/2013/08/19/the-u-s-has-a-7-25-minimum-wage-australias-is-16-88/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 spared the vicissitudes}}}\uc2  of America\u8217\'20\'19s boom-bust economic cycles in that time.\par \par \uc2 But after seven years of Liberal government policy actively corroding standards into ahistorical wage stagnation, if Biden\u8217\'20\'19s proposals pass, the American minimum wage will suddenly {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/CntrFutureWork/status/1352354918837805056?s=20"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 leapfrog Australia}}}\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/CntrFutureWork/status/1352354918837805056?s=20"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 s}}}\uc2 , in both real dollar terms and purchasing power.\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19ll be a sad day of realisation for Australia to see the Americans overtake us, while we try to comprehend just why we decided to get left behind.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020210124eh1o001xl\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
