\par\par \uc2 World news\par \b \uc2 Coronavirus live news: US nears 25m cases as three infections linked to Australian Open confirmed as UK strain\b0\par\par\uc2 Helen Sullivan \par \uc2 3,301 \uc2 words\par \uc2 24 January 2021\par 03:41 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2021.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 US nears 25m cases as one in 13 Americans have been infected ; no new local cases in NSW and Victoria ; three infections linked to Australian Open confirmed as UK strainVaccine experts defend UK decision to delay second Pfizer Covid jabThe new mutants: the Covid variants worrying health officials worldwideThree men arrested amid inquiry into \u163\'00\'A36m Covid loan fraudKenneth Branagh to play \uc2 Boris Johnson\uc2  in TV drama about Covid crisisSee all our coronavirus coverage\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.41am GMT\par \par \uc2 In the UK, ministers are at the centre of an explosive row over their failure to protect workers from Covid-19 as the Observer reveals the largest workplace outbreak of the virus has taken place at a top government organisation.\par \par \uc2 More than 500 cases have been recorded at the \uc2 Driver and Vehicle Licensing Agency\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s offices in Swansea, where employees claim people with symptoms were {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/jan/16/staff-pressured-back-to-work-breach-of-uk-covid-rules"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 encouraged to return to work}}}\uc2  while vulnerable workers have had requests to work from home turned down.\par \par \uc2 The revelation places the transport secretary, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/jan/15/grant-shapps-indicates-lorry-drivers-can-enter-france-with-rapid-covid-test"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Grant Shapps}}}\uc2 , under pressure to explain how such an outbreak could have happened in an agency where the strictest workplace rules are supposed to apply:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/jan/23/minister-faces-fury-over-mass-covid-outbreak-at-top-government-agency"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Grant Shapps faces fury over mass Covid outbreak at DVLA}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.25am GMT\par \par \uc2 Australia on track to receive vaccine from February, says treasurer\par \par \uc2 Treasurer \uc2 Josh Frydenberg\uc2  insists Australia is still on track to receive the Pfizer COVID-19 vaccine from February, as new figures suggest people are more than happy to get their jab, Australian Associated Press reports.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Therapeutic Goods Administration\uc2  is due to approve the \uc2 Pfizer\uc2  vaccine, and others Australia has signed up to, in the coming weeks.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe are not about to cut corners,\u8221\'20\'1D Mr Frydenberg told reporters in Melbourne on Sunday.\par \par \uc2 He said Australia is not in the same position as the US and UK where there are tens of thousands of cases each day with many lives lost.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe have the virus under control here in Australia,\u8221\'20\'1D the treasurer said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBut we do want to roll out the vaccine, that\u8217\'20\'19s why the TGA\u8217\'20\'19s is going through its normal processes and we are still on track to receive this \uc2 Pfizer\uc2  vaccine, mid to late February.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.11am GMT\par \par \uc2 Calls from adults worried about a child\u8217\'20\'19s welfare to the \uc2 NSPCC\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s helpline have jumped by 50% over the course of the pandemic, the charity has said.\par \par \uc2 PA Media: \uc2 NSPCC\uc2  said it was now receiving more than 30 calls a day from grown-ups worried that a child is living with domestic abuse, up 53% from pre-pandemic levels.\par \par \uc2 The charity warned the situation is likely to get worse as lockdown continues, and is calling for the \uc2 UK Government\uc2  to make extra provisions for child victims in its Domestic Abuse Bill.\par \par \uc2 The bill, hailed as a piece of landmark legislation, has had its second reading and is due to begin the committee stage on Monday.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 NSPCC\uc2  is calling for an amendment that would legally oblige all local authorities to fund community-based recovery services for child victims.\par \par \uc2 People who experience domestic abuse in childhood can experience difficulty learning, depression, eating disorders and addiction as they go through adolescence into adulthood.\par \par \uc2 The charity fears that without a statutory obligation, budgets for community-based support could be diverted to fund services such as refuges.\par \par \uc2 When the bill becomes law, councils will have to ensure all those who become homeless as a result of domestic abuse are prioritised for emergency housing.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 NSPCC\uc2  wants funding for community-based services - such as those that provide counselling to help child victims of domestic abuse to recover - also enshrined into law.\par \par \uc2 It is also calling for adequate funding for local agencies so they can meet all their obligations once the bill becomes law.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.48am GMT\par \par \uc2 PA Media reports that, according to a group of scientists, it could be necessary in the future to vaccinate domestic animals such as cats and dogs against Covid-19 to curb the spread of the virus.\par \par \uc2 Coronavirus can infect a wide range of species including cats, dogs, mink and other domesticated species, experts from the \uc2 University of East Anglia\uc2 , Norwich-based research facility the Earlham Institute and \uc2 University of Minnesota\uc2  have said.\par \par \uc2 In an editorial for the journal Virulence, they wrote that continued evolution of the virus in animals followed by transmission to humans \u8220\'20\'1Cposes a significant long-term risk to public health\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt is not unthinkable that vaccination of some domesticated animal species might... be necessary to curb the spread of the infection,\u8221\'20\'1D they said.\par \par \uc2 Last year, Denmark\u8217\'20\'19s government culled millions of mink after it emerged that hundreds of Covid-19 cases in the country were linked with coronavirus variants associated with farmed mink.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.27am GMT\par \par \uc2 Egypt to start Covid-19 vaccination campaign: Sisi\par \par \uc2 President \uc2 Abdel Fattah\uc2  al-Sisi announced Saturday that Egypt would start rolling out a mass Covid-19 vaccination campaign the following day with the Chinese-made Sinopharm jab, AFP reports.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe are starting a vaccination drive tomorrow beginning with healthcare workers followed by those suffering from chronic diseases and later the elderly,\u8221\'20\'1D Sisi said in brief comments after unveiling several development projects in Port Said.\par \par \uc2 Egypt, the Arab world\u8217\'20\'19s most populous country, received its first batch of the Sinopharm vaccines in December.\par \par \uc2 A man wearing a protective mask walks along the bank of the Nile river amid the coronavirus outbreak in Cairo, Egypt. Photograph: Mohamed Abd El Ghany/Reuters\par \par \uc2 Earlier this month, Health Minister \uc2 Hala Zayed\uc2  said Egypt would also receive 40 million doses, mostly of the \uc2 AstraZeneca\uc2 /Oxford jab, via the \uc2 Gavi vaccine alliance\uc2 , with the aim of inoculating 20 percent of its more than 100 million strong population.\par \par \uc2 Egypt has registered over 160,000 novel coronavirus infections, including more than 8,850 deaths.\par \par \uc2 Health officials have warned that low testing rates mean the real number could be at least 10 times higher.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.17am GMT\par \par \uc2 In December, the UK reported a Covid-19 variant of concern, commonly referred to as the B117 variant, which appeared to be more transmissible. Since then, scientists have established that B117 is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cmmid.github.io/topics/covid19/reports/uk-novel-variant/2020_12_23_Transmissibility_and_severity_of_VOC_202012_01_in_England.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 somewhere between 50% to 70% more transmissible}}}\uc2  than other variants. If more people are getting sick, there is more pressure on health systems, and in the UK health services are so overloaded a country-wide lockdown has been enforced.\par \par \uc2 While many scientists say B117 does not appear more deadly, researchers on the \uc2 UK government\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s New and Emerging Respiratory Virus Threats Advisory Group {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/nervtag-paper-on-covid-19-variant-of-concern-b117"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 found it may increase the death rate}}}\uc2  by 30% to 40%, though their sample size was small and they said more research is needed. With B117 now detected in more than 50 countries, understanding the variant is urgent.\par \par \uc2 But other variants of concern have also been identified, including in California, South Africa and Brazil.\par \par \uc2 So exactly what is a variant, and how many are there? And why are some variants of more concern than others?\par \par \uc2 Answers at the link below:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/science/2021/jan/24/the-new-mutants-what-we-know-about-the-covid-variants-worrying-health-officials-worldwide"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The new mutants: the Covid variants worrying health officials worldwide}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.56am GMT\par \par \uc2 And what a year it has been. In just over a month\u8217\'20\'19s time, I will have been liveblogging international developments in the coronavirus pandemic for eight hours a day, every day on the global blog \u8211\'20\'13 which has been running non-stop around the world almost uninterrupted for more than a year.\par \par \uc2 This time last year, I was living in Beirut, having just returned from reporting on the bushfires in Australia.\par \par \uc2 Where were you at the end of January 2020? Let me know on \uc2 Twitter{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/helenrsullivan"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @helenrsullivan}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.58am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.53am GMT\par \par \uc2 Monday marks one year since first cases in Australian state of New South Wales\par \par \uc2 In Australia, the state minister for health in New South Wales has noted that Monday will mark a year since the state confirmed its first four cases of coronavirus.\par \par \uc2 Today marks a week with no new local cases confirmed in the state:\par \par \uc2 enltrTomorrow is one very challenging year since NSW had first 4 Covid19 cases. But today, with incredible support of our community (testing)& stellar work of front line {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/NSWHealth?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @NSWHealth}}}\uc2  (inc??Tracers), {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/nswpolice?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @nswpolice}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/NSWHPathology?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @NSWHPathology}}}\uc2  it is one week since our last local transmission of Covid19.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Brad Hazzard\uc2  (@BradHazzard) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/BradHazzard/status/1353158021103243265?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 24, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.50am GMT\par \par \uc2 Summary\par \par \uc2 Here is a summary of the key developments from the last few hours:\par \par \uc2 * The US is nearing 25m cases. I\u8217\'20\'19ll post a summary shortly. For now, the US is nearing an astonishing 25 million cases of coronavirus \u8211\'20\'13 a quarter of the global total and one in every thirteen people in the country. There are currently 24,985,689 confirmed infections, according to the \uc2 Johns Hopkins University\uc2  tracker.\par \par \uc2 * UK to quarantine arrivals from high-risk countries \u8211\'20\'13 reports. Prime Minister \uc2 Boris Johnson\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s government is preparing to force travelers from countries where there is a high risk of Covid to go into quarantine for 10 days after arriving in Britain, the Daily Mail reported on Saturday.\par \par \uc2 * Three infections linked to Australian Open confirmed as UK strain. Coronavirus infections linked to the Australian Open are continuing to emerge, with a further three non-players - two men in their 30s and one in his 50s confirmed to have the highly contagious UK strain of the virus.\par \par \uc2 * Mainland China confirmed 80 new coronavirus cases on 23 January, down from 107 cases a day earlier, the country\u8217\'20\'19s national health authority said on Sunday. The National Health Commission, in a statement, said 65 of the new cases were local infections. The number of new asymptomatic cases, which China does not classify as confirmed cases, fell to 92 from 99 cases a day earlier. The total number of confirmed cases in Mainland China now stands at 88,991, while the death toll remained unchanged at 4,635.\par \par \uc2 * A possible community case of Covid is being reported in the northernmost New Zealand province of Northland. The \u8220\'20\'1Cprobable\u8221\'20\'1D case is in the community, a ministry of health spokesperson said, rather than a managed isolation facility. The director-general of health \uc2 Dr Ashley Bloomfield\uc2 , and the minister of covid-19 response, \uc2 Chris Hipkins\uc2 , will hold a media stand-up at 4pm to share the latest information.\par \par \uc2 * It has been a year since the Wuhan lockdown. The Chinese city of Wuhan marks one year since the start of its traumatic 76-day coronavirus lockdown. On 23 January 2020, Wuhan shocked the globe by confining its 11 million anxious citizens to their homes, starting a cycle that would spread across the world. But China largely brought its outbreak under control and Wuhan is nothing like the ghost town of a year ago, with traffic humming, sidewalks bustling, and citizens packing public transport and parks.\par \par \uc2 * Hong Kong and Oslo tightened measures. Thousands of people in one of Hong Kong\u8217\'20\'19s poorest and most densely packed districts have been ordered to stay in their homes. Norway\u8217\'20\'19s government, meanwhile, has imposed the strictest restrictions seen in the region of the capital, Oslo, since March after the discovery of the British variant in a retirement home.\par \par \uc2 * A French lockdown \u8216\'20\'18likely\u8217\'20\'19. A French government source has told AFP that \u8220\'20\'1Cthe hypothesis of confinement is more and more likely,\u8221\'20\'1D citing projections of a surge in cases due to the more transmissible British strain.\par \par \uc2 * Fabric masks still work, said the WHO. The \uc2 World Health Organization\uc2  says it has no plans to change its guidance recommending fabric face masks as new coronavirus variants spread because the mutated strains are transmitted in the same way. The statement comes after Germany and Austria made medical masks mandatory on public transport and in shops, allowing only surgical or FFP2 masks rather than fabric.\par \par \uc2 * There is a shortage of vaccines in Brazil. Brazil has just started its vaccination campaign but scientists are already warning the hard-hit country will quickly run out of doses and even syringes, some blaming the government for the shortages.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.38am GMT\par \par \uc2 Possible community case in New Zealand\par \par \uc2 An update on New Zealand now, where a possible community case of Covid is being reported in the northernmost province of Northland.\par \par \uc2 The \u8220\'20\'1Cprobable\u8221\'20\'1D case is in the community, a ministry of health spokesperson said, rather than a managed isolation facility.\par \par \uc2 The director-general of health \uc2 Dr Ashley Bloomfield\uc2 , and the minister of covid-19 response, \uc2 Chris Hipkins\uc2 , will hold a media stand-up at 4pm to share the latest information.\par \par \uc2 The last case of covid-19 in the community was recorded in Auckland on November 18 and contained within a matter of days after central Auckland was shut down.\par \par \uc2 Overall less than 2000 people contracted coronavirus in 2020, and 26 people died. New Zealand is pursuing an elimination strategy towards the disease.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.27am GMT\par \par \uc2 Mexico\u8217\'20\'19s Health Ministry on Saturday confirmed 20,057 new confirmed cases of coronavirus infection and 1,470 additional fatalities, bringing the country\u8217\'20\'19s total to 1,752,347 cases and 149,084 deaths, Reuters reports.\par \par \uc2 The government has said the real number of infected people is likely significantly higher than the confirmed cases.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.07am GMT\par \par \uc2 Mainland China reports 80 new cases vs 107 a day earlier\par \par \uc2 Mainland China confirmed 80 new coronavirus cases on 23 January, Reuters reports, down from 107 cases a day earlier, the country\u8217\'20\'19s national health authority said on Sunday.\par \par \uc2 The National Health Commission, in a statement, said 65 of the new cases were local infections. The number of new asymptomatic cases, which China does not classify as confirmed cases, fell to 92 from 99 cases a day earlier.\par \par \uc2 The total number of confirmed cases in Mainland China now stands at 88,991, while the death toll remained unchanged at 4,635.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.58am GMT\par \par \uc2 No new local cases in Australian state of Victoria\par \par \uc2 Victoria has recorded its 18th straight day without a local coronavirus case as the state\u8217\'20\'19s residents enjoy greater freedom to gather indoors, AAP reports.\par \par \uc2 The zero cases recorded on Saturday - as well as one case in Victoria\u8217\'20\'19s hotel quarantine system - came from just under 12,000 tests.\par \par \uc2 Only 30 active coronavirus cases remain in the state.\par \par \uc2 It comes as more visitors are allowed in Victorian households, with the indoor gathering limit at homes doubled from Saturday from 15 to 30.\par \par \uc2 The smaller limit on home gatherings had been introduced on New Year\u8217\'20\'19s Eve as the state battled a cluster linked to a Black Rock Thai restaurant.\par \par \uc2 More Victorians stranded interstate will also be able to return home, thanks to a further easing of interstate border restrictions.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.58am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.56am GMT\par \par \uc2 UK to quarantine arrivals from high-risk countries \u8211\'20\'13 reports\par \par \uc2 Prime Minister \uc2 Boris Johnson\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s government is preparing to force travelers from countries where there is a high risk of Covid to go into quarantine for 10 days after arriving in Britain, the Daily Mail reported on Saturday.\par \par \uc2 Via Reuters: Travellers from Brazil and South Africa, and neighbouring countries, will be met on arrival and escorted to hotels to quarantine, under plans being discussed by UK ministers, the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://dailym.ai/363vU7C"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Daily Mail}}}\uc2  said.\par \par \uc2 Johnson favoured a more targeted approach than making all air passengers go into quarantine, said the report, which added that the quarantine decision would be taken on Monday.\par \par \uc2 Britain has recorded more than 3.5 million Covid infections - the fifth-highest in the world - and nearly 96,000 deaths.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.54am GMT\par \par \uc2 Three infections linked to Australian Open confirmed as UK strain\par \par \uc2 Coronavirus infections linked to the Australian Open are continuing to emerge as the states and territories continue their run of no new locally acquired cases.\par \par \uc2 Victorian authorities on Saturday reported one new case linked to the Open, a man in his 20s who is not a player.\par \par \uc2 A further three non-players - two men in their 30s and one in his 50s - have meanwhile been confirmed to have the highly contagious UK strain of the virus.\par \par \uc2 Covid-19 Quarantine Victoria said all three had been in hard lockdown since they landed in Melbourne.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe residents arrived in Melbourne on a dedicated Australian Open charter flight on 15 January and returned their first positive tests on 15, 17 and 18 January,\u8221\'20\'1D a spokesperson said.\par \par \uc2 There are 10 active cases linked to the Open and 970 people associated with the tournament in quarantine.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.48am GMT\par \par \uc2 A possible outbreak of Covid-19 is being reported in New Zealand, in the northernmost province of Northland.\par \par \uc2 The probable case has emerged in the community, but is NOT a probable case of community transmission, according to the New Zealand Department of Health.\par \par \uc2 The outbreak - if confirmed - is said to be related to a person recently released from a managed isolation facility, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nzherald.co.nz/nz/covid-19-coronavirus-officials-responding-to-probable-community-case-in-northland/UKXYNUTBHCIKG4DZ2W5NQVSW3A/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  the New Zealand Herald reports.}}}\par \par \uc2 The director-general of health \uc2 Dr Ashley Bloomfield\uc2 , and the minister of covid-19 response, \uc2 Chris Hipkins\uc2 , will hold a media stand-up at 4pm to share the latest information.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.36am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.46am GMT\par \par \uc2 Australian state of New South Wales confirms zero local cases\par \par \uc2 New South Wales has recorded no new locally acquired cases of Covid-19 on Sunday and three in hotel quarantine. It brings the number of new cases listed in Australia today to four, all in hotel quarantine, after Victoria reported one new case in Melbourne\u8217\'20\'19s quarantine hotels. Queensland has recorded no new cases on Sunday.\par \par \uc2 Health officials in NSW have urged people to get a Covid-19 test if they have any cold or flu symptoms, however mild, after just 11,344 tests were conducted in the 24-hours to 8pm last night \u8211\'20\'13 well below the daily target of 30,000 tests.\par \par \uc2 Arriving passengers at Sydney\u8217\'20\'19s Kingsford Smith International airport are sent onto buses for mandatory 14 day quarantine on January 22, 2021 in Sydney, Australia. Photograph: James D Morgan/Getty Images\par \par \uc2 Authorities say they have also detected fragments of the virus in sewage tests at the Warriewood and North Head treatment plants,. The former covers about 70,000 people in the Northern Beaches area, and the latter has a catchment of 1.3 million people from a large chunk of Sydney extending north of the Parramatta River from Western Sydney to Manley.\par \par \uc2 NSW Health\uc2  said the detection \u8220\'20\'1Clikely reflects known recent confirmed cases in those areas,\u8221\'20\'1D but urged anyone living in those areas to get tested if they had any symptoms.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.43am GMT\par \par \uc2 Hello and welcome to today\u8217\'20\'19s live coverage of the coronavirus pandemic with me, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/helenrsullivan"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Helen Sullivan}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 I\u8217\'20\'19ll be bringing you the latest developments from around the world, with a focus on Australia, for the next few hours.\par \par \uc2 I\u8217\'20\'19ll post a summary shortly. For now, the US is nearing an astonishing 25 million cases of coronavirus \u8211\'20\'13 a quarter of the global total and one in every thirteen people in the country. There are currently 24,981,398 confirmed infections, with\par \par \uc2 In Australia, meanwhile, the states of New South Wales and Victoria have recorded zero local cases. We\u8217\'20\'19re awaiting the numbers from Queensland.\par \par \uc2 And three infections in hotel quarantine linked to the Australian Open have been confirmed to be the UK strain of the virus.\par \par \uc2 As always, you can say Hi (or shout at me) on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/helenrsullivan"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Twitter @helenrsullivan.}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.43am GMT\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020210124eh1o0005l\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
